sages?beta=true,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;18:1775474758.8798442^15:timestamp_start;18:1775474758.8790267^8:trailers;0:~7:content;119837:{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-04-06.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Read and analyze the file at /workspace/evaluation/usage/export_flows.py in full detail. Also check if there are any existing tests in /workspace/evaluation/usage/ directory, and look for any related files or imports that would help understand the context. Report back:\n1. The full content of export_flows.py\n2. All functions and their logic, including edge cases visible in the code\n3. Any existing test files in that directory\n4. The imports used (especially mitmproxy-related ones) so we can mock them properly"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you analyze the file and explore the directory structure. Let me start by reading the main file and examining the directory contents."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H38afqgVS9jdNdKPciBdj2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/evaluation/usage/export_flows.py"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YUV3mLGzXLLdDDmgHrsKaJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"ls -la /workspace/evaluation/usage/"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LUeQm4bQG6zL3fZgeYaHrp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"find /workspace/evaluation/usage/ -type f -name \"*.py\" | head -20"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"File does not exist. Note: your current working directory is /workspace.","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H38afqgVS9jdNdKPci