:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;18:1775475428.4461625^15:timestamp_start;18:1775475428.4451258^8:trailers;0:~7:content;186991:{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-04-06.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"I need to design a comprehensive pytest test suite for `/workspace/export_flows.py` that achieves at least 80% code coverage. The test file will be placed at `/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py`.\n\nHere's the complete module structure (1430 lines) I need to cover:\n\n## Key Functions to Test\n\n### Pure functions (no I/O):\n- `count_whitespace_stats(text)` - counts newlines, runs of 2+ spaces, total chars\n- `get_canonical_model(model_id)` - matches model ID with optional date suffix against MODEL_PRICING keys via longest-prefix matching\n- `get_pricing(model_id)` - returns pricing dict for a model\n- `sanitize_path(path)` - converts URL path to safe directory name (strips query, replaces /, removes non-alphanumeric, limit 80 chars)\n- `_system_prompt_hash(body_json, agent_name)` - SHA256 hash of system prompt text using SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX\n- `_resolve_read_file_name(name, tool_input)` - read_file ‚Üí compressed/uncompressed based on mode param\n- `_format_tool_params(input_data)` - formats dict as param=value pairs\n- `_get_file_path(input_data)` - extracts file_path/path from dict, makes absolute if relative\n- `_aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source)` - aggregates by_source dicts in-place\n- `_round_by_source(agg)` - rounds dollar values to 6 decimal places\n- `_agent_color(name)` - deterministic MD5-based hex color\n- `attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)` - proportional token/cost attribution\n- `extract_read_file_whitespace(body)` - counts whitespace from read_file tool results in request body\n- `categorize_input_sources(body)` - counts input chars by tool, split by cache position (last user msg = cache_write, second-to-last = cache_write for tool_use)\n\n### Functions requiring file I/O mocking:\n- `parse_request_body(request_path)` - reads JSON file, returns None on error\n- `format_headers(headers)` - needs headers object with .fields attribute (list of (k,v) byte pairs)\n- `write_request(flow, directory)` - writes request_headers.txt and request.json\n- `write_response(flow, directory)` - writes response_raw.txt\n- `extract_stop_reason(response_raw)` - parses SSE format or non-streaming JSON\n- `categorize_output_sources(response_path)` - SSE state machine for output char counting\n- `parse_response_content(response_path)` - parses SSE or non-streaming response into content blocks\n- `export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path)` - writes human-readable response_parsed.txt\n- `extract_file_ops(body, response_path)` - extracts read/write file stats\n\n### Functions requiring directory walking:\n- `redact_flow_files(directory)` - mitmproxy FlowReader/FlowWriter with redaction\n- `export_flows(input_dir, output_dir)` - main flow export, needs mitmproxy mocks\n- `extract_usage(directory)` - walks dirs, extracts token usage\n- `extract_prompts(directory)` - extracts system prompt and user messages  \n- `export_parsed_responses(directory)` - walks, calls export_parsed_response\n- `calculate_costs(directory)` - computes dollar costs from usage.json + request.json\n- `extract_source_attribution(directory)` - computes source attribution\n- `summarize_usage(directory)` - aggregates into per-agent summary\n\n## Key mitmproxy mocks needed:\n```python\n# HTTPFlow mock structure:\nflow.request.method = \"POST\"\nflow.request.pretty_url = \"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\"\nflow.request.headers.fields = [(b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"), (b\"x-api-key\", b\"secret\")]\nflow.request.headers.get(b\"x-api-key\") -> \"secret\" or None\nflow.request.get_text(strict=False) -> str\nflow.request.timestamp_start = 1700000000.0\nflow.response.status_code = 200\nflow.response.reason = \"OK\"\nflow.response.headers.fields = [...]\nflow.response.get_text(strict=False) -> str\nflow.response.timestamp_end = 1700000001.0\n\n# FlowReader mock (context manager-less, uses .stream() generator):\nfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader  # mock with: reader.stream() returns iter(flows)\n# Used as: with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f: reader = FlowReader(f); for flow in reader.stream()\n\n# FlowWriter mock:\nwriter = FlowWriter(f)\nwriter.add(flow)\n```\n\n## Critical test scenarios:\n\n1. **Longest-prefix model matching**: `claude-opus-4-5-20250101` should match `claude-opus-4-5`, NOT `claude-opus-4`\n2. **extract_stop_reason**: \n   - SSE with `\"type\":\"message_delta\"` and stop_reason\n   - SSE with `\"type\": \"message_delta\"` (space variant)\n   - Non-streaming JSON fallback with `\"type\":\"message\"` \n   - No stop_reason found ‚Üí returns \"unknown\"\n3. **categorize_input_sources cache position logic**:\n   - Last user message ‚Üí cache_write\n   - Second-to-last message (assistant) ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use\n   - All others ‚Üí cache_read\n4. **export_flows step boundary logic**:\n   - For \"cc\" agent: step increments when system prompt hash changes (before writing)\n   - For non-\"cc\" agents: step increments when stop_reason == \"end_turn\" (after writing)\n   - Skips /count_token URLs\n   - Skips requests where first message content is \"quota\" and no system prompt\n5. **_system_prompt_hash**: uses SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX[\"cc\"]=2, [\"vix\"]=0; returns None if index out of bounds\n6. **attribute_tokens**: proportional distribution, handles zero division cases\n7. **extract_file_ops**: deduplication via tool_ids map, both read and write tools\n\n## Import Strategy\nSince the test is in `evaluation/usage/` but the module is at `/workspace/export_flows.py`, add to sys.path:\n```python\nimport sys, os\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..', '..'))\nimport export_flows\n```\n\n## Test Organization\nOrganize tests into classes by function group:\n- `TestCountWhitespaceStats`\n- `TestGetCanonicalModel`  \n- `TestGetPricing`\n- `TestSanitizePath`\n- `TestFormatHeaders`\n- `TestExtractStopReason`\n- `TestSystemPromptHash`\n- `TestResolveReadFileName`\n- `TestFormatToolParams`\n- `TestGetFilePath`\n- `TestParseRequestBody`\n- `TestWriteRequest` / `TestWriteResponse`\n- `TestExtractReadFileWhitespace`\n- `TestCategorizeInputSources`\n- `TestCategorizeOutputSources`\n- `TestParseResponseContent`\n- `TestExportParsedResponse`\n- `TestAttributeTokens`\n- `TestAggregateBySource`\n- `TestRoundBySource`\n- `TestAgentColor`\n- `TestRedactFlowFiles`\n- `TestExportFlows`\n- `TestExtractUsage`\n- `TestExtractPrompts`\n- `TestCalculateCosts`\n- `TestExtractFileOps`\n- `TestSummarizeUsage`\n\nPlease design a detailed test plan including:\n1. The exact test file structure\n2. Which pytest features to use (fixtures, tmp_path, monkeypatch, parametrize)\n3. How to mock mitmproxy (since it may not be installed, consider conditional imports)\n4. The most critical test cases for each function\n5. How to achieve 80%+ coverage without testing trivial main() scaffolding\n6. Any conftest.py needed\n\nIMPORTANT: The mitmproxy package may or may not be installed. Design the mocks so that if mitmproxy IS installed, we test actual integration; if not, we mock at import level. Actually, let's assume mitmproxy IS installed (it's imported at module top level, so the module would fail to import without it). Design tests that mock it at the module level using `unittest.mock.patch`.\n"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll explore the codebase thoroughly before designing the test plan."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D3Dj9aiYSnuG3eHjbGQJS9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YVxGYTtsLwbWyrcfd3DgNv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"ls /workspace/evaluation/usage/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"Directory does not exist\"","description":"Check if evaluation/usage directory exists"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3Dj9aiYSnuG3eHjbGQJS9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Export mitmproxy flow files into per-flow directories with request.json, request_headers.txt, and response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n3\t\n4\timport argparse\n5\timport glob\n6\timport hashlib\n7\timport json\n8\timport os\n9\timport re\n10\timport shutil\n11\tfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter\n12\tfrom mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\n13\tfrom mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n14\t\n15\tSYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX = {\n16\t    \"cc\": 2,\n17\t    \"vix\": 0,\n18\t}\n19\t\n20\tMODEL_PRICING = {\n21\t    \"claude-opus-4-6\":   {\"input\": 5e-6,    \"cache_write\": 6.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.50e-6,  \"output\": 25e-6},\n22\t    \"claude-opus-4-5\":   {\"input\": 5e-6,    \"cache_write\": 6.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.50e-6,  \"output\": 25e-6},\n23\t    \"claude-opus-4-1\":   {\"input\": 15e-6,   \"cache_write\": 18.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 1.50e-6,  \"output\": 75e-6},\n24\t    \"claude-opus-4\":     {\"input\": 15e-6,   \"cache_write\": 18.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 1.50e-6,  \"output\": 75e-6},\n25\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\": {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n26\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-5\": {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n27\t    \"claude-sonnet-4\":   {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n28\t    \"claude-haiku-4-5\":  {\"input\": 1e-6,    \"cache_write\": 1.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.10e-6,  \"output\": 5e-6},\n29\t    \"claude-haiku-3-5\":  {\"input\": 0.80e-6, \"cache_write\": 1e-6,     \"cache_read\": 0.08e-6,  \"output\": 4e-6},\n30\t}\n31\t\n32\t# Sort prefixes longest-first so \"claude-opus-4-5\" matches before \"claude-opus-4\"\n33\t_SORTED_PREFIXES = sorted(MODEL_PRICING.keys(), key=len, reverse=True)\n34\t\n35\t\n36\tdef count_whitespace_stats(text):\n37\t    \"\"\"Count line returns and unnecessary spaces in text.\n38\t\n39\t    Returns dict with:\n40\t      - line_returns_count: number of \\\\n characters\n41\t      - unnecessary_space_count: for each run of 2+ spaces, count len(run) - 1\n42\t      - total_chars: total character count of the text\n43\t    \"\"\"\n44\t    line_returns = text.count(\"\\n\")\n45\t    unnecessary_spaces = sum(len(m) - 1 for m in re.findall(r\" {2,}\", text))\n46\t    return {\n47\t        \"line_returns_count\": line_returns,\n48\t        \"unnecessary_space_count\": unnecessary_spaces,\n49\t        \"total_chars\": len(text),\n50\t    }\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef parse_request_body(request_path: str):\n54\t    \"\"\"Parse the JSON body from a request.json file. Returns the parsed dict or None.\"\"\"\n55\t    try:\n56\t        with open(request_path, \"r\") as f:\n57\t            return json.load(f)\n58\t    except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n59\t        return None\n60\t\n61\t\n62\tdef get_canonical_model(model_id: str):\n63\t    \"\"\"Return the canonical model name (without date suffix) or None if unknown.\"\"\"\n64\t    for prefix in _SORTED_PREFIXES:\n65\t        if model_id.startswith(prefix):\n66\t            return prefix\n67\t    return None\n68\t\n69\t\n70\tdef get_pricing(model_id: str):\n71\t    \"\"\"Match a model ID (possibly with date suffix) to pricing. Returns pricing dict or None.\"\"\"\n72\t    canonical = get_canonical_model(model_id)\n73\t    if canonical:\n74\t        return MODEL_PRICING[canonical]\n75\t    return None\n76\t\n77\t\n78\tdef sanitize_path(path: str) -> str:\n79\t    \"\"\"Turn a URL path into a safe directory name component.\"\"\"\n80\t    path = path.split(\"?\")[0]\n81\t    path = path.replace(\"/\", \"_\")\n82\t    path = path.strip(\"_\")\n83\t    path = re.sub(r\"[^a-zA-Z0-9_\\-]\", \"\", path)\n84\t    return path[:80]\n85\t\n86\t\n87\t_REDACTED_HEADERS = {b\"x-api-key\", b\"authorization\"}\n88\t\n89\t\n90\tdef format_headers(headers) -> str:\n91\t    lines = []\n92\t    for k, v in headers.fields:\n93\t        if k.lower() in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n94\t            lines.append(f\"{k}: [REDACTED]\")\n95\t        else:\n96\t            lines.append(f\"{k}: {v}\")\n97\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n98\t\n99\t\n100\tdef write_request(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YVxGYTtsLwbWyrcfd3DgNv","type":"tool_result","content":"Directory does not exist\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so m‚Ä¶\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo, defaults to 10m) - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep‚Ä¶\n- claude-api: Build apps with the Claude API or Anthropic SDK.\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`/`claude_agent_sdk`, or user asks to use Claude API, Anthropic SDKs, or Agent SDK.\nDO NOT TRIGGER when: code imports `openai`/other AI SDK, ge‚Ä¶\n</system-reminder>\n\n<system-reminder>\nPlan mode is active. The user indicated that they do not want you to execute yet -- you MUST NOT make any edits, run any non-readonly tools (including changing configs or making commits), or otherwise make any changes to the system. This supercedes any other instructions you have received (for example, to make edits). Instead, you should:\n\n## Plan File Info:\nNo plan file exists yet. You should create your plan at /root/.claude/plans/tingly-forging-canyon-agent-a91c3de368e3444ce.md using the Write tool if you need to.\nYou should build your plan incrementally by writing to or editing this file. NOTE that this is the only file you are allowed to edit - other than this you are only allowed to take READ-ONLY actions.\nAnswer the user's query comprehensively, using the AskUserQuestion tool if you need to ask the user clarifying questions. If you do use the AskUserQuestion, make sure to ask all clarifying questions you need to fully understand the user's intent before proceeding.\n</system-reminder>","is_error":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fd69byJerh1Y16VH4DNWAE","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","limit":200,"offset":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019roTBgnH9jrczvtQzTtEyb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"ls /workspace/evaluation/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"No evaluation dir\"","description":"Check evaluation directory structure"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fd69byJerh1Y16VH4DNWAE","type":"tool_result","content":"100\tdef write_request(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):\n101\t    req = flow.request\n102\t    # Write headers file (method+URL line, blank line, headers)\n103\t    header_lines = [\n104\t        f\"{req.method} {req.pretty_url}\",\n105\t        \"\",\n106\t        format_headers(req.headers),\n107\t    ]\n108\t    with open(os.path.join(directory, \"request_headers.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n109\t        f.write(\"\\n\".join(header_lines))\n110\t    # Write body as JSON (pretty-printed if valid JSON, raw fallback)\n111\t    body = req.get_text(strict=False)\n112\t    if body:\n113\t        try:\n114\t            parsed = json.loads(body)\n115\t            body_out = json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n116\t        except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n117\t            body_out = body\n118\t        with open(os.path.join(directory, \"request.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n119\t            f.write(body_out)\n120\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n121\t\n122\t\n123\t\n124\tdef write_response(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):\n125\t    resp = flow.response\n126\t    if resp is None:\n127\t        return\n128\t    lines = [\n129\t        f\"{resp.status_code} {resp.reason}\",\n130\t        \"\",\n131\t        format_headers(resp.headers),\n132\t    ]\n133\t    body = resp.get_text(strict=False)\n134\t    if body:\n135\t        lines += [\"\", body]\n136\t    with open(os.path.join(directory, \"response_raw.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n137\t        f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n138\t\n139\t\n140\tdef extract_stop_reason(response_raw: str) -> str:\n141\t    \"\"\"Extract stop_reason from SSE message_delta event or non-streaming JSON response.\"\"\"\n142\t    # Try SSE streaming format\n143\t    for line in response_raw.splitlines():\n144\t        line = line.strip()\n145\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n146\t            continue\n147\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n148\t        if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n149\t            continue\n150\t        try:\n151\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n152\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n153\t            reason = delta.get(\"stop_reason\")\n154\t            if reason:\n155\t                return reason\n156\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n157\t            continue\n158\t\n159\t    # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response\n160\t    for line in reversed(response_raw.splitlines()):\n161\t        line = line.strip()\n162\t        if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n163\t            continue\n164\t        try:\n165\t            data = json.loads(line)\n166\t            if data.get(\"type\") == \"message\":\n167\t                reason = data.get(\"stop_reason\")\n168\t                if reason:\n169\t                    return reason\n170\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n171\t            continue\n172\t\n173\t    return \"unknown\"\n174\t\n175\t\n176\tdef redact_flow_files(directory: str):\n177\t    \"\"\"Redact sensitive headers (API keys) from .flow files in-place.\"\"\"\n178\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, \"*.flow\")))\n179\t    if not flow_files:\n180\t        return\n181\t\n182\t    count = 0\n183\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n184\t        flows = []\n185\t        modified = False\n186\t        try:\n187\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n188\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n189\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n190\t                    if isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n191\t                        for header in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n192\t                            if flow.request.headers.get(header):\n193\t                                flow.request.headers[header] = \"[REDACTED]\"\n194\t                                modified = True\n195\t                    flows.append(flow)\n196\t        except (FlowReadException, Exception) as e:\n197\t            print(f\"  Skipping {os.path.basename(filepath)}: {e}\")\n198\t            continue\n199\t\n200\t        if modified:\n201\t            with open(filepath, \"wb\") as f:\n202\t                writer = FlowWriter(f)\n203\t                for flow in flows:\n204\t                    writer.add(flow)\n205\t            count += 1\n206\t\n207\t    print(f\"\\nRedacted API keys in {count} flow files\")\n208\t\n209\t\n210\tdef _system_prompt_hash(body_json, agent_name):\n211\t    \"\"\"Return a short hash of the relevant system prompt, or None.\"\"\"\n212\t    system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n213\t    if not system:\n214\t        return None\n215\t    index = SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX.get(agent_name, 0)\n216\t    if index >= len(system):\n217\t        return None\n218\t    text = system[index].get(\"text\", \"\")\n219\t    if not text:\n220\t        return None\n221\t    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]\n222\t\n223\t\n224\tdef export_flows(input_dir: str, output_dir: str):\n225\t    \"\"\"Export .flow files from input_dir into per-flow directories under output_dir.\n226\t\n227\t    Directory structure: {agent}/{step_index}/{request_index}/\n228\t    Steps are delimited by end_turn stop_reason in responses.\n229\t    \"\"\"\n230\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(input_dir, \"*.flow\")))\n231\t    if not flow_files:\n232\t        print(f\"No *.flow files found in {input_dir}\")\n233\t        return\n234\t\n235\t    total = 0\n236\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n237\t        filename = os.path.basename(filepath)\n238\t        name = os.path.splitext(filename)[0]\n239\t        file_dir = os.path.join(output_dir, name)\n240\t        if os.path.exists(file_dir):\n241\t            shutil.rmtree(file_dir)\n242\t        os.makedirs(file_dir)\n243\t        print(f\"Reading {filename}...\")\n244\t        try:\n245\t            step_index = 1\n246\t            request_index = 1\n247\t            prev_prompt_hash = None\n248\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n249\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n250\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n251\t                    if not isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n252\t                        continue\n253\t\n254\t                    url = flow.request.pretty_url\n255\t                    if \"/count_token\" in url:\n256\t                        continue\n257\t\n258\t                    # Parse body to check for quota requests\n259\t                    body_text = flow.request.get_text(strict=False)\n260\t                    body_json = None\n261\t                    if body_text:\n262\t                        try:\n263\t                            body_json = json.loads(body_text)\n264\t                            messages = body_json.get(\"messages\", [])\n265\t                            system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n266\t                            if messages and not system:\n267\t                                first_msg = messages[0]\n268\t                                content = first_msg.get(\"content\", \"\")\n269\t                                if isinstance(content, str) and content == \"quota\":\n270\t                                    continue\n271\t                        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n272\t                            pass\n273\t\n274\t                    # For cc: step boundary = system prompt change (checked before writing)\n275\t                    if name == \"cc\" and body_json is not None:\n276\t                        prompt_hash = _system_prompt_hash(body_json, name)\n277\t                        if prompt_hash is not None and prev_prompt_hash is not None and prompt_hash != prev_prompt_hash:\n278\t                            step_index += 1\n279\t                            request_index = 1\n280\t                        if prompt_hash is not None:\n281\t                            prev_prompt_hash = prompt_hash\n282\t\n283\t                    flow_dir = os.path.join(file_dir, str(step_index), str(request_index))\n284\t                    os.makedirs(flow_dir, exist_ok=True)\n285\t\n286\t                    write_request(flow, flow_dir)\n287\t                    write_response(flow, flow_dir)\n288\t                    # Write timing data inline\n289\t                    timing = {}\n290\t                    if flow.request:\n291\t                        timing[\"request_start\"] = flow.request.timestamp_start\n292\t                    if flow.response:\n293\t                        timing[\"response_end\"] = flow.response.timestamp_end\n294\t                    with open(os.path.join(flow_dir, \"timing.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n295\t                        json.dump(timing, f, indent=2)\n296\t                        f.write(\"\\n\")\n297\t\n298\t                    # Extract stop_reason to determine step boundaries\n299\t                    response_raw = \"\""},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019roTBgnH9jrczvtQzTtEyb","type":"tool_result","content":"No evaluation dir","is_error":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EhCMG1GLAtkDyjaWWFTb3A","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","limit":200,"offset":300}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EhCMG1GLAtkDyjaWWFTb3A","type":"tool_result","content":"300\t                    resp = flow.response\n301\t                    if resp is not None:\n302\t                        response_raw = resp.get_text(strict=False) or \"\"\n303\t                    stop_reason = extract_stop_reason(response_raw)\n304\t\n305\t                    print(f\"  [step {step_index}, req {request_index}] {flow.request.method} {flow.request.pretty_url} ({stop_reason})\")\n306\t\n307\t                    # For vix: step boundary = end_turn stop_reason (checked after writing)\n308\t                    if name != \"cc\":\n309\t                        if stop_reason == \"end_turn\":\n310\t                            step_index += 1\n311\t                            request_index = 1\n312\t                        else:\n313\t                            request_index += 1\n314\t                    else:\n315\t                        request_index += 1\n316\t\n317\t                    total += 1\n318\t        except FlowReadException as e:\n319\t            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n320\t        except Exception as e:\n321\t            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n322\t\n323\t    print(f\"\\nExported {total} flows to {output_dir}\")\n324\t\n325\t\n326\tdef extract_usage(directory: str):\n327\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, extract token usage from SSE message_delta events into usage.json.\"\"\"\n328\t    count = 0\n329\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n330\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n331\t            continue\n332\t\n333\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n334\t        usage = None\n335\t        with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n336\t            content = f.read()\n337\t\n338\t        # Try SSE streaming format: look for message_delta events\n339\t        for line in content.splitlines():\n340\t            line = line.strip()\n341\t            if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n342\t                continue\n343\t            payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n344\t            if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n345\t                continue\n346\t            try:\n347\t                data = json.loads(payload)\n348\t                usage = data.get(\"usage\")\n349\t            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n350\t                continue\n351\t\n352\t        # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response (single message object)\n353\t        # The body comes after a blank line following the headers\n354\t        if usage is None:\n355\t            # Find the last {...\"type\":\"message\"...} JSON in the content\n356\t            for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n357\t                line = line.strip()\n358\t                if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n359\t                    continue\n360\t                try:\n361\t                    msg = json.loads(line)\n362\t                    if msg.get(\"type\") == \"message\" and \"usage\" in msg:\n363\t                        usage = msg[\"usage\"]\n364\t                        break\n365\t                except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n366\t                    continue\n367\t\n368\t        if usage is None:\n369\t            print(f\"  Warning: no usage found in {response_path}\")\n370\t            continue\n371\t\n372\t        # Keep only the token count fields we need\n373\t        TOKEN_FIELDS = (\"input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\")\n374\t        usage = {k: v for k, v in usage.items() if k in TOKEN_FIELDS}\n375\t\n376\t        # Merge timing data if available\n377\t        timing_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"timing.json\")\n378\t        if os.path.exists(timing_path):\n379\t            with open(timing_path, \"r\") as f:\n380\t                timing = json.load(f)\n381\t            request_start = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n382\t            response_end = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n383\t            timing_block = {}\n384\t            if request_start:\n385\t                timing_block[\"request_start\"] = request_start\n386\t            if response_end:\n387\t                timing_block[\"response_end\"] = response_end\n388\t            if request_start and response_end:\n389\t                timing_block[\"duration_ms\"] = round((response_end - request_start) * 1000)\n390\t            if timing_block:\n391\t                usage[\"timing\"] = timing_block\n392\t            os.remove(timing_path)\n393\t\n394\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n395\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n396\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n397\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n398\t        count += 1\n399\t\n400\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted usage for {count} flows\")\n401\t\n402\t\n403\t\n404\tdef extract_prompts(directory: str):\n405\t    \"\"\"Extract system prompt and first user message from request.json files into per-request markdown files.\"\"\"\n406\t    count = 0\n407\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n408\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames:\n409\t            continue\n410\t\n411\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n412\t\n413\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n414\t        if body is None:\n415\t            print(f\"  Warning: no JSON body found in {request_path}\")\n416\t            continue\n417\t\n418\t        # System prompt: concatenate all text blocks from body[\"system\"]\n419\t        system = body.get(\"system\")\n420\t        if system and isinstance(system, list):\n421\t            texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in system if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n422\t            system_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n423\t            if system_text:\n424\t                with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"system_prompt.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n425\t                    f.write(system_text)\n426\t\n427\t        # First user message: find first message with role==\"user\", concatenate text blocks\n428\t        messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n429\t        for msg in messages:\n430\t            if msg.get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n431\t                content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n432\t                if isinstance(content, list):\n433\t                    texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in content if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n434\t                    user_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n435\t                    if user_text:\n436\t                        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"first_user_message.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n437\t                            f.write(user_text)\n438\t                break\n439\t\n440\t        count += 1\n441\t\n442\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted prompts for {count} requests\")\n443\t\n444\t\n445\t\n446\tdef _resolve_read_file_name(name, tool_input):\n447\t    \"\"\"Resolve read_file tool name to compressed/uncompressed variant.\"\"\"\n448\t    if name == \"read_file\":\n449\t        mode = tool_input.get(\"mode\", \"original\") if isinstance(tool_input, dict) else \"original\"\n450\t        return \"read_file_compressed\" if mode == \"compress\" else \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n451\t    return name\n452\t\n453\t\n454\tdef extract_read_file_whitespace(body):\n455\t    \"\"\"Extract whitespace stats from read_file/Read tool results in the request body.\"\"\"\n456\t    ws = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n457\t\n458\t    # Build tool_use_id -> tool_name map from assistant messages\n459\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n460\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n461\t    for msg in messages:\n462\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n463\t            continue\n464\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n465\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n466\t            continue\n467\t        for block in content:\n468\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n469\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n470\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n471\t\n472\t    for msg in messages:\n473\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n474\t            continue\n475\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n476\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n477\t            continue\n478\t        for block in content:\n479\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n480\t                continue\n481\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n482\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n483\t            if not (tool_name.startswith(\"read_file\") or tool_name == \"Read\"):\n484\t                continue\n485\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n486\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n487\t                text_for_ws = result_content\n488\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n489\t                text_for_ws = \"\".join(b.get(\"text\", \"\") for b in result_content)\n490\t            else:\n491\t                text_for_ws = \"\"\n492\t            stats = count_whitespace_stats(text_for_ws)\n493\t            for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n494\t                ws[k] += stats[k]\n495\t\n496\t    return ws\n497\t\n498\t\n499\tdef categorize_input_sources(body):"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M4unhqrZK8K7jkPWALMQ3A","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","limit":250,"offset":499}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M4unhqrZK8K7jkPWALMQ3A","type":"tool_result","content":"499\tdef categorize_input_sources(body):\n500\t    \"\"\"Count input characters from tool results and tool use blocks, split by cache position.\n501\t\n502\t    Returns: {\n503\t        \"total_chars\": int,  # total chars of entire request body\n504\t        \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 1234}, ...},\n505\t        \"tool_calls\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 567}, ...},\n506\t    }\n507\t\n508\t    Position logic:\n509\t    - Last user message content ‚Üí cache_write (new content being written to cache)\n510\t    - Second-to-last message (assistant before last user) ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use blocks\n511\t    - Everything else ‚Üí cache_read\n512\t    \"\"\"\n513\t    total_chars = len(json.dumps(body))\n514\t    tool_results = {}\n515\t    tool_calls = {}\n516\t\n517\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n518\t\n519\t    # Find last user message index and second-to-last message index\n520\t    last_user_idx = -1\n521\t    for i in range(len(messages) - 1, -1, -1):\n522\t        if messages[i].get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n523\t            last_user_idx = i\n524\t            break\n525\t    second_to_last_idx = last_user_idx - 1 if last_user_idx > 0 else -1\n526\t\n527\t    # Build tool_use_id -> tool_name map from assistant messages\n528\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n529\t    for msg in messages:\n530\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n531\t            continue\n532\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n533\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n534\t            continue\n535\t        for block in content:\n536\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n537\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n538\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n539\t\n540\t    # Collect tool_result chars from user messages\n541\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n542\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n543\t            continue\n544\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n545\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n546\t            continue\n547\t        is_cache_write = (i == last_user_idx)\n548\t        for block in content:\n549\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n550\t                continue\n551\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n552\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n553\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n554\t            if tool_name not in tool_results:\n555\t                tool_results[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n556\t            if is_cache_write:\n557\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n558\t            else:\n559\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n560\t\n561\t    # Collect tool_use chars from assistant messages\n562\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n563\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n564\t            continue\n565\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n566\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n567\t            continue\n568\t        is_cache_write = (i == second_to_last_idx)\n569\t        for block in content:\n570\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n571\t                continue\n572\t            tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n573\t                block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n574\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n575\t            if tool_name not in tool_calls:\n576\t                tool_calls[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n577\t            if is_cache_write:\n578\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n579\t            else:\n580\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n581\t\n582\t    return {\"total_chars\": total_chars, \"tool_results\": tool_results, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n583\t\n584\t\n585\tdef categorize_output_sources(response_path):\n586\t    \"\"\"Count output characters from the actual response (SSE stream or single JSON).\n587\t\n588\t    Parses content_block_start/delta/stop events from response_raw.txt.\n589\t    Returns: {\"llm_text\": int, \"tool_calls\": {\"ToolName\": int, ...}}\n590\t    \"\"\"\n591\t    llm_text_chars = 0\n592\t    tool_calls = {}\n593\t\n594\t    with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n595\t        content = f.read()\n596\t\n597\t    # State machine for SSE content blocks\n598\t    # blocks[index] = {\"type\": \"text\"|\"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"text\": str, \"json\": str}\n599\t    blocks = {}\n600\t    found_sse = False\n601\t\n602\t    for line in content.splitlines():\n603\t        line = line.strip()\n604\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n605\t            continue\n606\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n607\t        try:\n608\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n609\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n610\t            continue\n611\t\n612\t        event_type = data.get(\"type\", \"\")\n613\t\n614\t        if event_type == \"content_block_start\":\n615\t            found_sse = True\n616\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n617\t            cb = data.get(\"content_block\", {})\n618\t            blocks[idx] = {\n619\t                \"type\": cb.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n620\t                \"name\": cb.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n621\t                \"text\": \"\",\n622\t                \"json\": \"\",\n623\t            }\n624\t\n625\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_delta\":\n626\t            found_sse = True\n627\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n628\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n629\t            delta_type = delta.get(\"type\", \"\")\n630\t            if idx in blocks:\n631\t                if delta_type == \"text_delta\":\n632\t                    blocks[idx][\"text\"] += delta.get(\"text\", \"\")\n633\t                elif delta_type == \"input_json_delta\":\n634\t                    blocks[idx][\"json\"] += delta.get(\"partial_json\", \"\")\n635\t\n636\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_stop\":\n637\t            found_sse = True\n638\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n639\t            if idx in blocks:\n640\t                block = blocks[idx]\n641\t                if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n642\t                    llm_text_chars += len(block[\"text\"])\n643\t                elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n644\t                    try:\n645\t                        input_data = json.loads(block[\"json\"]) if block[\"json\"] else {}\n646\t                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n647\t                        input_data = {}\n648\t                    tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(block[\"name\"], input_data)\n649\t                    # Reconstruct full block to count all chars (id, name, type, input)\n650\t                    full_block = {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block[\"name\"], \"input\": input_data}\n651\t                    chars = len(json.dumps(full_block))\n652\t                    tool_calls[tool_name] = tool_calls.get(tool_name, 0) + chars\n653\t                del blocks[idx]\n654\t\n655\t    # Non-streaming fallback: parse single JSON message\n656\t    if not found_sse:\n657\t        for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n658\t            line = line.strip()\n659\t            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n660\t                continue\n661\t            try:\n662\t                msg = json.loads(line)\n663\t                if msg.get(\"type\") != \"message\":\n664\t                    continue\n665\t                for block in msg.get(\"content\", []):\n666\t                    btype = block.get(\"type\", \"\")\n667\t                    if btype == \"text\":\n668\t                        llm_text_chars += len(block.get(\"text\", \"\"))\n669\t                    elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n670\t                        tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n671\t                            block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n672\t                        chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n673\t                        tool_calls[tool_name] = tool_calls.get(tool_name, 0) + chars\n674\t                break\n675\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n676\t                continue\n677\t\n678\t    return {\"llm_text\": llm_text_chars, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n679\t\n680\t\n681\tdef _format_tool_params(input_data):\n682\t    \"\"\"Format tool input as compact param=value pairs.\"\"\"\n683\t    parts = []\n684\t    for key, value in input_data.items():\n685\t        if isinstance(value, str):\n686\t            parts.append(f'{key}=\"{value}\"')\n687\t        else:\n688\t            parts.append(f\"{key}={json.dumps(value)}\")\n689\t    return \", \".join(parts)\n690\t\n691\t\n692\tdef parse_response_content(response_path):\n693\t    \"\"\"Parse response_raw.txt into a list of content blocks.\n694\t\n695\t    Returns: list of {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": str} or {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"input\": dict}\n696\t    \"\"\"\n697\t    with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n698\t        content = f.read()\n699\t\n700\t    # SSE streaming parse\n701\t    blocks = {}\n702\t    finished = []\n703\t    found_sse = False\n704\t\n705\t    for line in content.splitlines():\n706\t        line = line.strip()\n707\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n708\t            continue\n709\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n710\t        try:\n711\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n712\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n713\t            continue\n714\t\n715\t        event_type = data.get(\"type\", \"\")\n716\t\n717\t        if event_type == \"content_block_start\":\n718\t            found_sse = True\n719\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n720\t            cb = data.get(\"content_block\", {})\n721\t            blocks[idx] = {\n722\t                \"type\": cb.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n723\t                \"name\": cb.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n724\t                \"text\": \"\",\n725\t                \"json\": \"\",\n726\t            }\n727\t\n728\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_delta\":\n729\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n730\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n731\t            delta_type = delta.get(\"type\", \"\")\n732\t            if idx in blocks:\n733\t                if delta_type == \"text_delta\":\n734\t                    blocks[idx][\"text\"] += delta.get(\"text\", \"\")\n735\t                elif delta_type == \"input_json_delta\":\n736\t                    blocks[idx][\"json\"] += delta.get(\"partial_json\", \"\")\n737\t\n738\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_stop\":\n739\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n740\t            if idx in blocks:\n741\t                block = blocks[idx]\n742\t                if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n743\t                    finished.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": block[\"text\"]})\n744\t                elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n745\t                    try:\n746\t                        input_data = json.loads(block[\"json\"]) if block[\"json\"] else {}\n747\t                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n748\t                        input_data = {}"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F7XxyG6a8LXgjiq6yfKdyJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","limit":250,"offset":749}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F7XxyG6a8LXgjiq6yfKdyJ","type":"tool_result","content":"749\t                    finished.append({\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block[\"name\"], \"input\": input_data})\n750\t                del blocks[idx]\n751\t\n752\t    # Non-streaming fallback\n753\t    if not found_sse:\n754\t        for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n755\t            line = line.strip()\n756\t            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n757\t                continue\n758\t            try:\n759\t                msg = json.loads(line)\n760\t                if msg.get(\"type\") != \"message\":\n761\t                    continue\n762\t                for block in msg.get(\"content\", []):\n763\t                    btype = block.get(\"type\", \"\")\n764\t                    if btype == \"text\":\n765\t                        finished.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": block.get(\"text\", \"\")})\n766\t                    elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n767\t                        finished.append({\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), \"input\": block.get(\"input\", {})})\n768\t                break\n769\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n770\t                continue\n771\t\n772\t    return finished\n773\t\n774\t\n775\tdef export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path):\n776\t    \"\"\"Parse response_raw.txt and write a human-readable response_parsed.txt.\n777\t\n778\t    Text blocks are output as-is. Tool calls are displayed inline with params.\n779\t    \"\"\"\n780\t    blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n781\t    if not blocks:\n782\t        return False\n783\t\n784\t    lines = []\n785\t    for block in blocks:\n786\t        if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n787\t            lines.append(block[\"text\"])\n788\t        elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n789\t            params = _format_tool_params(block[\"input\"])\n790\t            lines.append(f'\\n[{block[\"name\"]}({params})]\\n')\n791\t\n792\t    with open(output_path, \"w\") as f:\n793\t        f.write(\"\".join(lines))\n794\t    return True\n795\t\n796\t\n797\tdef export_parsed_responses(directory: str):\n798\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, export response_parsed.txt for each response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n799\t    count = 0\n800\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n801\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n802\t            continue\n803\t\n804\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n805\t        output_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_parsed.txt\")\n806\t\n807\t        if export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path):\n808\t            count += 1\n809\t\n810\t    print(f\"\\nExported parsed responses for {count} flows\")\n811\t\n812\t\n813\tdef attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing):\n814\t    \"\"\"Attribute tokens/cost to source categories.\n815\t\n816\t    Input side: raw character counts per tool (no token/cost distribution ‚Äî flawed due to caching).\n817\t    Output side: proportional token/cost distribution (valid since output isn't cached).\n818\t    \"\"\"\n819\t    by_source = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n820\t\n821\t    # Input: distribute input tokens proportionally using total_chars as denominator\n822\t    cost_data = usage.get(\"cost\", {})\n823\t    _ci = cost_data.get(\"input\", {})\n824\t    _cw = cost_data.get(\"cache_write\", {})\n825\t    _cr = cost_data.get(\"cache_read\", {})\n826\t    input_tokens = _ci.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cw.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cr.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n827\t\n828\t    total_chars = input_sources.get(\"total_chars\", 0)\n829\t\n830\t    def _attribute_input_tool(tool_char_dict):\n831\t        \"\"\"Compute tokens/dollars/chars for a tool given its {cache_write_chars, cache_read_chars}.\"\"\"\n832\t        cw_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0)\n833\t        cr_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0)\n834\t        cw_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cw_chars / total_chars))\n835\t        cr_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cr_chars / total_chars))\n836\t        dollars = (\n837\t            round(cw_tokens * pricing[\"cache_write\"], 6) +\n838\t            round(cr_tokens * pricing[\"cache_read\"], 6)\n839\t        )\n840\t        return {\"tokens\": cw_tokens + cr_tokens, \"dollars\": dollars, \"chars\": cw_chars + cr_chars}\n841\t\n842\t    if total_chars > 0 and input_tokens > 0 and pricing:\n843\t        # Tool results (from user messages)\n844\t        tool_results = input_sources.get(\"tool_results\", {})\n845\t        if tool_results:\n846\t            tr_entry = {}\n847\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_results.items():\n848\t                tr_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n849\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"] = tr_entry\n850\t\n851\t        # Tool calls (from assistant messages)\n852\t        tool_calls_input = input_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n853\t        if tool_calls_input:\n854\t            tc_entry = {}\n855\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_calls_input.items():\n856\t                tc_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n857\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n858\t\n859\t    # Output: distribute output tokens proportionally by character count\n860\t    output_cost_entry = cost_data.get(\"output\", {})\n861\t    output_tokens = output_cost_entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n862\t    output_dollars = output_cost_entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n863\t\n864\t    llm_chars = output_sources.get(\"llm_text\", 0)\n865\t    tc = output_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n866\t    tc_total_chars = sum(tc.values())\n867\t    total_output_chars = llm_chars + tc_total_chars\n868\t\n869\t    if total_output_chars > 0 and output_tokens > 0:\n870\t        # LLM text\n871\t        llm_frac = llm_chars / total_output_chars\n872\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"] = {\n873\t            \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * llm_frac),\n874\t            \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * llm_frac, 6),\n875\t            \"chars\": llm_chars,\n876\t        }\n877\t\n878\t        # Tool calls\n879\t        tc_frac = tc_total_chars / total_output_chars\n880\t        tc_entry = {\n881\t            \"__total\": {\n882\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tc_frac),\n883\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tc_frac, 6),\n884\t                \"chars\": tc_total_chars,\n885\t            }\n886\t        }\n887\t        for tool_name, chars in tc.items():\n888\t            tool_frac = chars / total_output_chars\n889\t            tc_entry[tool_name] = {\n890\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tool_frac),\n891\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tool_frac, 6),\n892\t                \"chars\": chars,\n893\t            }\n894\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n895\t\n896\t    return by_source\n897\t\n898\t\n899\tREAD_TOOLS = {\"read_file\", \"Read\", \"read_file_compressed\", \"read_file_uncompressed\"}\n900\tWRITE_TOOLS = {\"write_file\", \"Write\", \"edit_file\", \"Edit\"}\n901\t\n902\t\n903\t_PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n904\t\n905\t\n906\tdef _get_file_path(input_data):\n907\t    \"\"\"Extract file path from tool input, checking common key names. Always returns an absolute path.\"\"\"\n908\t    if not isinstance(input_data, dict):\n909\t        return None\n910\t    fp = input_data.get(\"file_path\") or input_data.get(\"path\") or None\n911\t    if fp and not os.path.isabs(fp):\n912\t        fp = os.path.join(_PROJECT_ROOT, fp)\n913\t    return fp\n914\t\n915\t\n916\tdef extract_file_ops(body, response_path):\n917\t    \"\"\"Extract file operation stats from request body (reads) and response (writes).\n918\t\n919\t    Returns: {\n920\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": int, \"total_read_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n921\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": int, \"total_write_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n922\t    }\n923\t    \"\"\"\n924\t    # --- Input: files read (from conversation history in request body) ---\n925\t    read_per_file = {}  # path -> {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n926\t\n927\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n928\t\n929\t    # Build tool_use_id -> (resolved_name, file_path) map from assistant messages\n930\t    tool_id_info = {}\n931\t    for msg in messages:\n932\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n933\t            continue\n934\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n935\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n936\t            continue\n937\t        for block in content:\n938\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n939\t                name = _resolve_read_file_name(block.get(\"name\", \"\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n940\t                if name in READ_TOOLS:\n941\t                    fp = _get_file_path(block.get(\"input\", {}))\n942\t                    tool_id_info[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = fp\n943\t\n944\t    # Sum chars from tool_result blocks matching read tools\n945\t    for msg in messages:\n946\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n947\t            continue\n948\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n949\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n950\t            continue\n951\t        for block in content:\n952\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n953\t                continue\n954\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n955\t            if tool_use_id not in tool_id_info:\n956\t                continue\n957\t            fp = tool_id_info[tool_use_id]\n958\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n959\t            chars = 0\n960\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n961\t                chars = len(result_content)\n962\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n963\t                chars = sum(len(b.get(\"text\", \"\")) for b in result_content)\n964\t            if fp:\n965\t                if fp not in read_per_file:\n966\t                    read_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n967\t                read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tool_use_id] = chars\n968\t                read_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n969\t                read_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n970\t\n971\t    # --- Output: files written (from response) ---\n972\t    write_per_file = {}  # path -> {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n973\t\n974\t    response_blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n975\t    for block in response_blocks:\n976\t        if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n977\t            continue\n978\t        name = block.get(\"name\", \"\")\n979\t        if name not in WRITE_TOOLS:\n980\t            continue\n981\t        inp = block.get(\"input\", {})\n982\t        fp = _get_file_path(inp)\n983\t        # Sum content chars: \"content\" for Write/write_file, \"new_string\" for Edit/edit_file\n984\t        chars = 0\n985\t        if name in (\"Write\", \"write_file\"):\n986\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"content\", \"\"))\n987\t        elif name in (\"Edit\", \"edit_file\"):\n988\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"new_string\", \"\"))\n989\t        if fp:\n990\t            block_id = block.get(\"id\", \"\")\n991\t            if fp not in write_per_file:\n992\t                write_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n993\t            write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][block_id] = chars\n994\t            write_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n995\t            write_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n996\t\n997\t    # Add file_size for each file\n998\t    for pf in (read_per_file, write_per_file):"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LSuWybtVAnK6C8CxXSPNyp","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","limit":250,"offset":997}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LSuWybtVAnK6C8CxXSPNyp","type":"tool_result","content":"997\t    # Add file_size for each file\n998\t    for pf in (read_per_file, write_per_file):\n999\t        for fp in pf:\n1000\t            try:\n1001\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = os.path.getsize(fp)\n1002\t            except OSError:\n1003\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = None\n1004\t\n1005\t    # Derive aggregate scalars from deduplicated per_file data\n1006\t    unique_files_read = len(read_per_file)\n1007\t    total_read_chars = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in read_per_file.values())\n1008\t    unique_files_written = len(write_per_file)\n1009\t    total_write_chars_dedup = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n1010\t    total_write_calls = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n1011\t\n1012\t    return {\n1013\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": unique_files_read, \"total_read_chars\": total_read_chars, \"per_file\": read_per_file},\n1014\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": total_write_calls, \"unique_files_written\": unique_files_written, \"total_write_chars\": total_write_chars_dedup, \"per_file\": write_per_file},\n1015\t    }\n1016\t\n1017\t\n1018\tdef extract_source_attribution(directory: str):\n1019\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute source attribution, read_file whitespace, and file ops.\"\"\"\n1020\t    count = 0\n1021\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n1022\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames or \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n1023\t            continue\n1024\t\n1025\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n1026\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n1027\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n1028\t\n1029\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n1030\t        if body is None:\n1031\t            continue\n1032\t\n1033\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1034\t            usage = json.load(f)\n1035\t\n1036\t        # Get model pricing\n1037\t        model = body.get(\"model\", \"\")\n1038\t        pricing = get_pricing(model) if model else None\n1039\t\n1040\t        # Compute source attribution\n1041\t        input_sources = categorize_input_sources(body)\n1042\t        output_sources = categorize_output_sources(response_path)\n1043\t        by_source = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)\n1044\t\n1045\t        usage[\"by_source\"] = by_source\n1046\t\n1047\t        # Compute read_file whitespace\n1048\t        usage[\"read_file_whitespace\"] = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n1049\t\n1050\t        # Compute file operations\n1051\t        usage[\"file_ops\"] = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n1052\t\n1053\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n1054\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n1055\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n1056\t        count += 1\n1057\t\n1058\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted source attribution for {count} flows\")\n1059\t\n1060\t\n1061\tdef calculate_costs(directory: str):\n1062\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute dollar costs from usage.json and request.json model info.\"\"\"\n1063\t    count = 0\n1064\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n1065\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames:\n1066\t            continue\n1067\t\n1068\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n1069\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n1070\t        if body is None:\n1071\t            continue\n1072\t\n1073\t        model = body.get(\"model\")\n1074\t        if not model:\n1075\t            continue\n1076\t\n1077\t        pricing = get_pricing(model)\n1078\t        if pricing is None:\n1079\t            print(f\"  Warning: unknown model '{model}' in {request_path}, skipping cost calculation\")\n1080\t            continue\n1081\t\n1082\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n1083\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1084\t            usage = json.load(f)\n1085\t\n1086\t        tokens_input = usage.get(\"input_tokens\", 0)\n1087\t        tokens_cache_write = usage.get(\"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0)\n1088\t        tokens_cache_read = usage.get(\"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0)\n1089\t        tokens_output = usage.get(\"output_tokens\", 0)\n1090\t        tokens_total = tokens_input + tokens_cache_write + tokens_cache_read + tokens_output\n1091\t\n1092\t        cost_input = tokens_input * pricing[\"input\"]\n1093\t        cost_cache_write = tokens_cache_write * pricing[\"cache_write\"]\n1094\t        cost_cache_read = tokens_cache_read * pricing[\"cache_read\"]\n1095\t        cost_output = tokens_output * pricing[\"output\"]\n1096\t        cost_total = cost_input + cost_cache_write + cost_cache_read + cost_output\n1097\t\n1098\t        usage[\"cost\"] = {\n1099\t            \"input\": {\"tokens\": tokens_input, \"dollars\": round(cost_input, 6)},\n1100\t            \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_write, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_write, 6)},\n1101\t            \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_read, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_read, 6)},\n1102\t            \"output\": {\"tokens\": tokens_output, \"dollars\": round(cost_output, 6)},\n1103\t            \"total\": {\"tokens\": tokens_total, \"dollars\": round(cost_total, 6)},\n1104\t        }\n1105\t\n1106\t        # Remove top-level token keys (now redundant with cost entries)\n1107\t        for key in (\"input_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\"):\n1108\t            usage.pop(key, None)\n1109\t\n1110\t        canonical = get_canonical_model(model)\n1111\t        if canonical:\n1112\t            usage[\"model\"] = canonical\n1113\t\n1114\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n1115\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n1116\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n1117\t        count += 1\n1118\t\n1119\t    print(f\"\\nCalculated costs for {count} flows\")\n1120\t\n1121\t\n1122\tdef _aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source):\n1123\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-flow by_source into summary by_source.\n1124\t\n1125\t    Input side: sum tool_results {tokens, dollars} dicts.\n1126\t    Output side: sum token/dollars dicts.\n1127\t    \"\"\"\n1128\t    # Input: tool_results and tool_calls are {tokens, dollars} dicts\n1129\t    flow_input = flow_by_source.get(\"input\", {})\n1130\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n1131\t        flow_section = flow_input.get(input_key, {})\n1132\t        if not flow_section:\n1133\t            continue\n1134\t        if input_key not in agg[\"input\"]:\n1135\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key] = {}\n1136\t        for tool, entry in flow_section.items():\n1137\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n1138\t                continue\n1139\t            if tool not in agg[\"input\"][input_key]:\n1140\t                agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1141\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1142\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1143\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1144\t\n1145\t    # Output: token/dollars dicts\n1146\t    flow_output = flow_by_source.get(\"output\", {})\n1147\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n1148\t        entry = flow_output.get(key)\n1149\t        if entry:\n1150\t            if key not in agg[\"output\"]:\n1151\t                agg[\"output\"][key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1152\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1153\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1154\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1155\t\n1156\t    # Tool calls\n1157\t    flow_tc = flow_output.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n1158\t    if flow_tc:\n1159\t        if \"tool_calls\" not in agg[\"output\"]:\n1160\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = {}\n1161\t        for tool_key, entry in flow_tc.items():\n1162\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n1163\t                continue\n1164\t            if tool_key not in agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"]:\n1165\t                agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1166\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1167\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1168\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1169\t\n1170\t\n1171\tdef _round_by_source(agg):\n1172\t    \"\"\"Round dollar values in the by_source aggregate.\"\"\"\n1173\t    # Input: round dollars\n1174\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n1175\t        section = agg.get(\"input\", {}).get(input_key, {})\n1176\t        for entry in section.values():\n1177\t            if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n1178\t                entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1179\t    # Output: round dollars\n1180\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n1181\t        entry = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(key)\n1182\t        if entry:\n1183\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1184\t    tc = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n1185\t    for entry in tc.values():\n1186\t        if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n1187\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1188\t\n1189\t\n1190\tAGENT_COLORS = {\n1191\t    \"vix\": \"#7B2FBE\",\n1192\t    \"cc\": \"#D77656\",\n1193\t}\n1194\t\n1195\t\n1196\tdef _agent_color(name):\n1197\t    \"\"\"Return a deterministic hex color for an unknown agent name.\"\"\"\n1198\t    import hashlib\n1199\t    h = int(hashlib.md5(name.encode()).hexdigest()[:6], 16)\n1200\t    return f\"#{h:06x}\"\n1201\t\n1202\t\n1203\tdef summarize_usage(directory: str):\n1204\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-request usage.json files into a summary usage.json per agent type.\"\"\"\n1205\t    COST_FIELDS = [\"input\", \"cache_write\", \"cache_read\", \"output\", \"total\"]\n1206\t\n1207\t    def empty_bucket():\n1208\t        bucket = {\"request_count\": 0}\n1209\t        bucket[\"cost\"] = {f: {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0} for f in COST_FIELDS}\n1210\t        bucket[\"timing\"] = {\n1211\t            \"total_duration_ms\": 0,\n1212\t            \"min_request_start\": None, \"max_response_end\": None,\n1213\t        }\n1214\t        return bucket\n1215\t\n1216\t    def add_to_bucket(bucket, usage):\n1217\t        bucket[\"request_count\"] += 1\n1218\t        cost = usage.get(\"cost\")\n1219\t        if cost:\n1220\t            for f in COST_FIELDS:\n1221\t                entry = cost.get(f, {})\n1222\t                if isinstance(entry, dict):\n1223\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1224\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1225\t        timing = usage.get(\"timing\")\n1226\t        if timing:\n1227\t            bucket[\"timing\"][\"total_duration_ms\"] += timing.get(\"duration_ms\", 0)\n1228\t            rs = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n1229\t            re_ = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n1230\t            if rs is not None:\n1231\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"]\n1232\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"] = rs if cur is None else min(cur, rs)\n1233\t            if re_ is not None:\n1234\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"]\n1235\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"] = re_ if cur is None else max(cur, re_)\n1236\t\n1237\t    def round_costs(bucket):\n1238\t        for f in COST_FIELDS:\n1239\t            bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] = round(bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"], 6)\n1240\t\n1241\t    count = 0\n1242\t    for entry in sorted(os.listdir(directory)):\n1243\t        agent_dir = os.path.join(directory, entry)\n1244\t        if not os.path.isdir(agent_dir):\n1245\t            continue\n1246\t"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KLvzX1oAHKRHua3JKsP3dj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","limit":200,"offset":1246}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KLvzX1oAHKRHua3JKsP3dj","type":"tool_result","content":"1246\t\n1247\t        # Only process dirs that contain numbered step subdirs\n1248\t        has_numbered = False\n1249\t        for sub in os.listdir(agent_dir):\n1250\t            if sub.isdigit() and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(agent_dir, sub)):\n1251\t                has_numbered = True\n1252\t                break\n1253\t        if not has_numbered:\n1254\t            continue\n1255\t\n1256\t        by_model = {}\n1257\t        by_step = {}\n1258\t        total = empty_bucket()\n1259\t        ws_agg = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n1260\t        by_source_agg = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n1261\t        file_ops_agg = {\n1262\t            \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1263\t            \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1264\t        }\n1265\t\n1266\t        # Iterate step dirs: {agent_dir}/{step_number}/\n1267\t        for step_sub in sorted(os.listdir(agent_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n1268\t            if not step_sub.isdigit():\n1269\t                continue\n1270\t            step_dir = os.path.join(agent_dir, step_sub)\n1271\t            if not os.path.isdir(step_dir):\n1272\t                continue\n1273\t\n1274\t            step_key = step_sub  # Use step directory number as key\n1275\t\n1276\t            # Iterate request dirs: {step_dir}/{request_number}/usage.json\n1277\t            for req_sub in sorted(os.listdir(step_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n1278\t                if not req_sub.isdigit():\n1279\t                    continue\n1280\t                usage_path = os.path.join(step_dir, req_sub, \"usage.json\")\n1281\t                if not os.path.isfile(usage_path):\n1282\t                    continue\n1283\t\n1284\t                with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1285\t                    usage = json.load(f)\n1286\t\n1287\t                model_name = usage.get(\"model\", \"unknown\")\n1288\t                if model_name not in by_model:\n1289\t                    by_model[model_name] = empty_bucket()\n1290\t                add_to_bucket(by_model[model_name], usage)\n1291\t\n1292\t                add_to_bucket(total, usage)\n1293\t\n1294\t                # Aggregate by_source\n1295\t                flow_by_source = usage.get(\"by_source\")\n1296\t                if flow_by_source:\n1297\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_source_agg, flow_by_source)\n1298\t\n1299\t                # Aggregate read_file whitespace\n1300\t                flow_ws = usage.get(\"read_file_whitespace\")\n1301\t                if flow_ws:\n1302\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n1303\t                        ws_agg[k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n1304\t\n1305\t                # Aggregate file_ops\n1306\t                flow_file_ops = usage.get(\"file_ops\")\n1307\t                if flow_file_ops:\n1308\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n1309\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n1310\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n1311\t                    # Aggregate per-file details (merge tool_ids maps for dedup)\n1312\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n1313\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n1314\t                            agg_pf = file_ops_agg[side][\"per_file\"]\n1315\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n1316\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n1317\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n1318\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n1319\t\n1320\t                # Aggregate per step\n1321\t                if step_key not in by_step:\n1322\t                    by_step[step_key] = empty_bucket()\n1323\t                    by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"] = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n1324\t                    by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"] = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n1325\t                    by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"] = {\n1326\t                        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1327\t                        \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1328\t                    }\n1329\t                add_to_bucket(by_step[step_key], usage)\n1330\t                if flow_by_source:\n1331\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"], flow_by_source)\n1332\t                if f