,7:headers;1620:40:4:Date,29:Mon, 06 Apr 2026 11:51:15 GMT,]52:12:Content-Type,32:text/event-stream; charset=utf-8,]31:17:Transfer-Encoding,7:chunked,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:13:Cache-Control,8:no-cache,]52:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-limit,7:2000000,]56:42:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-remaining,7:1966000,]66:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T11:51:14Z,]52:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-limit,6:400000,]56:43:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-remaining,6:400000,]67:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T11:51:13Z,]45:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-limit,4:4000,]49:38:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-remaining,4:3999,]62:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-reset,20:2026-04-06T11:51:13Z,]46:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-limit,7:2400000,]50:36:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-remaining,7:2366000,]60:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T11:51:13Z,]46:10:request-id,28:req_011CZnU8mM4CGFQCMv7BFeMR,]77:25:strict-transport-security,44:max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload,]69:25:anthropic-organization-id,36:19d39eaa-efb4-49e0-afe8-a7359703719a,]23:6:Server,10:cloudflare,]40:29:x-envoy-upstream-service-time,4:2213,]46:13:server-timing,25:x-originResponse;dur=2295,]208:10:set-cookie,189:_cfuvid=6.qEomGL9YhG4pZ36nUaxtIzgrinl7xytTczh9hcIKs-1775476273.0291474-1.0.1.1-8QFOTuB8CwI.uFRtiBIv61fLbu.95u_9fm8j9HRRtOc; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Domain=api.anthropic.com,]23:12:X-Robots-Tag,4:none,]29:15:cf-cache-status,7:DYNAMIC,]73:23:Content-Security-Policy,42:default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none',]33:6:CF-RAY,20:9e8094526d18bf50-DUB,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}7:request;381192:4:path;22:/v1/messages?beta=true,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;18:1775476272.9569244^15:timestamp_start;18:1775476272.9553995^8:trailers;0:~7:content;379924:{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so m‚Ä¶\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo, defaults to 10m) - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep‚Ä¶\n- claude-api: Build apps with the Claude API or Anthropic SDK.\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`/`claude_agent_sdk`, or user asks to use Claude API, Anthropic SDKs, or Agent SDK.\nDO NOT TRIGGER when: code imports `openai`/other AI SDK, ge‚Ä¶\n</system-reminder>"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nPlan mode is active. The user indicated that they do not want you to execute yet -- you MUST NOT make any edits (with the exception of the plan file mentioned below), run any non-readonly tools (including changing configs or making commits), or otherwise make any changes to the system. This supercedes any other instructions you have received.\n\n## Plan File Info:\nNo plan file exists yet. You should create your plan at /root/.claude/plans/tingly-forging-canyon.md using the Write tool.\nYou should build your plan incrementally by writing to or editing this file. NOTE that this is the only file you are allowed to edit - other than this you are only allowed to take READ-ONLY actions.\n\n## Plan Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: Initial Understanding\nGoal: Gain a comprehensive understanding of the user's request by reading through code and asking them questions. Critical: In this phase you should only use the Explore subagent type.\n\n1. Focus on understanding the user's request and the code associated with their request. Actively search for existing functions, utilities, and patterns that can be reused ‚Äî avoid proposing new code when suitable implementations already exist.\n\n2. **Launch up to 3 Explore agents IN PARALLEL** (single message, multiple tool calls) to efficiently explore the codebase.\n   - Use 1 agent when the task is isolated to known files, the user provided specific file paths, or you're making a small targeted change.\n   - Use multiple agents when: the scope is uncertain, multiple areas of the codebase are involved, or you need to understand existing patterns before planning.\n   - Quality over quantity - 3 agents maximum, but you should try to use the minimum number of agents necessary (usually just 1)\n   - If using multiple agents: Provide each agent with a specific search focus or area to explore. Example: One agent searches for existing implementations, another explores related components, a third investigating testing patterns\n\n### Phase 2: Design\nGoal: Design an implementation approach.\n\nLaunch Plan agent(s) to design the implementation based on the user's intent and your exploration results from Phase 1.\n\nYou can launch up to 1 agent(s) in parallel.\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- **Default**: Launch at least 1 Plan agent for most tasks - it helps validate your understanding and consider alternatives\n- **Skip agents**: Only for truly trivial tasks (typo fixes, single-line changes, simple renames)\n\nIn the agent prompt:\n- Provide comprehensive background context from Phase 1 exploration including filenames and code path traces\n- Describe requirements and constraints\n- Request a detailed implementation plan\n\n### Phase 3: Review\nGoal: Review the plan(s) from Phase 2 and ensure alignment with the user's intentions.\n1. Read the critical files identified by agents to deepen your understanding\n2. Ensure that the plans align with the user's original request\n3. Use AskUserQuestion to clarify any remaining questions with the user\n\n### Phase 4: Final Plan\nGoal: Write your final plan to the plan file (the only file you can edit).\n- Begin with a **Context** section: explain why this change is being made ‚Äî the problem or need it addresses, what prompted it, and the intended outcome\n- Include only your recommended approach, not all alternatives\n- Ensure that the plan file is concise enough to scan quickly, but detailed enough to execute effectively\n- Include the paths of critical files to be modified\n- Reference existing functions and utilities you found that should be reused, with their file paths\n- Include a verification section describing how to test the changes end-to-end (run the code, use MCP tools, run tests)\n\n### Phase 5: Call ExitPlanMode\nAt the very end of your turn, once you have asked the user questions and are happy with your final plan file - you should always call ExitPlanMode to indicate to the user that you are done planning.\nThis is critical - your turn should only end with either using the AskUserQuestion tool OR calling ExitPlanMode. Do not stop unless it's for these 2 reasons\n\n**Important:** Use AskUserQuestion ONLY to clarify requirements or choose between approaches. Use ExitPlanMode to request plan approval. Do NOT ask about plan approval in any other way - no text questions, no AskUserQuestion. Phrases like \"Is this plan okay?\", \"Should I proceed?\", \"How does this plan look?\", \"Any changes before we start?\", or similar MUST use ExitPlanMode.\n\nNOTE: At any point in time through this workflow you should feel free to ask the user questions or clarifications using the AskUserQuestion tool. Don't make large assumptions about user intent. The goal is to present a well researched plan to the user, and tie any loose ends before implementation begins.\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-04-06.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Write tests for evaluation/usage/export_flows.py to achieve at least 80% code coverage. Read the file to understand all the functions, then write a comprehensive test suite in evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py. Use pytest with mocks for filesystem and mitmproxy dependencies. Focus on testing the pure logic functions with various inputs, edge cases, and error paths."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011sdCqoKtM92nJp5XSwbugs","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore export_flows.py and related files","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"Read and analyze the file at /workspace/evaluation/usage/export_flows.py in full detail. Also check if there are any existing tests in /workspace/evaluation/usage/ directory, and look for any related files or imports that would help understand the context. Report back:\n1. The full content of export_flows.py\n2. All functions and their logic, including edge cases visible in the code\n3. Any existing test files in that directory\n4. The imports used (especially mitmproxy-related ones) so we can mock them properly"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011sdCqoKtM92nJp5XSwbugs","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete understanding. Let me create a comprehensive report:\n\n## Analysis Report: export_flows.py\n\n### 1. Full File Content\nThe file is located at `/workspace/export_flows.py` and is 1430 lines long. I've read it in full above.\n\n---\n\n### 2. All Functions and Their Logic\n\n#### **Data Constants (Lines 15-33)**\n- **SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX**: Maps agent names (\"cc\", \"vix\") to system prompt indices\n- **MODEL_PRICING**: Dict containing pricing for various Claude models with input, cache_write, cache_read, and output rates\n- **_SORTED_PREFIXES**: Pre-sorted model keys by length (longest first) for prefix matching\n\n#### **Utility Functions**\n\n**count_whitespace_stats(text)** (Lines 36-50)\n- Counts newlines, unnecessary spaces (runs of 2+ spaces), and total characters\n- Returns dict with line_returns_count, unnecessary_space_count, total_chars\n\n**parse_request_body(request_path: str)** (Lines 53-59)\n- Reads JSON from request.json file\n- Returns parsed dict or None on JSONDecodeError/ValueError\n\n**get_canonical_model(model_id: str)** (Lines 62-67)\n- Matches model_id (with optional date suffix) to canonical model name\n- Uses _SORTED_PREFIXES to ensure longest prefix matches first\n- Returns None if unknown\n\n**get_pricing(model_id: str)** (Lines 70-75)\n- Gets pricing dict for a model ID\n- Returns None if unknown\n\n**sanitize_path(path: str)** (Lines 78-84)\n- Converts URL path to safe directory name\n- Removes query string, replaces \"/\" with \"_\", strips trailing underscores\n- Removes non-alphanumeric characters except \"-\" and \"_\"\n- Limits to 80 characters\n\n**format_headers(headers)** (Lines 90-97)\n- Formats HTTP headers as text\n- Redacts x-api-key and authorization headers\n\n#### **Flow Export Functions**\n\n**write_request(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str)** (Lines 100-120)\n- Writes request headers to request_headers.txt (method, URL, headers)\n- Writes request body to request.json (pretty-printed if valid JSON)\n\n**write_response(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str)** (Lines 124-137)\n- Writes response status, headers, and body to response_raw.txt\n- Skips if response is None\n\n**extract_stop_reason(response_raw: str)** (Lines 140-173)\n- Extracts stop_reason from SSE streaming format (message_delta events)\n- Falls back to non-streaming JSON format\n- Returns \"unknown\" if not found\n- **Edge cases**: Handles both spacing variations in JSON (\"type\":\"message_delta\" vs \"type\": \"message_delta\")\n\n**redact_flow_files(directory: str)** (Lines 176-207)\n- In-place redaction of .flow files\n- Replaces x-api-key and authorization headers with \"[REDACTED]\"\n- Uses FlowReader/FlowWriter with error handling\n- Prints count of redacted files\n\n**_system_prompt_hash(body_json, agent_name)** (Lines 210-221)\n- Returns 12-char SHA256 hash of system prompt text\n- Uses agent-specific index from SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX\n- Returns None if prompt not found or index out of bounds\n\n**export_flows(input_dir: str, output_dir: str)** (Lines 224-323)\n- **Core function**: Exports .flow files into per-flow directory structure\n- Directory structure: {agent}/{step_index}/{request_index}/\n- **Step boundary logic**:\n  - For \"cc\" agent: step boundary when system prompt hash changes (checked BEFORE writing)\n  - For \"vix\" agent: step boundary when stop_reason == \"end_turn\" (checked AFTER writing)\n- **Flow filtering**:\n  - Skips /count_token URLs\n  - Skips \"quota\" message requests\n- **Output files per flow**: request_headers.txt, request.json, response_raw.txt, timing.json\n- **Edge cases**: \n  - Handles non-HTTPFlow types\n  - Handles missing response\n  - Handles JSON parsing failures gracefully\n  - Prints progress with step/request indices and stop_reason\n\n---\n\n#### **Token & Usage Extraction Functions**\n\n**extract_usage(directory: str)** (Lines 326-400)\n- Walks output directory finding response_raw.txt files\n- Extracts token usage from SSE message_delta events or fallback JSON\n- Keeps only: input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens\n- Merges timing data and computes duration_ms\n- Removes timing.json after processing\n\n**extract_prompts(directory: str)** (Lines 404-442)\n- Extracts system prompt and first user message\n- Writes system_prompt.md and first_user_message.md\n- Handles both system as list of text blocks and messages with content blocks\n\n**extract_read_file_whitespace(body)** (Lines 454-496)\n- Extracts whitespace stats from read_file/Read tool results in request body\n- Maps tool_use_id to tool_name using SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX resolution\n- Accumulates stats from all read tool results\n- **Edge cases**: Handles both string and list result_content formats\n\n**categorize_input_sources(body)** (Lines 499-582)\n- Counts input characters split by cache position\n- Returns structure with tool_results and tool_calls\n- **Logic**: Last user message content = cache_write, second-to-last assistant message = cache_write for tool_use, everything else = cache_read\n- **Edge cases**: Handles missing messages, non-list content\n\n**categorize_output_sources(response_path)** (Lines 585-678)\n- Counts output characters from response (SSE or single JSON)\n- Uses state machine for SSE content blocks\n- Reconstructs full blocks to count characters\n- Returns {\"llm_text\": int, \"tool_calls\": {toolname: int, ...}}\n\n**_format_tool_params(input_data)** (Lines 681-689)\n- Formats tool input as compact param=value pairs for display\n\n**parse_response_content(response_path)** (Lines 692-772)\n- Parses response_raw.txt into list of content blocks\n- SSE streaming parse with state machine\n- Fallback to non-streaming JSON\n- Returns: [{\"type\": \"text\"|\"tool_use\", ...}]\n\n**export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path)** (Lines 775-794)\n- Parses response and writes human-readable response_parsed.txt\n- Text blocks output as-is\n- Tool calls formatted inline with parameters\n\n**export_parsed_responses(directory: str)** (Lines 797-810)\n- Walks directory calling export_parsed_response for each response_raw.txt\n\n---\n\n#### **File Operation Tracking Functions**\n\n**_resolve_read_file_name(name, tool_input)** (Lines 446-451)\n- Resolves read_file to read_file_compressed or read_file_uncompressed based on mode\n\n**_get_file_path(input_data)** (Lines 906-913)\n- Extracts file_path from tool input\n- Converts relative paths to absolute using _PROJECT_ROOT\n- Returns None if not found\n\n**extract_file_ops(body, response_path)** (Lines 916-1015)\n- Extracts file operation stats from request (reads) and response (writes)\n- Builds tool_id_info map for read tools\n- Tracks per-file calls and character counts\n- Adds file_size for each file\n- Returns structure with per_file deduplication\n\n**extract_source_attribution(directory: str)** (Lines 1018-1058)\n- Walks directory computing source attribution\n- Calls: categorize_input_sources, categorize_output_sources, attribute_tokens\n- Also extracts read_file whitespace and file_ops\n- Merges into usage.json\n\n---\n\n#### **Cost Calculation Functions**\n\n**attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)** (Lines 813-896)\n- Attributes tokens/cost to source categories\n- Input side: uses total_chars for proportional distribution (acknowledges caching flaw)\n- Output side: proportional distribution by character count\n- Returns {\"input\": {...}, \"output\": {...}}\n\n**calculate_costs(directory: str)** (Lines 1061-1119)\n- Computes dollar costs from token usage and model pricing\n- Structures costs with input, cache_write, cache_read, output, total entries\n- Removes redundant top-level token keys\n- Normalizes model name to canonical form\n\n---\n\n#### **Aggregation & Summary Functions**\n\n**_aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source)** (Lines 1122-1168)\n- Aggregates per-flow by_source into summary\n- Sums tokens and dollars for tool_results, tool_calls, llm_text\n\n**_round_by_source(agg)** (Lines 1171-1187)\n- Rounds dollar values to 6 decimal places\n\n**summarize_usage(directory: str)** (Lines 1203-1402)\n- **Large complex function**: Aggregates per-request usage into per-agent summary\n- Walks agent directories with numbered step subdirectories\n- Aggregates by model, by step, and total\n- Finalizes file_ops, timing, and by_source aggregations\n- Returns structure with color, by_model, by_step, by_source, file_ops\n- **Edge cases**: Handles per-file deduplication with tool_ids maps\n\n**_agent_color(name)** (Lines 1196-1200)\n- Returns deterministic hex color using MD5 hash\n\n---\n\n#### **Main Entry Point**\n\n**main()** (Lines 1405-1425)\n- Orchestrates complete pipeline:\n  1. redact_flow_files() - remove API keys\n  2. export_flows() - parse .flow files\n  3. extract_usage() - extract token counts\n  4. export_parsed_responses() - human-readable responses\n  5. extract_prompts() - extract prompts to markdown\n  6. calculate_costs() - compute dollar costs\n  7. extract_source_attribution() - attribute tokens to sources\n  8. summarize_usage() - aggregate to summaries\n\n---\n\n### 3. Existing Test Files\n**Result: No test files exist** in the repository. Only `/workspace/export_flows.py` is present.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Imports Used (Especially mitmproxy-related)\n\n**mitmproxy imports** (Lines 11-13):\n```python\nfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter\nfrom mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\nfrom mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n```\n\n**Standard library imports** (Lines 4-10):\n- argparse, glob, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil\n\n**How to mock mitmproxy**:\n- **FlowReader**: Mock with a context manager that yields HTTPFlow objects\n- **FlowWriter**: Mock with add() method that accepts flow objects\n- **FlowReadException**: Custom exception for read errors\n- **HTTPFlow**: Object with request/response attributes; request has method, pretty_url, headers, get_text(); response has status_code, reason, headers, get_text(), timestamp_end; request has timestamp_start\n\n**Key flow structure for mocking**:\n```python\nHTTPFlow:\n  .request: \n    .method (str)\n    .pretty_url (str)\n    .headers (has .fields, .get(key))\n    .get_text(strict=False) -> str\n    .timestamp_start (float)\n  .response:\n    .status_code (int)\n    .reason (str)\n    .headers (has .fields, .get(key))\n    .get_text(strict=False) -> str\n    .timestamp_end (float)\n```"}]}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SCZWyaq7GxxzLffBP7ngBN","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Check project structure and test config","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"Look at the /workspace directory structure. I need to find:\n1. Any pytest.ini, setup.cfg, pyproject.toml, or conftest.py files\n2. The exact directory structure under /workspace/evaluation/usage/\n3. Read /workspace/evaluation/usage/export_flows.py lines 1-100 to confirm the actual file path and imports\n\nRun these searches and report back the exact file paths found."}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCZWyaq7GxxzLffBP7ngBN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me provide a comprehensive summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nBased on my thorough search of the /workspace directory:\n\n### 1. Configuration Files Search Results\n**None found.** There are no pytest.ini, setup.cfg, pyproject.toml, or conftest.py files anywhere in the /workspace directory structure.\n\n### 2. Directory Structure Under /workspace/evaluation/\n**Does not exist.** The `/workspace/evaluation/` directory does not exist in the current repository structure.\n\n### 3. export_flows.py File Location and First 100 Lines\n**File path:** `/workspace/export_flows.py` (located directly in /workspace, NOT under an evaluation/usage/ subdirectory)\n\n**Key imports (lines 1-100):**\n- Standard library: `argparse`, `glob`, `hashlib`, `json`, `os`, `re`, `shutil`\n- mitmproxy library: `from mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter`, `from mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException`, `from mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow`\n\n**File contents:** The file is a script for exporting mitmproxy flow files into per-flow directories with request.json, request_headers.txt, and response_raw.txt files. It includes model pricing configurations and various helper functions for processing HTTP flows.\n\n### Current /workspace Structure\n```\n/workspace/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ .DS_Store\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ .git/\n‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ export_flows.py\n```\n\n**Key Finding:** The export_flows.py script is directly in `/workspace/`, not in any evaluation/usage/ subdirectory as you were looking for."}]}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WtsY3gV7jGdhBWw5mCGqiY","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WtsY3gV7jGdhBWw5mCGqiY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Export mitmproxy flow files into per-flow directories with request.json, request_headers.txt, and response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n3\t\n4\timport argparse\n5\timport glob\n6\timport hashlib\n7\timport json\n8\timport os\n9\timport re\n10\timport shutil\n11\tfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter\n12\tfrom mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\n13\tfrom mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n14\t\n15\tSYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX = {\n16\t    \"cc\": 2,\n17\t    \"vix\": 0,\n18\t}\n19\t\n20\tMODEL_PRICING = {\n21\t    \"claude-opus-4-6\":   {\"input\": 5e-6,    \"cache_write\": 6.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.50e-6,  \"output\": 25e-6},\n22\t    \"claude-opus-4-5\":   {\"input\": 5e-6,    \"cache_write\": 6.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.50e-6,  \"output\": 25e-6},\n23\t    \"claude-opus-4-1\":   {\"input\": 15e-6,   \"cache_write\": 18.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 1.50e-6,  \"output\": 75e-6},\n24\t    \"claude-opus-4\":     {\"input\": 15e-6,   \"cache_write\": 18.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 1.50e-6,  \"output\": 75e-6},\n25\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\": {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n26\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-5\": {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n27\t    \"claude-sonnet-4\":   {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n28\t    \"claude-haiku-4-5\":  {\"input\": 1e-6,    \"cache_write\": 1.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.10e-6,  \"output\": 5e-6},\n29\t    \"claude-haiku-3-5\":  {\"input\": 0.80e-6, \"cache_write\": 1e-6,     \"cache_read\": 0.08e-6,  \"output\": 4e-6},\n30\t}\n31\t\n32\t# Sort prefixes longest-first so \"claude-opus-4-5\" matches before \"claude-opus-4\"\n33\t_SORTED_PREFIXES = sorted(MODEL_PRICING.keys(), key=len, reverse=True)\n34\t\n35\t\n36\tdef count_whitespace_stats(text):\n37\t    \"\"\"Count line returns and unnecessary spaces in text.\n38\t\n39\t    Returns dict with:\n40\t      - line_returns_count: number of \\\\n characters\n41\t      - unnecessary_space_count: for each run of 2+ spaces, count len(run) - 1\n42\t      - total_chars: total character count of the text\n43\t    \"\"\"\n44\t    line_returns = text.count(\"\\n\")\n45\t    unnecessary_spaces = sum(len(m) - 1 for m in re.findall(r\" {2,}\", text))\n46\t    return {\n47\t        \"line_returns_count\": line_returns,\n48\t        \"unnecessary_space_count\": unnecessary_spaces,\n49\t        \"total_chars\": len(text),\n50\t    }\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef parse_request_body(request_path: str):\n54\t    \"\"\"Parse the JSON body from a request.json file. Returns the parsed dict or None.\"\"\"\n55\t    try:\n56\t        with open(request_path, \"r\") as f:\n57\t            return json.load(f)\n58\t    except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n59\t        return None\n60\t\n61\t\n62\tdef get_canonical_model(model_id: str):\n63\t    \"\"\"Return the canonical model name (without date suffix) or None if unknown.\"\"\"\n64\t    for prefix in _SORTED_PREFIXES:\n65\t        if model_id.startswith(prefix):\n66\t            return prefix\n67\t    return None\n68\t\n69\t\n70\tdef get_pricing(model_id: str):\n71\t    \"\"\"Match a model ID (possibly with date suffix) to pricing. Returns pricing dict or None.\"\"\"\n72\t    canonical = get_canonical_model(model_id)\n73\t    if canonical:\n74\t        return MODEL_PRICING[canonical]\n75\t    return None\n76\t\n77\t\n78\tdef sanitize_path(path: str) -> str:\n79\t    \"\"\"Turn a URL path into a safe directory name component.\"\"\"\n80\t    path = path.split(\"?\")[0]\n81\t    path = path.replace(\"/\", \"_\")\n82\t    path = path.strip(\"_\")\n83\t    path = re.sub(r\"[^a-zA-Z0-9_\\-]\", \"\", path)\n84\t    return path[:80]\n85\t\n86\t\n87\t_REDACTED_HEADERS = {b\"x-api-key\", b\"authorization\"}\n88\t\n89\t\n90\tdef format_headers(headers) -> str:\n91\t    lines = []\n92\t    for k, v in headers.fields:\n93\t        if k.lower() in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n94\t            lines.append(f\"{k}: [REDACTED]\")\n95\t        else:\n96\t            lines.append(f\"{k}: {v}\")\n97\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n98\t\n99\t\n100\tdef write_request(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):\n101\t    req = flow.request\n102\t    # Write headers file (method+URL line, blank line, headers)\n103\t    header_lines = [\n104\t        f\"{req.method} {req.pretty_url}\",\n105\t        \"\",\n106\t        format_headers(req.headers),\n107\t    ]\n108\t    with open(os.path.join(directory, \"request_headers.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n109\t        f.write(\"\\n\".join(header_lines))\n110\t    # Write body as JSON (pretty-printed if valid JSON, raw fallback)\n111\t    body = req.get_text(strict=False)\n112\t    if body:\n113\t        try:\n114\t            parsed = json.loads(body)\n115\t            body_out = json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n116\t        except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n117\t            body_out = body\n118\t        with open(os.path.join(directory, \"request.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n119\t            f.write(body_out)\n120\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n121\t\n122\t\n123\t\n124\tdef write_response(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):\n125\t    resp = flow.response\n126\t    if resp is None:\n127\t        return\n128\t    lines = [\n129\t        f\"{resp.status_code} {resp.reason}\",\n130\t        \"\",\n131\t        format_headers(resp.headers),\n132\t    ]\n133\t    body = resp.get_text(strict=False)\n134\t    if body:\n135\t        lines += [\"\", body]\n136\t    with open(os.path.join(directory, \"response_raw.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n137\t        f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n138\t\n139\t\n140\tdef extract_stop_reason(response_raw: str) -> str:\n141\t    \"\"\"Extract stop_reason from SSE message_delta event or non-streaming JSON response.\"\"\"\n142\t    # Try SSE streaming format\n143\t    for line in response_raw.splitlines():\n144\t        line = line.strip()\n145\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n146\t            continue\n147\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n148\t        if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n149\t            continue\n150\t        try:\n151\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n152\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n153\t            reason = delta.get(\"stop_reason\")\n154\t            if reason:\n155\t                return reason\n156\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n157\t            continue\n158\t\n159\t    # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response\n160\t    for line in reversed(response_raw.splitlines()):\n161\t        line = line.strip()\n162\t        if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n163\t            continue\n164\t        try:\n165\t            data = json.loads(line)\n166\t            if data.get(\"type\") == \"message\":\n167\t                reason = data.get(\"stop_reason\")\n168\t                if reason:\n169\t                    return reason\n170\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n171\t            continue\n172\t\n173\t    return \"unknown\"\n174\t\n175\t\n176\tdef redact_flow_files(directory: str):\n177\t    \"\"\"Redact sensitive headers (API keys) from .flow files in-place.\"\"\"\n178\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, \"*.flow\")))\n179\t    if not flow_files:\n180\t        return\n181\t\n182\t    count = 0\n183\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n184\t        flows = []\n185\t        modified = False\n186\t        try:\n187\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n188\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n189\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n190\t                    if isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n191\t                        for header in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n192\t                            if flow.request.headers.get(header):\n193\t                                flow.request.headers[header] = \"[REDACTED]\"\n194\t                                modified = True\n195\t                    flows.append(flow)\n196\t        except (FlowReadException, Exception) as e:\n197\t            print(f\"  Skipping {os.path.basename(filepath)}: {e}\")\n198\t            continue\n199\t\n200\t        if modified:\n201\t            with open(filepath, \"wb\") as f:\n202\t                writer = FlowWriter(f)\n203\t                for flow in flows:\n204\t                    writer.add(flow)\n205\t            count += 1\n206\t\n207\t    print(f\"\\nRedacted API keys in {count} flow files\")\n208\t\n209\t\n210\tdef _system_prompt_hash(body_json, agent_name):\n211\t    \"\"\"Return a short hash of the relevant system prompt, or None.\"\"\"\n212\t    system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n213\t    if not system:\n214\t        return None\n215\t    index = SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX.get(agent_name, 0)\n216\t    if index >= len(system):\n217\t        return None\n218\t    text = system[index].get(\"text\", \"\")\n219\t    if not text:\n220\t        return None\n221\t    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]\n222\t\n223\t\n224\tdef export_flows(input_dir: str, output_dir: str):\n225\t    \"\"\"Export .flow files from input_dir into per-flow directories under output_dir.\n226\t\n227\t    Directory structure: {agent}/{step_index}/{request_index}/\n228\t    Steps are delimited by end_turn stop_reason in responses.\n229\t    \"\"\"\n230\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(input_dir, \"*.flow\")))\n231\t    if not flow_files:\n232\t        print(f\"No *.flow files found in {input_dir}\")\n233\t        return\n234\t\n235\t    total = 0\n236\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n237\t        filename = os.path.basename(filepath)\n238\t        name = os.path.splitext(filename)[0]\n239\t        file_dir = os.path.join(output_dir, name)\n240\t        if os.path.exists(file_dir):\n241\t            shutil.rmtree(file_dir)\n242\t        os.makedirs(file_dir)\n243\t        print(f\"Reading {filename}...\")\n244\t        try:\n245\t            step_index = 1\n246\t            request_index = 1\n247\t            prev_prompt_hash = None\n248\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n249\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n250\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n251\t                    if not isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n252\t                        continue\n253\t\n254\t                    url = flow.request.pretty_url\n255\t                    if \"/count_token\" in url:\n256\t                        continue\n257\t\n258\t                    # Parse body to check for quota requests\n259\t                    body_text = flow.request.get_text(strict=False)\n260\t                    body_json = None\n261\t                    if body_text:\n262\t                        try:\n263\t                            body_json = json.loads(body_text)\n264\t                            messages = body_json.get(\"messages\", [])\n265\t                            system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n266\t                            if messages and not system:\n267\t                                first_msg = messages[0]\n268\t                                content = first_msg.get(\"content\", \"\")\n269\t                                if isinstance(content, str) and content == \"quota\":\n270\t                                    continue\n271\t                        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n272\t                            pass\n273\t\n274\t                    # For cc: step boundary = system prompt change (checked before writing)\n275\t                    if name == \"cc\" and body_json is not None:\n276\t                        prompt_hash = _system_prompt_hash(body_json, name)\n277\t                        if prompt_hash is not None and prev_prompt_hash is not None and prompt_hash != prev_prompt_hash:\n278\t                            step_index += 1\n279\t                            request_index = 1\n280\t                        if prompt_hash is not None:\n281\t                            prev_prompt_hash = prompt_hash\n282\t\n283\t                    flow_dir = os.path.join(file_dir, str(step_index), str(request_index))\n284\t                    os.makedirs(flow_dir, exist_ok=True)\n285\t\n286\t                    write_request(flow, flow_dir)\n287\t                    write_response(flow, flow_dir)\n288\t                    # Write timing data inline\n289\t                    timing = {}\n290\t                    if flow.request:\n291\t                        timing[\"request_start\"] = flow.request.timestamp_start\n292\t                    if flow.response:\n293\t                        timing[\"response_end\"] = flow.response.timestamp_end\n294\t                    with open(os.path.join(flow_dir, \"timing.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n295\t                        json.dump(timing, f, indent=2)\n296\t                        f.write(\"\\n\")\n297\t\n298\t                    # Extract stop_reason to determine step boundaries\n299\t                    response_raw = \"\"\n300\t                    resp = flow.response\n301\t                    if resp is not None:\n302\t                        response_raw = resp.get_text(strict=False) or \"\"\n303\t                    stop_reason = extract_stop_reason(response_raw)\n304\t\n305\t                    print(f\"  [step {step_index}, req {request_index}] {flow.request.method} {flow.request.pretty_url} ({stop_reason})\")\n306\t\n307\t                    # For vix: step boundary = end_turn stop_reason (checked after writing)\n308\t                    if name != \"cc\":\n309\t                        if stop_reason == \"end_turn\":\n310\t                            step_index += 1\n311\t                            request_index = 1\n312\t                        else:\n313\t                            request_index += 1\n314\t                    else:\n315\t                        request_index += 1\n316\t\n317\t                    total += 1\n318\t        except FlowReadException as e:\n319\t            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n320\t        except Exception as e:\n321\t            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n322\t\n323\t    print(f\"\\nExported {total} flows to {output_dir}\")\n324\t\n325\t\n326\tdef extract_usage(directory: str):\n327\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, extract token usage from SSE message_delta events into usage.json.\"\"\"\n328\t    count = 0\n329\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n330\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n331\t            continue\n332\t\n333\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n334\t        usage = None\n335\t        with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n336\t            content = f.read()\n337\t\n338\t        # Try SSE streaming format: look for message_delta events\n339\t        for line in content.splitlines():\n340\t            line = line.strip()\n341\t            if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n342\t                continue\n343\t            payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n344\t            if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n345\t                continue\n346\t            try:\n347\t                data = json.loads(payload)\n348\t                usage = data.get(\"usage\")\n349\t            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n350\t                continue\n351\t\n352\t        # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response (single message object)\n353\t        # The body comes after a blank line following the headers\n354\t        if usage is None:\n355\t            # Find the last {...\"type\":\"message\"...} JSON in the content\n356\t            for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n357\t                line = line.strip()\n358\t                if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n359\t                    continue\n360\t                try:\n361\t                    msg = json.loads(line)\n362\t                    if msg.get(\"type\") == \"message\" and \"usage\" in msg:\n363\t                        usage = msg[\"usage\"]\n364\t                        break\n365\t                except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n366\t                    continue\n367\t\n368\t        if usage is None:\n369\t            print(f\"  Warning: no usage found in {response_path}\")\n370\t            continue\n371\t\n372\t        # Keep only the token count fields we need\n373\t        TOKEN_FIELDS = (\"input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\")\n374\t        usage = {k: v for k, v in usage.items() if k in TOKEN_FIELDS}\n375\t\n376\t        # Merge timing data if available\n377\t        timing_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"timing.json\")\n378\t        if os.path.exists(timing_path):\n379\t            with open(timing_path, \"r\") as f:\n380\t                timing = json.load(f)\n381\t            request_start = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n382\t            response_end = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n383\t            timing_block = {}\n384\t            if request_start:\n385\t                timing_block[\"request_start\"] = request_start\n386\t            if response_end:\n387\t                timing_block[\"response_end\"] = response_end\n388\t            if request_start and response_end:\n389\t                timing_block[\"duration_ms\"] = round((response_end - request_start) * 1000)\n390\t            if timing_block:\n391\t                usage[\"timing\"] = timing_block\n392\t            os.remove(timing_path)\n393\t\n394\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n395\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n396\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n397\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n398\t        count += 1\n399\t\n400\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted usage for {count} flows\")\n401\t\n402\t\n403\t\n404\tdef extract_prompts(directory: str):\n405\t    \"\"\"Extract system prompt and first user message from request.json files into per-request markdown files.\"\"\"\n406\t    count = 0\n407\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n408\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames:\n409\t            continue\n410\t\n411\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n412\t\n413\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n414\t        if body is None:\n415\t            print(f\"  Warning: no JSON body found in {request_path}\")\n416\t            continue\n417\t\n418\t        # System prompt: concatenate all text blocks from body[\"system\"]\n419\t        system = body.get(\"system\")\n420\t        if system and isinstance(system, list):\n421\t            texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in system if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n422\t            system_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n423\t            if system_text:\n424\t                with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"system_prompt.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n425\t                    f.write(system_text)\n426\t\n427\t        # First user message: find first message with role==\"user\", concatenate text blocks\n428\t        messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n429\t        for msg in messages:\n430\t            if msg.get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n431\t                content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n432\t                if isinstance(content, list):\n433\t                    texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in content if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n434\t                    user_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n435\t                    if user_text:\n436\t                        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"first_user_message.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n437\t                            f.write(user_text)\n438\t                break\n439\t\n440\t        count += 1\n441\t\n442\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted prompts for {count} requests\")\n443\t\n444\t\n445\t\n446\tdef _resolve_read_file_name(name, tool_input):\n447\t    \"\"\"Resolve read_file tool name to compressed/uncompressed variant.\"\"\"\n448\t    if name == \"read_file\":\n449\t        mode = tool_input.get(\"mode\", \"original\") if isinstance(tool_input, dict) else \"original\"\n450\t        return \"read_file_compressed\" if mode == \"compress\" else \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n451\t    return name\n452\t\n453\t\n454\tdef extract_read_file_whitespace(body):\n455\t    \"\"\"Extract whitespace stats from read_file/Read tool results in the request body.\"\"\"\n456\t    ws = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n457\t\n458\t    # Build tool_use_id -> tool_name map from assistant messages\n459\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n460\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n461\t    for msg in messages:\n462\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n463\t            continue\n464\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n465\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n466\t            continue\n467\t        for block in content:\n468\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n469\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n470\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n471\t\n472\t    for msg in messages:\n473\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n474\t            continue\n475\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n476\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n477\t            continue\n478\t        for block in content:\n479\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n480\t                continue\n481\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n482\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n483\t            if not (tool_name.startswith(\"read_file\") or tool_name == \"Read\"):\n484\t                continue\n485\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n486\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n487\t                text_for_ws = result_content\n488\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n489\t                text_for_ws = \"\".join(b.get(\"text\", \"\") for b in result_content)\n490\t            else:\n491\t                text_for_ws = \"\"\n492\t            stats = count_whitespace_stats(text_for_ws)\n493\t            for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n494\t                ws[k] += stats[k]\n495\t\n496\t    return ws\n497\t\n498\t\n499\tdef categorize_input_sources(body):\n500\t    \"\"\"Count input characters from tool results and tool use blocks, split by cache position.\n501\t\n502\t    Returns: {\n503\t        \"total_chars\": int,  # total chars of entire request body\n504\t        \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 1234}, ...},\n505\t        \"tool_calls\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 567}, ...},\n506\t    }\n507\t\n508\t    Position logic:\n509\t    - Last user message content ‚Üí cache_write (new content being written to cache)\n510\t    - Second-to-last message (assistant before last user) ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use blocks\n511\t    - Everything else ‚Üí cache_read\n512\t    \"\"\"\n513\t    total_chars = len(json.dumps(body))\n514\t    tool_results = {}\n515\t    tool_calls = {}\n516\t\n517\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n518\t\n519\t    # Find last user message index and second-to-last message index\n520\t    last_user_idx = -1\n521\t    for i in range(len(messages) - 1, -1, -1):\n522\t        if messages[i].get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n523\t            last_user_idx = i\n524\t            break\n525\t    second_to_last_idx = last_user_idx - 1 if last_user_idx > 0 else -1\n526\t\n527\t    # Build tool_use_id -> tool_name map from assistant messages\n528\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n529\t    for msg in messages:\n530\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n531\t            continue\n532\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n533\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n534\t            continue\n535\t        for block in content:\n536\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n537\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n538\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n539\t\n540\t    # Collect tool_result chars from user messages\n541\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n542\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n543\t            continue\n544\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n545\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n546\t            continue\n547\t        is_cache_write = (i == last_user_idx)\n548\t        for block in content:\n549\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n550\t                continue\n551\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n552\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n553\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n554\t            if tool_name not in tool_results:\n555\t                tool_results[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n556\t            if is_cache_write:\n557\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n558\t            else:\n559\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n560\t\n561\t    # Collect tool_use chars from assistant messages\n562\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n563\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n564\t            continue\n565\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n566\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n567\t            continue\n568\t        is_cache_write = (i == second_to_last_idx)\n569\t        for block in content:\n570\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n571\t                continue\n572\t            tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n573\t                block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n574\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n575\t            if tool_name not in tool_calls:\n576\t                tool_calls[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n577\t            if is_cache_write:\n578\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n579\t            else:\n580\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n581\t\n582\t    return {\"total_chars\": total_chars, \"tool_results\": tool_results, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n583\t\n584\t\n585\tdef categorize_output_sources(response_path):\n586\t    \"\"\"Count output characters from the actual response (SSE stream or single JSON).\n587\t\n588\t    Parses content_block_start/delta/stop events from response_raw.txt.\n589\t    Returns: {\"llm_text\": int, \"tool_calls\": {\"ToolName\": int, ...}}\n590\t    \"\"\"\n591\t    llm_text_chars = 0\n592\t    tool_calls = {}\n593\t\n594\t    with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n595\t        content = f.read()\n596\t\n597\t    # State machine for SSE content blocks\n598\t    # blocks[index] = {\"type\": \"text\"|\"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"text\": str, \"json\": str}\n599\t    blocks = {}\n600\t    found_sse = False\n601\t\n602\t    for line in content.splitlines():\n603\t        line = line.strip()\n604\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n605\t            continue\n606\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n607\t        try:\n608\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n609\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n610\t            continue\n611\t\n612\t        event_type = data.get(\"type\", \"\")\n613\t\n614\t        if event_type == \"content_block_start\":\n615\t            found_sse = True\n616\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n617\t            cb = data.get(\"content_block\", {})\n618\t            blocks[idx] = {\n619\t                \"type\": cb.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n620\t                \"name\": cb.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n621\t                \"text\": \"\",\n622\t                \"json\": \"\",\n623\t            }\n624\t\n625\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_delta\":\n626\t            found_sse = True\n627\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n628\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n629\t            delta_type = delta.get(\"type\", \"\")\n630\t            if idx in blocks:\n631\t                if delta_type == \"text_delta\":\n632\t                    blocks[idx][\"text\"] += delta.get(\"text\", \"\")\n633\t                elif delta_type == \"input_json_delta\":\n634\t                    blocks[idx][\"json\"] += delta.get(\"partial_json\", \"\")\n635\t\n636\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_stop\":\n637\t            found_sse = True\n638\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n639\t            if idx in blocks:\n640\t                block = blocks[idx]\n641\t                if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n642\t                    llm_text_chars += len(block[\"text\"])\n643\t                elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n644\t                    try:\n645\t                        input_data = json.loads(block[\"json\"]) if block[\"json\"] else {}\n646\t                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n647\t                        input_data = {}\n648\t                    tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(block[\"name\"], input_data)\n649\t                    # Reconstruct full block to count all chars (id, name, type, input)\n650\t                    full_block = {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block[\"name\"], \"input\": input_data}\n651\t                    chars = len(json.dumps(full_block))\n652\t                    tool_calls[tool_name] = tool_calls.get(tool_name, 0) + chars\n653\t                del blocks[idx]\n654\t\n655\t    # Non-streaming fallback: parse single JSON message\n656\t    if not found_sse:\n657\t        for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n658\t            line = line.strip()\n659\t            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n660\t                continue\n661\t            try:\n662\t                msg = json.loads(line)\n663\t                if msg.get(\"type\") != \"message\":\n664\t                    continue\n665\t                for block in msg.get(\"content\", []):\n666\t                    btype = block.get(\"type\", \"\")\n667\t                    if btype == \"text\":\n668\t                        llm_text_chars += len(block.get(\"text\", \"\"))\n669\t                    elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n670\t                        tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n671\t                            block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n672\t                        chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n673\t                        tool_calls[tool_name] = tool_calls.get(tool_name, 0) + chars\n674\t                break\n675\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n676\t                continue\n677\t\n678\t    return {\"llm_text\": llm_text_chars, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n679\t\n680\t\n681\tdef _format_tool_params(input_data):\n682\t    \"\"\"Format tool input as compact param=value pairs.\"\"\"\n683\t    parts = []\n684\t    for key, value in input_data.items():\n685\t        if isinstance(value, str):\n686\t            parts.append(f'{key}=\"{value}\"')\n687\t        else:\n688\t            parts.append(f\"{key}={json.dumps(value)}\")\n689\t    return \", \".join(parts)\n690\t\n691\t\n692\tdef parse_response_content(response_path):\n693\t    \"\"\"Parse response_raw.txt into a list of content blocks.\n694\t\n695\t    Returns: list of {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": str} or {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"input\": dict}\n696\t    \"\"\"\n697\t    with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n698\t        content = f.read()\n699\t\n700\t    # SSE streaming parse\n701\t    blocks = {}\n702\t    finished = []\n703\t    found_sse = False\n704\t\n705\t    for line in content.splitlines():\n706\t        line = line.strip()\n707\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n708\t            continue\n709\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n710\t        try:\n711\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n712\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n713\t            continue\n714\t\n715\t        event_type = data.get(\"type\", \"\")\n716\t\n717\t        if event_type == \"content_block_start\":\n718\t            found_sse = True\n719\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n720\t            cb = data.get(\"content_block\", {})\n721\t            blocks[idx] = {\n722\t                \"type\": cb.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n723\t                \"name\": cb.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n724\t                \"text\": \"\",\n725\t                \"json\": \"\",\n726\t            }\n727\t\n728\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_delta\":\n729\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n730\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n731\t            delta_type = delta.get(\"type\", \"\")\n732\t            if idx in blocks:\n733\t                if delta_type == \"text_delta\":\n734\t                    blocks[idx][\"text\"] += delta.get(\"text\", \"\")\n735\t                elif delta_type == \"input_json_delta\":\n736\t                    blocks[idx][\"json\"] += delta.get(\"partial_json\", \"\")\n737\t\n738\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_stop\":\n739\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n740\t            if idx in blocks:\n741\t                block = blocks[idx]\n742\t                if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n743\t                    finished.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": block[\"text\"]})\n744\t                elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n745\t                    try:\n746\t                        input_data = json.loads(block[\"json\"]) if block[\"json\"] else {}\n747\t                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n748\t                        input_data = {}\n749\t                    finished.append({\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block[\"name\"], \"input\": input_data})\n750\t                del blocks[idx]\n751\t\n752\t    # Non-streaming fallback\n753\t    if not found_sse:\n754\t        for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n755\t            line = line.strip()\n756\t            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n757\t                continue\n758\t            try:\n759\t                msg = json.loads(line)\n760\t                if msg.get(\"type\") != \"message\":\n761\t                    continue\n762\t                for block in msg.get(\"content\", []):\n763\t                    btype = block.get(\"type\", \"\")\n764\t                    if btype == \"text\":\n765\t                        finished.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": block.get(\"text\", \"\")})\n766\t                    elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n767\t                        finished.append({\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), \"input\": block.get(\"input\", {})})\n768\t                break\n769\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n770\t                continue\n771\t\n772\t    return finished\n773\t\n774\t\n775\tdef export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path):\n776\t    \"\"\"Parse response_raw.txt and write a human-readable response_parsed.txt.\n777\t\n778\t    Text blocks are output as-is. Tool calls are displayed inline with params.\n779\t    \"\"\"\n780\t    blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n781\t    if not blocks:\n782\t        return False\n783\t\n784\t    lines = []\n785\t    for block in blocks:\n786\t        if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n787\t            lines.append(block[\"text\"])\n788\t        elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n789\t            params = _format_tool_params(block[\"input\"])\n790\t            lines.append(f'\\n[{block[\"name\"]}({params})]\\n')\n791\t\n792\t    with open(output_path, \"w\") as f:\n793\t        f.write(\"\".join(lines))\n794\t    return True\n795\t\n796\t\n797\tdef export_parsed_responses(directory: str):\n798\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, export response_parsed.txt for each response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n799\t    count = 0\n800\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n801\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n802\t            continue\n803\t\n804\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n805\t        output_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_parsed.txt\")\n806\t\n807\t        if export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path):\n808\t            count += 1\n809\t\n810\t    print(f\"\\nExported parsed responses for {count} flows\")\n811\t\n812\t\n813\tdef attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing):\n814\t    \"\"\"Attribute tokens/cost to source categories.\n815\t\n816\t    Input side: raw character counts per tool (no token/cost distribution ‚Äî flawed due to caching).\n817\t    Output side: proportional token/cost distribution (valid since output isn't cached).\n818\t    \"\"\"\n819\t    by_source = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n820\t\n821\t    # Input: distribute input tokens proportionally using total_chars as denominator\n822\t    cost_data = usage.get(\"cost\", {})\n823\t    _ci = cost_data.get(\"input\", {})\n824\t    _cw = cost_data.get(\"cache_write\", {})\n825\t    _cr = cost_data.get(\"cache_read\", {})\n826\t    input_tokens = _ci.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cw.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cr.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n827\t\n828\t    total_chars = input_sources.get(\"total_chars\", 0)\n829\t\n830\t    def _attribute_input_tool(tool_char_dict):\n831\t        \"\"\"Compute tokens/dollars/chars for a tool given its {cache_write_chars, cache_read_chars}.\"\"\"\n832\t        cw_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0)\n833\t        cr_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0)\n834\t        cw_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cw_chars / total_chars))\n835\t        cr_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cr_chars / total_chars))\n836\t        dollars = (\n837\t            round(cw_tokens * pricing[\"cache_write\"], 6) +\n838\t            round(cr_tokens * pricing[\"cache_read\"], 6)\n839\t        )\n840\t        return {\"tokens\": cw_tokens + cr_tokens, \"dollars\": dollars, \"chars\": cw_chars + cr_chars}\n841\t\n842\t    if total_chars > 0 and input_tokens > 0 and pricing:\n843\t        # Tool results (from user messages)\n844\t        tool_results = input_sources.get(\"tool_results\", {})\n845\t        if tool_results:\n846\t            tr_entry = {}\n847\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_results.items():\n848\t                tr_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n849\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"] = tr_entry\n850\t\n851\t        # Tool calls (from assistant messages)\n852\t        tool_calls_input = input_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n853\t        if tool_calls_input:\n854\t            tc_entry = {}\n855\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_calls_input.items():\n856\t                tc_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n857\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n858\t\n859\t    # Output: distribute output tokens proportionally by character count\n860\t    output_cost_entry = cost_data.get(\"output\", {})\n861\t    output_tokens = output_cost_entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n862\t    output_dollars = output_cost_entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n863\t\n864\t    llm_chars = output_sources.get(\"llm_text\", 0)\n865\t    tc = output_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n866\t    tc_total_chars = sum(tc.values())\n867\t    total_output_chars = llm_chars + tc_total_chars\n868\t\n869\t    if total_output_chars > 0 and output_tokens > 0:\n870\t        # LLM text\n871\t        llm_frac = llm_chars / total_output_chars\n872\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"] = {\n873\t            \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * llm_frac),\n874\t            \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * llm_frac, 6),\n875\t            \"chars\": llm_chars,\n876\t        }\n877\t\n878\t        # Tool calls\n879\t        tc_frac = tc_total_chars / total_output_chars\n880\t        tc_entry = {\n881\t            \"__total\": {\n882\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tc_frac),\n883\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tc_frac, 6),\n884\t                \"chars\": tc_total_chars,\n885\t            }\n886\t        }\n887\t        for tool_name, chars in tc.items():\n888\t            tool_frac = chars / total_output_chars\n889\t            tc_entry[tool_name] = {\n890\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tool_frac),\n891\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tool_frac, 6),\n892\t                \"chars\": chars,\n893\t            }\n894\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n895\t\n896\t    return by_source\n897\t\n898\t\n899\tREAD_TOOLS = {\"read_file\", \"Read\", \"read_file_compressed\", \"read_file_uncompressed\"}\n900\tWRITE_TOOLS = {\"write_file\", \"Write\", \"edit_file\", \"Edit\"}\n901\t\n902\t\n903\t_PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n904\t\n905\t\n906\tdef _get_file_path(input_data):\n907\t    \"\"\"Extract file path from tool input, checking common key names. Always returns an absolute path.\"\"\"\n908\t    if not isinstance(input_data, dict):\n909\t        return None\n910\t    fp = input_data.get(\"file_path\") or input_data.get(\"path\") or None\n911\t    if fp and not os.path.isabs(fp):\n912\t        fp = os.path.join(_PROJECT_ROOT, fp)\n913\t    return fp\n914\t\n915\t\n916\tdef extract_file_ops(body, response_path):\n917\t    \"\"\"Extract file operation stats from request body (reads) and response (writes).\n918\t\n919\t    Returns: {\n920\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": int, \"total_read_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n921\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": int, \"total_write_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n922\t    }\n923\t    \"\"\"\n924\t    # --- Input: files read (from conversation history in request body) ---\n925\t    read_per_file = {}  # path -> {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n926\t\n927\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n928\t\n929\t    # Build tool_use_id -> (resolved_name, file_path) map from assistant messages\n930\t    tool_id_info = {}\n931\t    for msg in messages:\n932\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n933\t            continue\n934\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n935\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n936\t            continue\n937\t        for block in content:\n938\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n939\t                name = _resolve_read_file_name(block.get(\"name\", \"\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n940\t                if name in READ_TOOLS:\n941\t                    fp = _get_file_path(block.get(\"input\", {}))\n942\t                    tool_id_info[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = fp\n943\t\n944\t    # Sum chars from tool_result blocks matching read tools\n945\t    for msg in messages:\n946\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n947\t            continue\n948\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n949\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n950\t            continue\n951\t        for block in content:\n952\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n953\t                continue\n954\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n955\t            if tool_use_id not in tool_id_info:\n956\t                continue\n957\t            fp = tool_id_info[tool_use_id]\n958\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n959\t            chars = 0\n960\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n961\t                chars = len(result_content)\n962\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n963\t                chars = sum(len(b.get(\"text\", \"\")) for b in result_content)\n964\t            if fp:\n965\t                if fp not in read_per_file:\n966\t                    read_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n967\t                read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tool_use_id] = chars\n968\t                read_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n969\t                read_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n970\t\n971\t    # --- Output: files written (from response) ---\n972\t    write_per_file = {}  # path -> {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n973\t\n974\t    response_blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n975\t    for block in response_blocks:\n976\t        if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n977\t            continue\n978\t        name = block.get(\"name\", \"\")\n979\t        if name not in WRITE_TOOLS:\n980\t            continue\n981\t        inp = block.get(\"input\", {})\n982\t        fp = _get_file_path(inp)\n983\t        # Sum content chars: \"content\" for Write/write_file, \"new_string\" for Edit/edit_file\n984\t        chars = 0\n985\t        if name in (\"Write\", \"write_file\"):\n986\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"content\", \"\"))\n987\t        elif name in (\"Edit\", \"edit_file\"):\n988\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"new_string\", \"\"))\n989\t        if fp:\n990\t            block_id = block.get(\"id\", \"\")\n991\t            if fp not in write_per_file:\n992\t                write_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n993\t            write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][block_id] = chars\n994\t            write_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n995\t            write_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n996\t\n997\t    # Add file_size for each file\n998\t    for pf in (read_per_file, write_per_file):\n999\t        for fp in pf:\n1000\t            try:\n1001\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = os.path.getsize(fp)\n1002\t            except OSError:\n1003\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = None\n1004\t\n1005\t    # Derive aggregate scalars from deduplicated per_file data\n1006\t    unique_files_read = len(read_per_file)\n1007\t    total_read_chars = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in read_per_file.values())\n1008\t    unique_files_written = len(write_per_file)\n1009\t    total_write_chars_dedup = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n1010\t    total_write_calls = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n1011\t\n1012\t    return {\n1013\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": unique_files_read, \"total_read_chars\": total_read_chars, \"per_file\": read_per_file},\n1014\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": total_write_calls, \"unique_files_written\": unique_files_written, \"total_write_chars\": total_write_chars_dedup, \"per_file\": write_per_file},\n1015\t    }\n1016\t\n1017\t\n1018\tdef extract_source_attribution(directory: str):\n1019\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute source attribution, read_file whitespace, and file ops.\"\"\"\n1020\t    count = 0\n1021\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n1022\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames or \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n1023\t            continue\n1024\t\n1025\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n1026\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n1027\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n1028\t\n1029\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n1030\t        if body is None:\n1031\t            continue\n1032\t\n1033\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1034\t            usage = json.load(f)\n1035\t\n1036\t        # Get model pricing\n1037\t        model = body.get(\"model\", \"\")\n1038\t        pricing = get_pricing(model) if model else None\n1039\t\n1040\t        # Compute source attribution\n1041\t        input_sources = categorize_input_sources(body)\n1042\t        output_sources = categorize_output_sources(response_path)\n1043\t        by_source = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)\n1044\t\n1045\t        usage[\"by_source\"] = by_source\n1046\t\n1047\t        # Compute read_file whitespace\n1048\t        usage[\"read_file_whitespace\"] = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n1049\t\n1050\t        # Compute file operations\n1051\t        usage[\"file_ops\"] = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n1052\t\n1053\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n1054\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n1055\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n1056\t        count += 1\n1057\t\n1058\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted source attribution for {count} flows\")\n1059\t\n1060\t\n1061\tdef calculate_costs(directory: str):\n1062\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute dollar costs from usage.json and request.json model info.\"\"\"\n1063\t    count = 0\n1064\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n1065\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames:\n1066\t            continue\n1067\t\n1068\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n1069\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n1070\t        if body is None:\n1071\t            continue\n1072\t\n1073\t        model = body.get(\"model\")\n1074\t        if not model:\n1075\t            continue\n1076\t\n1077\t        pricing = get_pricing(model)\n1078\t        if pricing is None:\n1079\t            print(f\"  Warning: unknown model '{model}' in {request_path}, skipping cost calculation\")\n1080\t            continue\n1081\t\n1082\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n1083\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1084\t            usage = json.load(f)\n1085\t\n1086\t        tokens_input = usage.get(\"input_tokens\", 0)\n1087\t        tokens_cache_write = usage.get(\"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0)\n1088\t        tokens_cache_read = usage.get(\"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0)\n1089\t        tokens_output = usage.get(\"output_tokens\", 0)\n1090\t        tokens_total = tokens_input + tokens_cache_write + tokens_cache_read + tokens_output\n1091\t\n1092\t        cost_input = tokens_input * pricing[\"input\"]\n1093\t        cost_cache_write = tokens_cache_write * pricing[\"cache_write\"]\n1094\t        cost_cache_read = tokens_cache_read * pricing[\"cache_read\"]\n1095\t        cost_output = tokens_output * pricing[\"output\"]\n1096\t        cost_total = cost_input + cost_cache_write + cost_cache_read + cost_output\n1097\t\n1098\t        usage[\"cost\"] = {\n1099\t            \"input\": {\"tokens\": tokens_input, \"dollars\": round(cost_input, 6)},\n1100\t            \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_write, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_write, 6)},\n1101\t            \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_read, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_read, 6)},\n1102\t            \"output\": {\"tokens\": tokens_output, \"dollars\": round(cost_output, 6)},\n1103\t            \"total\": {\"tokens\": tokens_total, \"dollars\": round(cost_total, 6)},\n1104\t        }\n1105\t\n1106\t        # Remove top-level token keys (now redundant with cost entries)\n1107\t        for key in (\"input_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\"):\n1108\t            usage.pop(key, None)\n1109\t\n1110\t        canonical = get_canonical_model(model)\n1111\t        if canonical:\n1112\t            usage[\"model\"] = canonical\n1113\t\n1114\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n1115\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n1116\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n1117\t        count += 1\n1118\t\n1119\t    print(f\"\\nCalculated costs for {count} flows\")\n1120\t\n1121\t\n1122\tdef _aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source):\n1123\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-flow by_source into summary by_source.\n1124\t\n1125\t    Input side: sum tool_results {tokens, dollars} dicts.\n1126\t    Output side: sum token/dollars dicts.\n1127\t    \"\"\"\n1128\t    # Input: tool_results and tool_calls are {tokens, dollars} dicts\n1129\t    flow_input = flow_by_source.get(\"input\", {})\n1130\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n1131\t        flow_section = flow_input.get(input_key, {})\n1132\t        if not flow_section:\n1133\t            continue\n1134\t        if input_key not in agg[\"input\"]:\n1135\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key] = {}\n1136\t        for tool, entry in flow_section.items():\n1137\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n1138\t                continue\n1139\t            if tool not in agg[\"input\"][input_key]:\n1140\t                agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1141\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1142\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1143\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1144\t\n1145\t    # Output: token/dollars dicts\n1146\t    flow_output = flow_by_source.get(\"output\", {})\n1147\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n1148\t        entry = flow_output.get(key)\n1149\t        if entry:\n1150\t            if key not in agg[\"output\"]:\n1151\t                agg[\"output\"][key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1152\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1153\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1154\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1155\t\n1156\t    # Tool calls\n1157\t    flow_tc = flow_output.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n1158\t    if flow_tc:\n1159\t        if \"tool_calls\" not in agg[\"output\"]:\n1160\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = {}\n1161\t        for tool_key, entry in flow_tc.items():\n1162\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n1163\t                continue\n1164\t            if tool_key not in agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"]:\n1165\t                agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1166\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1167\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1168\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1169\t\n1170\t\n1171\tdef _round_by_source(agg):\n1172\t    \"\"\"Round dollar values in the by_source aggregate.\"\"\"\n1173\t    # Input: round dollars\n1174\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n1175\t        section = agg.get(\"input\", {}).get(input_key, {})\n1176\t        for entry in section.values():\n1177\t            if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n1178\t                entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1179\t    # Output: round dollars\n1180\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n1181\t        entry = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(key)\n1182\t        if entry:\n1183\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1184\t    tc = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n1185\t    for entry in tc.values():\n1186\t        if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n1187\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1188\t\n1189\t\n1190\tAGENT_COLORS = {\n1191\t    \"vix\": \"#7B2FBE\",\n1192\t    \"cc\": \"#D77656\",\n1193\t}\n1194\t\n1195\t\n1196\tdef _agent_color(name):\n1197\t    \"\"\"Return a deterministic hex color for an unknown agent name.\"\"\"\n1198\t    import hashlib\n1199\t    h = int(hashlib.md5(name.encode()).hexdigest()[:6], 16)\n1200\t    return f\"#{h:06x}\"\n1201\t\n1202\t\n1203\tdef summarize_usage(directory: str):\n1204\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-request usage.json files into a summary usage.json per agent type.\"\"\"\n1205\t    COST_FIELDS = [\"input\", \"cache_write\", \"cache_read\", \"output\", \"total\"]\n1206\t\n1207\t    def empty_bucket():\n1208\t        bucket = {\"request_count\": 0}\n1209\t        bucket[\"cost\"] = {f: {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0} for f in COST_FIELDS}\n1210\t        bucket[\"timing\"] = {\n1211\t            \"total_duration_ms\": 0,\n1212\t            \"min_request_start\": None, \"max_response_end\": None,\n1213\t        }\n1214\t        return bucket\n1215\t\n1216\t    def add_to_bucket(bucket, usage):\n1217\t        bucket[\"request_count\"] += 1\n1218\t        cost = usage.get(\"cost\")\n1219\t        if cost:\n1220\t            for f in COST_FIELDS:\n1221\t                entry = cost.get(f, {})\n1222\t                if isinstance(entry, dict):\n1223\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1224\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1225\t        timing = usage.get(\"timing\")\n1226\t        if timing:\n1227\t            bucket[\"timing\"][\"total_duration_ms\"] += timing.get(\"duration_ms\", 0)\n1228\t            rs = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n1229\t            re_ = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n1230\t            if rs is not None:\n1231\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"]\n1232\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"] = rs if cur is None else min(cur, rs)\n1233\t            if re_ is not None:\n1234\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"]\n1235\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"] = re_ if cur is None else max(cur, re_)\n1236\t\n1237\t    def round_costs(bucket):\n1238\t        for f in COST_FIELDS:\n1239\t            bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] = round(bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"], 6)\n1240\t\n1241\t    count = 0\n1242\t    for entry in sorted(os.listdir(directory)):\n1243\t        agent_dir = os.path.join(directory, entry)\n1244\t        if not os.path.isdir(agent_dir):\n1245\t            continue\n1246\t\n1247\t        # Only process dirs that contain numbered step subdirs\n1248\t        has_numbered = False\n1249\t        for sub in os.listdir(agent_dir):\n1250\t            if sub.isdigit() and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(agent_dir, sub)):\n1251\t                has_numbered = True\n1252\t                break\n1253\t        if not has_numbered:\n1254\t            continue\n1255\t\n1256\t        by_model = {}\n1257\t        by_step = {}\n1258\t        total = empty_bucket()\n1259\t        ws_agg = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n1260\t        by_source_agg = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n1261\t        file_ops_agg = {\n1262\t            \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1263\t            \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1264\t        }\n1265\t\n1266\t        # Iterate step dirs: {agent_dir}/{step_number}/\n1267\t        for step_sub in sorted(os.listdir(agent_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n1268\t            if not step_sub.isdigit():\n1269\t                continue\n1270\t            step_dir = os.path.join(agent_dir, step_sub)\n1271\t            if not os.path.isdir(step_dir):\n1272\t                continue\n1273\t\n1274\t            step_key = step_sub  # Use step directory number as key\n1275\t\n1276\t            # Iterate request dirs: {step_dir}/{request_number}/usage.json\n1277\t            for req_sub in sorted(os.listdir(step_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n1278\t                if not req_sub.isdigit():\n1279\t                    continue\n1280\t                usage_path = os.path.join(step_dir, req_sub, \"usage.json\")\n1281\t                if not os.path.isfile(usage_path):\n1282\t                    continue\n1283\t\n1284\t                with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1285\t                    usage = json.load(f)\n1286\t\n1287\t                model_name = usage.get(\"model\", \"unknown\")\n1288\t                if model_name not in by_model:\n1289\t                    by_model[model_name] = empty_bucket()\n1290\t                add_to_bucket(by_model[model_name], usage)\n1291\t\n1292\t                add_to_bucket(total, usage)\n1293\t\n1294\t                # Aggregate by_source\n1295\t                flow_by_source = usage.get(\"by_source\")\n1296\t                if flow_by_source:\n1297\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_source_agg, flow_by_source)\n1298\t\n1299\t                # Aggregate read_file whitespace\n1300\t                flow_ws = usage.get(\"read_file_whitespace\")\n1301\t                if flow_ws:\n1302\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n1303\t                        ws_agg[k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n1304\t\n1305\t                # Aggregate file_ops\n1306\t                flow_file_ops = usage.get(\"file_ops\")\n1307\t                if flow_file_ops:\n1308\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n1309\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n1310\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n1311\t                    # Aggregate per-file details (merge tool_ids maps for dedup)\n1312\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n1313\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n1314\t                            agg_pf = file_ops_agg[side][\"per_file\"]\n1315\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n1316\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n1317\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n1318\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n1319\t\n1320\t                # Aggregate per step\n1321\t                if step_key not in by_step:\n1322\t                    by_step[step_key] = empty_bucket()\n1323\t                    by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"] = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n1324\t                    by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"] = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n1325\t                    by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"] = {\n1326\t                        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1327\t                        \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1328\t                    }\n1329\t                add_to_bucket(by_step[step_key], usage)\n1330\t                if flow_by_source:\n1331\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"], flow_by_source)\n1332\t                if flow_ws:\n1333\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n1334\t                        by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"][k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n1335\t                if flow_file_ops:\n1336\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n1337\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n1338\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n1339\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n1340\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n1341\t                            agg_pf = by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"][side][\"per_file\"]\n1342\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n1343\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n1344\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n1345\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n1346\t\n1347\t        round_costs(total)\n1348\t        for bucket in by_model.values():\n1349\t            round_costs(bucket)\n1350\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n1351\t            round_costs(bucket)\n1352\t            if \"by_source\" in bucket:\n1353\t                _round_by_source(bucket[\"by_source\"])\n1354\t        _round_by_source(by_source_agg)\n1355\t\n1356\t        # Finalize file_ops: convert tool_ids maps to calls/chars, recompute scalars\n1357\t        def _finalize_file_ops(fops):\n1358\t            for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n1359\t                pf = fops[side][\"per_file\"]\n1360\t                for fp in pf:\n1361\t                    pf[fp][\"calls\"] = len(pf[fp].get(\"tool_ids\", {}))\n1362\t                    pf[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(pf[fp].get(\"tool_ids\", {}).values())\n1363\t                    pf[fp].pop(\"tool_ids\", None)\n1364\t            fops[\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] = len(fops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"])\n1365\t            fops[\"input\"][\"total_read_chars\"] = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in fops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n1366\t            fops[\"output\"][\"unique_files_written\"] = len(fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"])\n1367\t            fops[\"output\"][\"files_written\"] = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n1368\t            fops[\"output\"][\"total_write_chars\"] = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n1369\t\n1370\t        _finalize_file_ops(file_ops_agg)\n1371\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n1372\t            if \"file_ops\" in bucket:\n1373\t                _finalize_file_ops(bucket[\"file_ops\"])\n1374\t\n1375\t        # Finalize timing for each bucket\n1376\t        def _finalize_timing(bucket):\n1377\t            t = bucket[\"timing\"]\n1378\t            req_count = bucket[\"request_count\"]\n1379\t            mn = t.pop(\"min_request_start\", None)\n1380\t            mx = t.pop(\"max_response_end\", None)\n1381\t            if mn is not None and mx is not None:\n1382\t                t[\"wall_clock_ms\"] = round((mx - mn) * 1000)\n1383\t            else:\n1384\t                t[\"wall_clock_ms\"] = 0\n1385\t            t[\"avg_duration_ms\"] = round(t[\"total_duration_ms\"] / req_count) if req_count > 0 else 0\n1386\t\n1387\t        _finalize_timing(total)\n1388\t        for bucket in by_model.values():\n1389\t            _finalize_timing(bucket)\n1390\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n1391\t            _finalize_timing(bucket)\n1392\t\n1393\t        total[\"file_ops\"] = file_ops_agg\n1394\t        summary = {\"title\": entry, \"color\": AGENT_COLORS.get(entry, _agent_color(entry)), \"by_model\": by_model, \"by_step\": by_step, \"by_source\": by_source_agg, \"read_file_whitespace\": ws_agg, \"total\": total}\n1395\t        summary_path = os.path.join(agent_dir, \"usage.json\")\n1396\t        with open(summary_path, \"w\") as f:\n1397\t            json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n1398\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n1399\t        count += 1\n1400\t        print(f\"  Wrote summary: {summary_path} ({total['request_count']} requests)\")\n1401\t\n1402\t    print(f\"\\nSummarized usage for {count} agent types\")\n1403\t\n1404\t\n1405\tdef main():\n1406\t    script_dir = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n1407\t    data_dir = os.path.join(script_dir, \"data\")\n1408\t\n1409\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Export mitmproxy flow files to text.\")\n1410\t    parser.add_argument(\"--input-directory\", default=data_dir, help=\"Directory containing *.flow files (default: data/ next to script)\")\n1411\t    parser.add_argument(\"--output-directory\", default=data_dir, help=\"Output directory for exported flows (default: data/ next to script)\")\n1412\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n1413\t\n1414\t    input_dir = args.input_directory\n1415\t    output_dir = args.output_directory\n1416\t    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n1417\t\n1418\t    redact_flow_files(input_dir)\n1419\t    export_flows(input_dir, output_dir)\n1420\t    extract_usage(output_dir)\n1421\t    export_parsed_responses(output_dir)\n1422\t    extract_prompts(output_dir)\n1423\t    calculate_costs(output_dir)\n1424\t    extract_source_attribution(output_dir)\n1425\t    summarize_usage(output_dir)\n1426\t\n1427\t\n1428\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n1429\t    main()\n1430\t"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me design the test plan:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BS9T7fXwxfC7ttnnnpwFZX","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Design comprehensive test plan","subagent_type":"Plan","prompt":"I need to design a comprehensive pytest test suite for `/workspace/export_flows.py` that achieves at least 80% code coverage. The test file will be placed at `/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py`.\n\nHere's the complete module structure (1430 lines) I need to cover:\n\n## Key Functions to Test\n\n### Pure functions (no I/O):\n- `count_whitespace_stats(text)` - counts newlines, runs of 2+ spaces, total chars\n- `get_canonical_model(model_id)` - matches model ID with optional date suffix against MODEL_PRICING keys via longest-prefix matching\n- `get_pricing(model_id)` - returns pricing dict for a model\n- `sanitize_path(path)` - converts URL path to safe directory name (strips query, replaces /, removes non-alphanumeric, limit 80 chars)\n- `_system_prompt_hash(body_json, agent_name)` - SHA256 hash of system prompt text using SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX\n- `_resolve_read_file_name(name, tool_input)` - read_file ‚Üí compressed/uncompressed based on mode param\n- `_format_tool_params(input_data)` - formats dict as param=value pairs\n- `_get_file_path(input_data)` - extracts file_path/path from dict, makes absolute if relative\n- `_aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source)` - aggregates by_source dicts in-place\n- `_round_by_source(agg)` - rounds dollar values to 6 decimal places\n- `_agent_color(name)` - deterministic MD5-based hex color\n- `attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)` - proportional token/cost attribution\n- `extract_read_file_whitespace(body)` - counts whitespace from read_file tool results in request body\n- `categorize_input_sources(body)` - counts input chars by tool, split by cache position (last user msg = cache_write, second-to-last = cache_write for tool_use)\n\n### Functions requiring file I/O mocking:\n- `parse_request_body(request_path)` - reads JSON file, returns None on error\n- `format_headers(headers)` - needs headers object with .fields attribute (list of (k,v) byte pairs)\n- `write_request(flow, directory)` - writes request_headers.txt and request.json\n- `write_response(flow, directory)` - writes response_raw.txt\n- `extract_stop_reason(response_raw)` - parses SSE format or non-streaming JSON\n- `categorize_output_sources(response_path)` - SSE state machine for output char counting\n- `parse_response_content(response_path)` - parses SSE or non-streaming response into content blocks\n- `export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path)` - writes human-readable response_parsed.txt\n- `extract_file_ops(body, response_path)` - extracts read/write file stats\n\n### Functions requiring directory walking:\n- `redact_flow_files(directory)` - mitmproxy FlowReader/FlowWriter with redaction\n- `export_flows(input_dir, output_dir)` - main flow export, needs mitmproxy mocks\n- `extract_usage(directory)` - walks dirs, extracts token usage\n- `extract_prompts(directory)` - extracts system prompt and user messages  \n- `export_parsed_responses(directory)` - walks, calls export_parsed_response\n- `calculate_costs(directory)` - computes dollar costs from usage.json + request.json\n- `extract_source_attribution(directory)` - computes source attribution\n- `summarize_usage(directory)` - aggregates into per-agent summary\n\n## Key mitmproxy mocks needed:\n```python\n# HTTPFlow mock structure:\nflow.request.method = \"POST\"\nflow.request.pretty_url = \"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\"\nflow.request.headers.fields = [(b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"), (b\"x-api-key\", b\"secret\")]\nflow.request.headers.get(b\"x-api-key\") -> \"secret\" or None\nflow.request.get_text(strict=False) -> str\nflow.request.timestamp_start = 1700000000.0\nflow.response.status_code = 200\nflow.response.reason = \"OK\"\nflow.response.headers.fields = [...]\nflow.response.get_text(strict=False) -> str\nflow.response.timestamp_end = 1700000001.0\n\n# FlowReader mock (context manager-less, uses .stream() generator):\nfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader  # mock with: reader.stream() returns iter(flows)\n# Used as: with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f: reader = FlowReader(f); for flow in reader.stream()\n\n# FlowWriter mock:\nwriter = FlowWriter(f)\nwriter.add(flow)\n```\n\n## Critical test scenarios:\n\n1. **Longest-prefix model matching**: `claude-opus-4-5-20250101` should match `claude-opus-4-5`, NOT `claude-opus-4`\n2. **extract_stop_reason**: \n   - SSE with `\"type\":\"message_delta\"` and stop_reason\n   - SSE with `\"type\": \"message_delta\"` (space variant)\n   - Non-streaming JSON fallback with `\"type\":\"message\"` \n   - No stop_reason found ‚Üí returns \"unknown\"\n3. **categorize_input_sources cache position logic**:\n   - Last user message ‚Üí cache_write\n   - Second-to-last message (assistant) ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use\n   - All others ‚Üí cache_read\n4. **export_flows step boundary logic**:\n   - For \"cc\" agent: step increments when system prompt hash changes (before writing)\n   - For non-\"cc\" agents: step increments when stop_reason == \"end_turn\" (after writing)\n   - Skips /count_token URLs\n   - Skips requests where first message content is \"quota\" and no system prompt\n5. **_system_prompt_hash**: uses SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX[\"cc\"]=2, [\"vix\"]=0; returns None if index out of bounds\n6. **attribute_tokens**: proportional distribution, handles zero division cases\n7. **extract_file_ops**: deduplication via tool_ids map, both read and write tools\n\n## Import Strategy\nSince the test is in `evaluation/usage/` but the module is at `/workspace/export_flows.py`, add to sys.path:\n```python\nimport sys, os\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..', '..'))\nimport export_flows\n```\n\n## Test Organization\nOrganize tests into classes by function group:\n- `TestCountWhitespaceStats`\n- `TestGetCanonicalModel`  \n- `TestGetPricing`\n- `TestSanitizePath`\n- `TestFormatHeaders`\n- `TestExtractStopReason`\n- `TestSystemPromptHash`\n- `TestResolveReadFileName`\n- `TestFormatToolParams`\n- `TestGetFilePath`\n- `TestParseRequestBody`\n- `TestWriteRequest` / `TestWriteResponse`\n- `TestExtractReadFileWhitespace`\n- `TestCategorizeInputSources`\n- `TestCategorizeOutputSources`\n- `TestParseResponseContent`\n- `TestExportParsedResponse`\n- `TestAttributeTokens`\n- `TestAggregateBySource`\n- `TestRoundBySource`\n- `TestAgentColor`\n- `TestRedactFlowFiles`\n- `TestExportFlows`\n- `TestExtractUsage`\n- `TestExtractPrompts`\n- `TestCalculateCosts`\n- `TestExtractFileOps`\n- `TestSummarizeUsage`\n\nPlease design a detailed test plan including:\n1. The exact test file structure\n2. Which pytest features to use (fixtures, tmp_path, monkeypatch, parametrize)\n3. How to mock mitmproxy (since it may not be installed, consider conditional imports)\n4. The most critical test cases for each function\n5. How to achieve 80%+ coverage without testing trivial main() scaffolding\n6. Any conftest.py needed\n\nIMPORTANT: The mitmproxy package may or may not be installed. Design the mocks so that if mitmproxy IS installed, we test actual integration; if not, we mock at import level. Actually, let's assume mitmproxy IS installed (it's imported at module top level, so the module would fail to import without it). Design tests that mock it at the module level using `unittest.mock.patch`.\n"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BS9T7fXwxfC7ttnnnpwFZX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have a complete, verified understanding of the entire module. Let me compile the comprehensive test plan.\n\n---\n\n## Comprehensive pytest Test Plan for `export_flows.py`\n\n### Overview\n\nThe test file will be placed at `/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py`, with a `conftest.py` in the same directory. Because `mitmproxy` is not installed in this environment but is imported at the module's top level, the entire import must be bootstrapped by injecting fake modules into `sys.modules` before `export_flows` is imported. This is done once via a `conftest.py` session-scoped fixture, and the `export_flows` module is exposed to every test through a module-level reference.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Directory and File Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/evaluation/usage/\n    conftest.py\n    test_export_flows.py\n```\n\nNo `__init__.py` is needed since pytest will discover the test file directly. The `evaluation/usage/` directories must be created before the test file is placed.\n\n---\n\n### 2. `conftest.py`\n\nThe conftest handles three responsibilities:\n\n**a) Mitmproxy stub injection** - must happen before any `import export_flows` anywhere in the test session.\n\n**b) Shared pytest fixtures** for `tmp_path`-based flows (request headers mock objects, etc.).\n\n**c) The `ef` module fixture** that exposes the imported `export_flows` module.\n\n```python\n# /workspace/evaluation/usage/conftest.py\n\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport types\n\n# --- Inject mitmproxy stubs BEFORE any module import ---\n\nclass _FakeFlowReadException(Exception):\n    pass\n\nclass _FakeHTTPFlow:\n    pass\n\nclass _FakeFlowReader:\n    def __init__(self, f):\n        pass\n    def stream(self):\n        return iter([])\n\nclass _FakeFlowWriter:\n    def __init__(self, f):\n        pass\n    def add(self, flow):\n        pass\n\n_mitmproxy_io = types.ModuleType(\"mitmproxy.io\")\n_mitmproxy_io.FlowReader = _FakeFlowReader\n_mitmproxy_io.FlowWriter = _FakeFlowWriter\n\n_mitmproxy_exceptions = types.ModuleType(\"mitmproxy.exceptions\")\n_mitmproxy_exceptions.FlowReadException = _FakeFlowReadException\n\n_mitmproxy_http = types.ModuleType(\"mitmproxy.http\")\n_mitmproxy_http.HTTPFlow = _FakeHTTPFlow\n\nsys.modules[\"mitmproxy\"] = types.ModuleType(\"mitmproxy\")\nsys.modules[\"mitmproxy.io\"] = _mitmproxy_io\nsys.modules[\"mitmproxy.exceptions\"] = _mitmproxy_exceptions\nsys.modules[\"mitmproxy.http\"] = _mitmproxy_http\n\n# Expose these stubs for tests to reference\nFAKE_HTTPFlow = _FakeHTTPFlow\nFAKE_FlowReadException = _FakeFlowReadException\n\n# --- sys.path setup ---\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n\n# --- Fixtures ---\nimport pytest\nimport json\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef ef():\n    \"\"\"Return the export_flows module (imported once per session).\"\"\"\n    import export_flows\n    return export_flows\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef fake_http_flow_class():\n    return _FakeHTTPFlow\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef fake_flow_read_exception():\n    return _FakeFlowReadException\n\n# Shared helpers for building mock flows\nclass FakeHeaders:\n    def __init__(self, fields=None):\n        self.fields = fields or []\n        self._map = {k.lower(): v for k, v in (fields or [])}\n    def get(self, key, default=None):\n        return self._map.get(key.lower() if isinstance(key, bytes) else key.lower().encode(), default)\n\nclass FakeRequest:\n    def __init__(self, url, body_dict=None, body_text=None, method=\"POST\"):\n        self.method = method\n        self.pretty_url = url\n        self.timestamp_start = 1700000000.0\n        self.headers = FakeHeaders([\n            (b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"),\n        ])\n        if body_text is not None:\n            self._body = body_text\n        elif body_dict is not None:\n            self._body = json.dumps(body_dict)\n        else:\n            self._body = \"\"\n    def get_text(self, strict=False):\n        return self._body\n\nclass FakeResponse:\n    def __init__(self, text=\"\", status_code=200, reason=\"OK\"):\n        self.status_code = status_code\n        self.reason = reason\n        self.timestamp_end = 1700000001.0\n        self.headers = FakeHeaders([(b\"content-type\", b\"text/event-stream\")])\n        self._text = text\n    def get_text(self, strict=False):\n        return self._text\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef make_flow(fake_http_flow_class):\n    \"\"\"Factory for creating mock HTTPFlow instances.\"\"\"\n    FakeHTTPFlowBase = fake_http_flow_class\n    def _make(url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\",\n              body_dict=None, body_text=None, response_text=\"\",\n              response=True, method=\"POST\"):\n        class _Flow(FakeHTTPFlowBase):\n            pass\n        flow = _Flow.__new__(_Flow)\n        flow.request = FakeRequest(url, body_dict=body_dict, body_text=body_text, method=method)\n        if response:\n            flow.response = FakeResponse(response_text)\n        else:\n            flow.response = None\n        return flow\n    return _make\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Test File Structure\n\n```python\n# /workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py\n\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport json\nimport hashlib\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock, patch, mock_open\n\n# conftest.py already injected mitmproxy stubs and set sys.path\nimport export_flows as ef_module  # module-level reference for parametrize decorators\n```\n\nNote: All test classes use `ef` session fixture rather than direct `ef_module` import, but `ef_module` is imported at module level so `@pytest.mark.parametrize` decorators that reference `ef_module.MODEL_PRICING` work correctly.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Test Classes and Cases\n\n#### `TestCountWhitespaceStats`\n\nPurpose: Pure string analysis function. No mocking needed.\n\n```\ntest_empty_string() - all zeros\ntest_single_newline() - line_returns=1, spaces=0\ntest_no_whitespace() - all zeros\ntest_double_spaces() - unnecessary_space_count = len(run) - 1 per run\ntest_triple_spaces() - counts 2 excess\ntest_multiple_runs() - sum of multiple runs\ntest_total_chars_accurate() - total_chars equals len(text)\ntest_combined_newlines_and_spaces() - verifies dict structure and all keys\n```\n\nKey assertion pattern:\n```python\nr = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"hello\\nworld  test   end\")\nassert r == {\"line_returns_count\": 1, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 3, \"total_chars\": 23}\n```\n\n#### `TestGetCanonicalModel`\n\nPurpose: Longest-prefix matching - the critical scenario from the spec.\n\n```\ntest_exact_match(\"claude-opus-4-5\") -> \"claude-opus-4-5\"\ntest_date_suffix_longer_prefix(\"claude-opus-4-5-20250101\") -> \"claude-opus-4-5\" NOT \"claude-opus-4\"\ntest_date_suffix_shorter_prefix(\"claude-opus-4-20250101\") -> \"claude-opus-4\"\ntest_haiku_with_date(\"claude-haiku-3-5-20241022\") -> \"claude-haiku-3-5\"\ntest_unknown_model(\"gpt-4\") -> None\ntest_empty_string(\"\") -> None\ntest_all_known_models_match() - parametrize over MODEL_PRICING.keys()\n```\n\nUse `@pytest.mark.parametrize` with the model keys from `ef_module.MODEL_PRICING`.\n\n#### `TestGetPricing`\n\n```\ntest_known_model_returns_dict()\ntest_model_with_date_suffix_returns_pricing()\ntest_unknown_model_returns_none()\ntest_pricing_has_required_keys() - input, cache_write, cache_read, output\n```\n\n#### `TestSanitizePath`\n\n```\ntest_strips_query_string()\ntest_replaces_slashes_with_underscores()\ntest_strips_leading_trailing_underscores()\ntest_removes_special_chars()\ntest_preserves_alphanumeric_hyphen_underscore()\ntest_truncates_to_80_chars()\ntest_empty_string()\ntest_path_with_no_changes_needed()\n```\n\n#### `TestFormatHeaders`\n\n```\ntest_redacts_x_api_key()\ntest_redacts_authorization()\ntest_preserves_content_type()\ntest_multiple_headers_joined_by_newline()\ntest_empty_headers()\ntest_case_insensitive_redaction() - bytes comparison is lowercase\n```\n\nUse `FakeHeaders` from conftest.\n\n#### `TestExtractStopReason`\n\nThis is a high-priority test class.\n\n```\ntest_sse_no_space_variant(\"type\\\":\\\"message_delta\\\"\") -> end_turn\ntest_sse_space_variant(\"type\\\": \\\"message_delta\\\"\") -> tool_use\ntest_sse_no_stop_reason_in_delta() -> unknown (delta present but no stop_reason)\ntest_non_streaming_json_message_type() -> end_turn\ntest_non_streaming_json_multiple_lines() - header lines before JSON\ntest_no_stop_reason_found() -> \"unknown\"\ntest_sse_malformed_json_data_line() -> continues, falls back\ntest_empty_string() -> \"unknown\"\ntest_sse_takes_priority_over_non_streaming()\n```\n\nBuild raw text strings directly - no file I/O needed.\n\n#### `TestSystemPromptHash`\n\n```\ntest_cc_uses_index_2()\ntest_vix_uses_index_0()\ntest_unknown_agent_defaults_to_index_0()\ntest_index_out_of_bounds_returns_none()  - system has only 1 block for cc\ntest_no_system_returns_none()\ntest_empty_system_list_returns_none()\ntest_empty_text_returns_none()  - block has empty text\ntest_hash_is_12_char_hex()\ntest_deterministic_same_text_same_hash()\ntest_different_texts_different_hashes()\n```\n\nVerify sha256 manually: `hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]`.\n\n#### `TestResolveReadFileName`\n\n```\ntest_read_file_compress_mode() -> \"read_file_compressed\"\ntest_read_file_original_mode() -> \"read_file_uncompressed\"\ntest_read_file_no_mode_key() -> \"read_file_uncompressed\" (default)\ntest_read_file_non_dict_input() -> \"read_file_uncompressed\" (mode='original')\ntest_other_name_passthrough() -> \"Write\", \"Read\", \"edit_file\" unchanged\n```\n\n#### `TestFormatToolParams`\n\n```\ntest_string_value_gets_quoted()\ntest_non_string_value_json_dumped()\ntest_multiple_params()\ntest_empty_dict()\ntest_mixed_types()\n```\n\n#### `TestGetFilePath`\n\n```\ntest_file_path_key_absolute()\ntest_path_key_absolute()\ntest_relative_path_made_absolute()  - os.path.isabs(result) is True\ntest_file_path_takes_priority_over_path()\ntest_empty_dict_returns_none()\ntest_non_dict_returns_none()\ntest_none_value_returns_none()\n```\n\n#### `TestParseRequestBody`\n\n```\ntest_valid_json(tmp_path) - reads and returns dict\ntest_invalid_json_returns_none(tmp_path)\ntest_empty_json_object(tmp_path)  - valid: {}\ntest_file_not_found_raises() - FileNotFoundError is NOT caught, verify behavior\n```\n\nNote: `parse_request_body` only catches `json.JSONDecodeError` and `ValueError`, NOT `FileNotFoundError`. Tests should verify this behavior (the file-not-found case raises).\n\n#### `TestWriteRequest`\n\nUse `tmp_path` fixture. Build `make_flow` from conftest.\n\n```\ntest_creates_request_headers_txt(tmp_path, make_flow)\ntest_header_file_starts_with_method_url_line(tmp_path, make_flow)\ntest_x_api_key_redacted_in_headers(tmp_path, make_flow)\ntest_valid_json_body_pretty_printed(tmp_path, make_flow)\ntest_invalid_json_body_written_raw(tmp_path, make_flow)\ntest_empty_body_no_request_json(tmp_path, make_flow)\n```\n\n#### `TestWriteResponse`\n\n```\ntest_creates_response_raw_txt(tmp_path, make_flow)\ntest_none_response_no_file(tmp_path, make_flow)  - flow.response = None\ntest_status_code_and_reason_on_first_line(tmp_path, make_flow)\ntest_response_body_included(tmp_path, make_flow)\ntest_empty_response_body_no_body_section(tmp_path, make_flow)\n```\n\n#### `TestExtractReadFileWhitespace`\n\n```\ntest_read_tool_string_content()\ntest_read_tool_list_content()\ntest_ignores_non_read_tools()\ntest_read_file_compressed_tool()  - resolves correctly\ntest_empty_messages()\ntest_accumulates_multiple_reads()\n```\n\n#### `TestCategorizeInputSources`\n\nCritical: cache position logic.\n\n```\ntest_last_user_message_is_cache_write()\ntest_earlier_user_messages_are_cache_read()\ntest_second_to_last_assistant_tool_use_is_cache_write()\ntest_earlier_assistant_tool_use_is_cache_read()\ntest_total_chars_equals_json_dumps_length()\ntest_unknown_tool_id_uses_unknown_key()\ntest_empty_messages_all_zeros()\ntest_tool_results_and_tool_calls_separate()\ntest_single_message_is_both_last_and_only()\n```\n\nFor the cache_write vs cache_read assertion, build a 5-message conversation (2 user messages, 2 assistant, 1 final user) and verify:\n- last user's tool_result -> `cache_write_chars > 0`\n- first user's tool_result -> `cache_read_chars > 0`\n- second-to-last assistant's tool_use -> `cache_write_chars > 0`\n\n#### `TestCategorizeOutputSources`\n\nUses `tmp_path` for SSE and non-streaming files.\n\n```\ntest_sse_text_block(tmp_path)\ntest_sse_tool_use_block(tmp_path)\ntest_sse_mixed_blocks(tmp_path)\ntest_sse_malformed_delta_skipped(tmp_path)\ntest_non_streaming_fallback_text(tmp_path)\ntest_non_streaming_fallback_tool_use(tmp_path)\ntest_non_streaming_skips_non_message_type(tmp_path)\ntest_empty_file(tmp_path)\ntest_read_file_tool_name_resolved(tmp_path)  - tool_use block with read_file name\n```\n\n#### `TestParseResponseContent`\n\nSame SSE parsing as `categorize_output_sources` but returns structured blocks.\n\n```\ntest_sse_text_block_parsed(tmp_path)\ntest_sse_tool_use_input_assembled(tmp_path)\ntest_sse_invalid_json_input_returns_empty_dict(tmp_path)\ntest_non_streaming_text_block(tmp_path)\ntest_non_streaming_tool_use(tmp_path)\ntest_empty_sse(tmp_path)\n```\n\n#### `TestExportParsedResponse`\n\n```\ntest_creates_output_file(tmp_path)\ntest_returns_true_on_success(tmp_path)\ntest_returns_false_on_empty_blocks(tmp_path)\ntest_text_block_written_asis(tmp_path)\ntest_tool_use_formatted_with_brackets(tmp_path)\ntest_tool_use_params_included(tmp_path)\n```\n\n#### `TestAttributeTokens`\n\n```\ntest_zero_total_chars_returns_empty_input()\ntest_zero_input_tokens_returns_empty_input()\ntest_none_pricing_returns_empty_input()\ntest_zero_total_output_chars_returns_empty_output()\ntest_zero_output_tokens_returns_empty_output()\ntest_proportional_input_attribution()\ntest_proportional_output_attribution()\ntest_output_tool_calls_fractional()\ntest_both_tool_results_and_tool_calls()\ntest_output_total_included_in_tool_calls()\n```\n\nFor `test_proportional_input_attribution`: build a case where `Read` has 500/1000 chars, verify `tokens` is approximately half of total input tokens.\n\n#### `TestAggregateBySource`\n\n```\ntest_first_call_initializes_keys()\ntest_accumulates_on_second_call()\ntest_skips_non_dict_entries()\ntest_empty_flow_by_source()\ntest_tool_calls_section()\ntest_output_llm_text()\ntest_output_tool_calls()\n```\n\n#### `TestRoundBySource`\n\n```\ntest_rounds_input_tool_results_dollars()\ntest_rounds_input_tool_calls_dollars()\ntest_rounds_output_llm_text_dollars()\ntest_rounds_output_tool_calls_dollars()\ntest_six_decimal_places()\ntest_empty_agg_no_error()\n```\n\n#### `TestAgentColor`\n\n```\ntest_returns_hash_prefixed_color()\ntest_deterministic()\ntest_format_7_chars_starting_with_hash()\ntest_different_names_different_colors()\ntest_known_agents_use_AGENT_COLORS_not_md5()  - vix and cc are in AGENT_COLORS\n```\n\nNote: `_agent_color` is only called for names NOT in `AGENT_COLORS`. The `summarize_usage` function does `AGENT_COLORS.get(entry, _agent_color(entry))`. Test `_agent_color` directly with arbitrary names.\n\n#### `TestRedactFlowFiles`\n\nUses `tmp_path` + patching `FlowReader`/`FlowWriter` on the `export_flows` module.\n\n```\ntest_no_flow_files_no_op(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_redacts_x_api_key(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_redacts_authorization(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_non_http_flow_not_modified(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_flow_read_exception_skipped(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_unmodified_flow_not_rewritten(tmp_path, ef)  - modified=False branch\ntest_multiple_flow_files(tmp_path, ef)\n```\n\nKey mock pattern:\n```python\nclass HeadersMock:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._h = {b\"x-api-key\": \"secret\"}\n    def get(self, key):\n        return self._h.get(key)\n    def __setitem__(self, k, v):\n        self._h[k] = v\n\nwritten = []\nclass CapturingWriter:\n    def __init__(self, f): pass\n    def add(self, flow): written.append(flow)\n\nwith patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", ...), patch.object(ef, \"FlowWriter\", CapturingWriter):\n    ef.redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))\n```\n\n#### `TestExportFlows`\n\nThis is the most complex class. Split into sub-scenarios.\n\n```\ntest_no_flow_files_prints_message(tmp_path, ef, capsys)\ntest_count_token_url_skipped(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_quota_message_skipped(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_quota_with_system_not_skipped(tmp_path, ef)  - quota string + system key -> NOT skipped\ntest_non_http_flow_skipped(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_creates_flow_directory_structure(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_writes_timing_json(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_cc_step_increments_on_hash_change(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_cc_step_stays_same_on_same_hash(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_cc_request_index_increments_within_step(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_vix_step_increments_on_end_turn(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_vix_request_index_increments_on_non_end_turn(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_existing_output_dir_removed_and_recreated(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_flow_read_exception_skipped(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_none_response_handled(tmp_path, ef)\n```\n\nBuilder pattern: each test creates a list of fake flows, patches `FlowReader.stream()` to yield them, patches `FlowWriter`, calls `ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(tmp_path))`, then asserts on directory structure.\n\nThe step boundary tests need multiple flows with carefully crafted system prompts.\n\n**cc step boundary test setup:**\n```python\n# Flow 1: system_text=\"promptA\" -> prev_hash=None, hash=hashA -> no step increment (prev is None)\n# Flow 2: system_text=\"promptA\" -> hash=hashA == hashA -> no increment, step=1, req=2\n# Flow 3: system_text=\"promptB\" -> hash=hashB != hashA -> step=2, req=1\n```\n\n**vix step boundary test setup:**\n```python\n# Flow 1: stop=tool_use -> step=1, req=1, then req_index++\n# Flow 2: stop=end_turn -> step=1, req=2, then step++, req=1\n# Flow 3: stop=tool_use -> step=2, req=1\n```\n\n#### `TestExtractUsage`\n\n```\ntest_sse_usage_extracted(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_sse_space_variant_in_type_key(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_non_streaming_fallback(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_timing_merged_and_timing_file_deleted(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_no_usage_found_warning(tmp_path, ef, capsys)\ntest_token_fields_filtered(tmp_path, ef)  - only known fields kept\ntest_no_response_raw_skipped(tmp_path, ef)\n```\n\n#### `TestExtractPrompts`\n\n```\ntest_extracts_system_prompt(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_extracts_first_user_message(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_system_prompt_concatenates_text_blocks(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_skips_non_text_system_blocks(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_user_message_string_content_no_file(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_no_system_no_system_file(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_invalid_request_json_warning(tmp_path, ef, capsys)\ntest_first_user_message_only(tmp_path, ef)  - multiple user msgs, only first extracted\n```\n\n#### `TestCalculateCosts`\n\n```\ntest_computes_all_cost_fields(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_removes_top_level_token_keys(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_adds_canonical_model(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_unknown_model_warning(tmp_path, ef, capsys)\ntest_no_model_skipped(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_zero_tokens_zero_cost(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_model_with_date_suffix_resolved(tmp_path, ef)\n```\n\n#### `TestExtractFileOps`\n\n```\ntest_read_file_tracked(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_write_file_tracked(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_edit_file_uses_new_string(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_deduplication_by_tool_id(tmp_path, ef)  - same file_path, different tool_ids -> calls=2\ntest_same_tool_id_not_duplicated(tmp_path, ef)  - same tool_id appears in multiple turns\ntest_relative_path_made_absolute(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_file_size_none_when_file_missing(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_unique_files_read_count(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_total_read_chars_sum(tmp_path, ef)\n```\n\nFor `test_deduplication_by_tool_id`: Two separate tool_use blocks with same `file_path` but different IDs (tid1, tid2) -> `calls=2`, `chars=sum`. Same file_path + same ID appearing in 2 messages -> still `calls=1` (dedup by ID).\n\n#### `TestSummarizeUsage`\n\n```\ntest_single_agent_single_request(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_by_model_aggregation(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_by_step_aggregation(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_known_agent_uses_preset_color(tmp_path, ef)  - vix -> #7B2FBE\ntest_unknown_agent_uses_md5_color(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_skips_non_dir_entries(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_skips_dirs_without_numbered_subdirs(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_timing_wall_clock_computed(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_timing_avg_duration_computed(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_file_ops_aggregated_and_finalized(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_by_source_aggregated(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_read_file_whitespace_aggregated(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_writes_usage_json(tmp_path, ef)\ntest_multiple_agents(tmp_path, ef)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Pytest Features to Use\n\n**Fixtures:**\n- `tmp_path` - built-in pytest fixture for temporary directories, used in all I/O tests\n- `capsys` - capture stdout for functions that print warnings and status\n- `ef` - session-scoped fixture from conftest returning the `export_flows` module\n- `make_flow` - factory fixture from conftest for building mock HTTPFlow objects\n- `fake_http_flow_class` / `fake_flow_read_exception` - expose stub classes\n\n**`@pytest.mark.parametrize`:**\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"model_id,expected\", [\n    (\"claude-opus-4-5\", \"claude-opus-4-5\"),\n    (\"claude-opus-4-5-20250101\", \"claude-opus-4-5\"),\n    (\"claude-opus-4-20250101\", \"claude-opus-4\"),\n    (\"claude-haiku-3-5\", \"claude-haiku-3-5\"),\n    (\"gpt-4\", None),\n    (\"\", None),\n])\ndef test_get_canonical_model(ef, model_id, expected):\n    assert ef.get_canonical_model(model_id) == expected\n```\n\n**`unittest.mock.patch` via `with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", ...):`** - used throughout `TestRedactFlowFiles` and `TestExportFlows`.\n\n**`monkeypatch`** - for patching module-level globals when needed (e.g., temporarily altering `SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX`).\n\n**Helper builders** defined as module-level functions in the test file:\n\n```python\ndef make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"end_turn\", usage=None):\n    \"\"\"Build a minimal SSE response string.\"\"\"\n\ndef make_request_body(model=\"claude-sonnet-4-5\", messages=None, system=None):\n    \"\"\"Build a minimal request body dict.\"\"\"\n\ndef write_files(dirpath, request_body=None, usage=None, response_raw=None):\n    \"\"\"Write request.json, usage.json, response_raw.txt to dirpath.\"\"\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Mocking Strategy\n\n**Session-level stub injection** (in `conftest.py`, before any imports) handles the top-level `from mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter` etc. The stubs use real Python classes (not `MagicMock`) so that `isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow)` checks work correctly.\n\n**Test-level flow reader mocking** uses `patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", SomeClass)` because `export_flows` imports `FlowReader` into its own namespace via `from mitmproxy.io import FlowReader`. Patching `ef.FlowReader` (the name as bound in the module) is the correct approach.\n\nVerified pattern:\n```python\nclass SpecificFlowReader:\n    def __init__(self, f): pass\n    def stream(self):\n        return iter([flow1, flow2])\n\nwith patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", SpecificFlowReader):\n    ef.export_flows(input_dir, output_dir)\n```\n\nThe `FlowWriter` is patched similarly: `patch.object(ef, \"FlowWriter\", MagicMock())`.\n\n**File I/O** uses real temporary files via `tmp_path` rather than `mock_open`, because the functions do complex file walking (os.walk). `mock_open` would be too brittle. Real temp directories are cleaner and more reliable.\n\n**`glob.glob`** does NOT need mocking since actual `.flow` files are created in `tmp_path`.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Coverage Strategy - Reaching 80%+\n\nThe lines that are difficult to cover:\n\n| Lines | Reason | Strategy |\n|-------|---------|----------|\n| `main()` (lines 1405-1429) | Requires `argparse` + full pipeline | Skip entirely (add `pragma: no cover` or just don't test - it's <30 lines of ~1430 total = ~2%) |\n| `_PROJECT_ROOT` definition (line 903) | Module-level, executed on import | Covered automatically by import |\n| `print()` statements | Side effects | Covered by capsys tests |\n| FlowReadException import | Covered by session import | Auto-covered |\n\nThe functions most critical for hitting 80% (by line count contribution):\n\n1. `export_flows()` - ~100 lines, high complexity, needs careful scenario coverage\n2. `summarize_usage()` - ~160 lines, needs multiple usage.json files with all optional fields\n3. `categorize_input_sources()` / `categorize_output_sources()` - ~80+80 lines\n4. `extract_file_ops()` - ~100 lines\n5. `attribute_tokens()` - ~80 lines\n\nTo cover the nested `_finalize_file_ops`, `_finalize_timing`, `add_to_bucket`, `empty_bucket`, `round_costs` inner functions in `summarize_usage`, the tests need to provide multi-step, multi-request data with `by_source`, `read_file_whitespace`, and `file_ops` fields in the usage JSON.\n\n**Estimated coverage by class:**\n- All pure functions (count_whitespace, get_canonical, get_pricing, sanitize, format_headers, extract_stop_reason, _system_prompt_hash, etc.): ~95%\n- I/O functions with tmp_path: ~90%\n- export_flows/redact_flow_files with patched FlowReader: ~85%\n- summarize_usage with full fixture: ~80%\n- main(): excluded from count\n\nTotal estimated: ~83-87% coverage achievable with the test plan above.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Key Edge Cases That Must Not Be Missed\n\n1. **`parse_request_body` does NOT catch `FileNotFoundError`** - test should expect it to raise, not return `None`.\n\n2. **`extract_stop_reason` SSE vs non-streaming priority** - SSE is tried first, non-streaming only if no SSE lines found. A file with both SSE lines AND a JSON message line uses SSE result.\n\n3. **`categorize_input_sources` with `second_to_last_idx = -1`** - when there is only one message (the last user message), `second_to_last_idx = last_user_idx - 1 = -1`, so `is_cache_write = (i == -1)` is always False for valid indices (since `enumerate` starts at 0). This means single-message conversations have everything in `cache_read` from the assistant side (which is an empty conversation anyway).\n\n4. **`export_flows` for `cc` agent**: the first flow's `prev_prompt_hash` is `None`, so no step increment on the first flow regardless of hash. The step only increments when BOTH `prompt_hash is not None` AND `prev_prompt_hash is not None` AND they differ.\n\n5. **`export_flows` quota check** - `content == \"quota\"` AND `not system`. A flow where content is \"quota\" BUT system IS present should NOT be skipped.\n\n6. **`write_request` with invalid JSON body** - writes the raw body string to `request.json`, not `None`.\n\n7. **`_resolve_read_file_name` with non-dict tool_input** - `mode` defaults to `\"original\"` ‚Üí returns `\"read_file_uncompressed\"`.\n\n8. **`sanitize_path` with underscore stripping** - `/v1/messages` ‚Üí after replace: `_v1_messages` ‚Üí after strip `_`: `v1_messages`.\n\n9. **`format_headers` uses raw bytes in output** - the output contains `b'content-type': b'application/json'` style (with `b` prefix), not decoded strings. Tests must verify against the actual byte repr format.\n\n10. **`extract_file_ops` deduplication**: same `file_path`, multiple tool_use invocations ‚Üí `calls` = number of unique `tool_use_id`s, `chars` = sum of their contents. The dedup key is `tool_use_id`, NOT `(file_path, content)`.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `/workspace/export_flows.py`\n- `/workspace/evaluation/usage/conftest.py`\n- `/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py`\n- `/workspace/evaluation/` (directory - must be created)\n- `/workspace/evaluation/usage/` (directory - must be created)"}]}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll write the plan file:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016HDoMrkmSWBChut115t4uL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/.claude/plans/tingly-forging-canyon.md","content":"# Plan: Write Tests for evaluation/usage/export_flows.py\n\n## Context\n\nThe user wants a comprehensive pytest test suite for `/workspace/export_flows.py` placed at\n`/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py`. The module is 1430 lines and processes\nmitmproxy flow files ‚Äî exporting them to per-flow directory structures with token usage,\ncost calculations, and source attribution. The goal is ‚â•80% code coverage.\n\nThe `evaluation/usage/` directory does not yet exist and must be created.\n\n---\n\n## Files to Create\n\n1. `/workspace/evaluation/usage/conftest.py` ‚Äî mitmproxy stub injection + shared fixtures\n2. `/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py` ‚Äî full test suite\n\n---\n\n## Critical Design Decisions\n\n### Import Strategy\nThe test file lives in `evaluation/usage/` but the module is at `/workspace/export_flows.py`.\n`conftest.py` injects the path:\n```python\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..', '..'))\n```\n\n### Mitmproxy Mocking\n`export_flows.py` imports from mitmproxy at module level. Since mitmproxy may not be\ninstalled, `conftest.py` injects fake stub modules into `sys.modules` **before** any import\nof `export_flows`. Tests then use `patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", ...)` to control flow\nstreams per-test, since `export_flows` binds the names locally via `from mitmproxy.io import`.\n\n### File I/O\nAll filesystem tests use real `tmp_path` directories (not `mock_open`) because the functions\ndo `os.walk`, `glob.glob`, and multi-file operations that are too brittle to mock at the fd level.\n\n---\n\n## conftest.py Structure\n\n```python\n# Inject stubs before any import:\n# - mitmproxy.io:         FlowReader (with .stream()), FlowWriter (with .add())\n# - mitmproxy.exceptions: FlowReadException\n# - mitmproxy.http:       HTTPFlow\n\n# Session fixture `ef` returns the imported `export_flows` module.\n\n# Helper classes: FakeHeaders, FakeRequest, FakeResponse\n# Factory fixture `make_flow` creates mock HTTPFlow-like objects.\n# Helper `write_flow_files(dirpath, ...)` writes request.json/usage.json/response_raw.txt.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Test Classes and Key Cases\n\n### TestCountWhitespaceStats\n- Empty string ‚Üí all zeros\n- Single `\\n` ‚Üí line_returns=1\n- `\"  \"` (2 spaces) ‚Üí unnecessary_space_count=1\n- `\"   \"` (3 spaces) ‚Üí unnecessary_space_count=2\n- Multiple runs accumulated\n- total_chars matches `len(text)`\n\n### TestGetCanonicalModel\n- `\"claude-opus-4-5-20250101\"` ‚Üí `\"claude-opus-4-5\"` NOT `\"claude-opus-4\"` (longest-prefix)\n- `\"claude-opus-4-20250101\"` ‚Üí `\"claude-opus-4\"`\n- Unknown model ‚Üí `None`\n- Parametrize over all MODEL_PRICING keys (exact match)\n\n### TestGetPricing\n- Returns dict with input/cache_write/cache_read/output keys\n- Model with date suffix resolved\n- Unknown ‚Üí `None`\n\n### TestSanitizePath\n- `/v1/messages` ‚Üí `\"v1_messages\"` (strips leading `_`, replaces `/`)\n- Query string stripped: `/path?foo=bar` ‚Üí `\"path\"`\n- Special chars removed: `\"/v1/!messages@\"` ‚Üí `\"v1_messages\"`\n- Truncated to 80 chars\n\n### TestFormatHeaders\n- `x-api-key` ‚Üí `[REDACTED]`\n- `authorization` ‚Üí `[REDACTED]`\n- Case-insensitive redaction (bytes lowered before comparison)\n- Other headers preserved\n\n### TestExtractStopReason\n- SSE `\"type\":\"message_delta\"` (no space) with stop_reason\n- SSE `\"type\": \"message_delta\"` (with space) with stop_reason\n- SSE present but no stop_reason in delta ‚Üí falls through to \"unknown\"\n- Non-streaming JSON `\"type\":\"message\"` fallback\n- No matching data ‚Üí `\"unknown\"`\n- Malformed JSON in SSE lines ‚Üí skipped, continues\n\n### TestSystemPromptHash\n- cc uses index 2, vix uses index 0\n- Index out of bounds ‚Üí `None`\n- Missing \"system\" key ‚Üí `None`\n- Empty text ‚Üí `None`\n- Returns 12-char hex string\n- Deterministic: same text ‚Üí same hash\n\n### TestResolveReadFileName\n- `read_file` + `{\"mode\": \"compress\"}` ‚Üí `\"read_file_compressed\"`\n- `read_file` + `{}` ‚Üí `\"read_file_uncompressed\"`\n- `read_file` + non-dict input ‚Üí `\"read_file_uncompressed\"`\n- Any other name ‚Üí unchanged\n\n### TestFormatToolParams\n- String values quoted: `key=\"val\"`\n- Non-string JSON-dumped: `key=42`\n- Empty dict ‚Üí `\"\"`\n\n### TestGetFilePath\n- Returns `file_path` key if present (absolute unchanged, relative made absolute)\n- Falls back to `path` key\n- `None` dict or missing keys ‚Üí `None`\n\n### TestParseRequestBody\n- Valid JSON file ‚Üí dict returned\n- Invalid JSON ‚Üí `None`\n- FileNotFoundError is NOT caught (raises)\n\n### TestWriteRequest / TestWriteResponse\n- Creates `request_headers.txt` with METHOD URL line\n- `x-api-key` redacted in headers\n- Valid JSON body pretty-printed in `request.json`\n- Invalid JSON body written raw\n- Empty body ‚Üí no `request.json` created\n- `None` response ‚Üí no `response_raw.txt` created\n\n### TestExtractReadFileWhitespace\n- `read_file` tool_result with string content ‚Üí stats counted\n- List content ‚Üí concatenated then counted\n- Non-read tools ignored\n- Multiple reads accumulated\n\n### TestCategorizeInputSources\n- Last user message tool_result ‚Üí `cache_write_chars > 0`\n- Earlier user message tool_result ‚Üí `cache_read_chars > 0`\n- Second-to-last message (assistant) tool_use ‚Üí `cache_write_chars > 0`\n- Earlier assistant tool_use ‚Üí `cache_read_chars > 0`\n- `total_chars == len(json.dumps(body))`\n\n### TestCategorizeOutputSources\n- SSE `content_block_start/delta/stop` sequence for text ‚Üí `llm_text` chars counted\n- SSE tool_use block ‚Üí `tool_calls[name]` chars counted\n- Non-streaming fallback (no SSE data lines)\n- `read_file` tool name resolved via `_resolve_read_file_name`\n\n### TestParseResponseContent\n- SSE text block assembled from deltas\n- SSE tool_use block with JSON input assembled\n- Invalid JSON in input_json_delta ‚Üí empty dict fallback\n- Non-streaming `{\"type\":\"message\",\"content\":[...]}` fallback\n\n### TestExportParsedResponse\n- Returns `True` on success, `False` when no blocks\n- Text blocks written as-is\n- Tool use formatted as `[name(params)]`\n\n### TestAttributeTokens\n- Zero `total_chars` ‚Üí empty input attribution\n- Zero `output_tokens` ‚Üí empty output attribution\n- Proportional input: tool with 50% of chars gets ~50% of tokens\n- Output has `__total` entry in tool_calls\n- `None` pricing ‚Üí empty input attribution\n\n### TestAggregateBySource / TestRoundBySource\n- Accumulates tokens, dollars, chars across calls\n- Non-dict entries skipped\n- Rounds dollars to 6 decimal places\n\n### TestAgentColor\n- Returns `#xxxxxx` format (7 chars)\n- Deterministic for same name\n- Different names ‚Üí different colors\n\n### TestRedactFlowFiles\n- No `.flow` files ‚Üí no-op\n- Flow with `x-api-key` ‚Üí header replaced with `[REDACTED]`, file rewritten\n- Flow without sensitive headers ‚Üí `modified=False`, file NOT rewritten\n- `FlowReadException` ‚Üí skipped\n- Non-HTTPFlow objects processed without error\n\n### TestExportFlows\n- No `.flow` files ‚Üí prints message, returns\n- `/count_token` URL ‚Üí flow skipped\n- Quota message (content==\"quota\", no system) ‚Üí flow skipped\n- Quota with system present ‚Üí NOT skipped\n- cc agent: step increments when system prompt hash changes (prev_hash must be non-None)\n- cc agent: first flow never increments step (prev_hash is None)\n- vix agent: step increments after `end_turn` response\n- vix agent: request_index increments for `tool_use` response\n- `FlowReadException` ‚Üí file skipped\n- `None` response ‚Üí timing.json still written (without response_end)\n- Creates `{step}/{request}/` directory structure\n\n### TestExtractUsage\n- SSE `message_delta` usage extracted and written to `usage.json`\n- Only TOKEN_FIELDS kept\n- Timing merged from `timing.json`, which is then deleted\n- Non-streaming fallback (`\"type\":\"message\"`)\n- No usage found ‚Üí warning printed, file not written\n\n### TestExtractPrompts\n- `system_prompt.md` written from text blocks\n- `first_user_message.md` written from first user message\n- Non-text system blocks skipped\n- Invalid request.json ‚Üí warning printed\n- String content in user message ‚Üí no file (only list content processed)\n\n### TestCalculateCosts\n- All cost fields computed: input, cache_write, cache_read, output, total\n- Top-level token keys removed\n- Canonical model name added\n- Unknown model ‚Üí warning, usage.json unchanged\n- No model field ‚Üí skipped\n\n### TestExtractFileOps\n- Read file tracked with file_path key\n- Write file (Write/write_file) uses `content` for chars\n- Edit file (Edit/edit_file) uses `new_string` for chars\n- Deduplication: same file_path + same tool_id ‚Üí counted once\n- Same file_path + different tool_ids ‚Üí calls=2\n- Missing file ‚Üí `file_size=None`\n\n### TestSummarizeUsage\n- Writes `usage.json` to agent directory\n- `by_model` aggregated per model\n- `by_step` aggregated per step directory\n- Known agent (vix/cc) gets preset color from `AGENT_COLORS`\n- Unknown agent gets MD5 color\n- `timing.wall_clock_ms` = (max_response_end - min_request_start) * 1000\n- `timing.avg_duration_ms` = total_duration_ms / request_count\n- `file_ops.tool_ids` maps finalized to `calls`/`chars` (dedup)\n- Dirs without numbered subdirectories skipped\n\n---\n\n## Coverage Exclusion\n`main()` (~25 lines) is not tested ‚Äî it's argparse scaffolding over functions already\ntested individually. This keeps overall covered % well above 80%.\n\n---\n\n## Verification\nRun: `cd /workspace && python -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py -v --tb=short`\n\nWith coverage: `python -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py --cov=export_flows --cov-report=term-missing`\n"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HDoMrkmSWBChut115t4uL","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/.claude/plans/tingly-forging-canyon.md"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T1ac1zikZPCqJLzR1WzDYD","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"User has approved your plan. You can now start coding. Start with updating your todo list if applicable\n\nYour plan has been saved to: /root/.claude/plans/tingly-forging-canyon.md\nYou can refer back to it if needed during implementation.\n\n## Approved Plan:\n# Plan: Write Tests for evaluation/usage/export_flows.py\n\n## Context\n\nThe user wants a comprehensive pytest test suite for `/workspace/export_flows.py` placed at\n`/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py`. The module is 1430 lines and processes\nmitmproxy flow files ‚Äî exporting them to per-flow directory structures with token usage,\ncost calculations, and source attribution. The goal is ‚â•80% code coverage.\n\nThe `evaluation/usage/` directory does not yet exist and must be created.\n\n---\n\n## Files to Create\n\n1. `/workspace/evaluation/usage/conftest.py` ‚Äî mitmproxy stub injection + shared fixtures\n2. `/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py` ‚Äî full test suite\n\n---\n\n## Critical Design Decisions\n\n### Import Strategy\nThe test file lives in `evaluation/usage/` but the module is at `/workspace/export_flows.py`.\n`conftest.py` injects the path:\n```python\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..', '..'))\n```\n\n### Mitmproxy Mocking\n`export_flows.py` imports from mitmproxy at module level. Since mitmproxy may not be\ninstalled, `conftest.py` injects fake stub modules into `sys.modules` **before** any import\nof `export_flows`. Tests then use `patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", ...)` to control flow\nstreams per-test, since `export_flows` binds the names locally via `from mitmproxy.io import`.\n\n### File I/O\nAll filesystem tests use real `tmp_path` directories (not `mock_open`) because the functions\ndo `os.walk`, `glob.glob`, and multi-file operations that are too brittle to mock at the fd level.\n\n---\n\n## conftest.py Structure\n\n```python\n# Inject stubs before any import:\n# - mitmproxy.io:         FlowReader (with .stream()), FlowWriter (with .add())\n# - mitmproxy.exceptions: FlowReadException\n# - mitmproxy.http:       HTTPFlow\n\n# Session fixture `ef` returns the imported `export_flows` module.\n\n# Helper classes: FakeHeaders, FakeRequest, FakeResponse\n# Factory fixture `make_flow` creates mock HTTPFlow-like objects.\n# Helper `write_flow_files(dirpath, ...)` writes request.json/usage.json/response_raw.txt.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Test Classes and Key Cases\n\n### TestCountWhitespaceStats\n- Empty string ‚Üí all zeros\n- Single `\\n` ‚Üí line_returns=1\n- `\"  \"` (2 spaces) ‚Üí unnecessary_space_count=1\n- `\"   \"` (3 spaces) ‚Üí unnecessary_space_count=2\n- Multiple runs accumulated\n- total_chars matches `len(text)`\n\n### TestGetCanonicalModel\n- `\"claude-opus-4-5-20250101\"` ‚Üí `\"claude-opus-4-5\"` NOT `\"claude-opus-4\"` (longest-prefix)\n- `\"claude-opus-4-20250101\"` ‚Üí `\"claude-opus-4\"`\n- Unknown model ‚Üí `None`\n- Parametrize over all MODEL_PRICING keys (exact match)\n\n### TestGetPricing\n- Returns dict with input/cache_write/cache_read/output keys\n- Model with date suffix resolved\n- Unknown ‚Üí `None`\n\n### TestSanitizePath\n- `/v1/messages` ‚Üí `\"v1_messages\"` (strips leading `_`, replaces `/`)\n- Query string stripped: `/path?foo=bar` ‚Üí `\"path\"`\n- Special chars removed: `\"/v1/!messages@\"` ‚Üí `\"v1_messages\"`\n- Truncated to 80 chars\n\n### TestFormatHeaders\n- `x-api-key` ‚Üí `[REDACTED]`\n- `authorization` ‚Üí `[REDACTED]`\n- Case-insensitive redaction (bytes lowered before comparison)\n- Other headers preserved\n\n### TestExtractStopReason\n- SSE `\"type\":\"message_delta\"` (no space) with stop_reason\n- SSE `\"type\": \"message_delta\"` (with space) with stop_reason\n- SSE present but no stop_reason in delta ‚Üí falls through to \"unknown\"\n- Non-streaming JSON `\"type\":\"message\"` fallback\n- No matching data ‚Üí `\"unknown\"`\n- Malformed JSON in SSE lines ‚Üí skipped, continues\n\n### TestSystemPromptHash\n- cc uses index 2, vix uses index 0\n- Index out of bounds ‚Üí `None`\n- Missing \"system\" key ‚Üí `None`\n- Empty text ‚Üí `None`\n- Returns 12-char hex string\n- Deterministic: same text ‚Üí same hash\n\n### TestResolveReadFileName\n- `read_file` + `{\"mode\": \"compress\"}` ‚Üí `\"read_file_compressed\"`\n- `read_file` + `{}` ‚Üí `\"read_file_uncompressed\"`\n- `read_file` + non-dict input ‚Üí `\"read_file_uncompressed\"`\n- Any other name ‚Üí unchanged\n\n### TestFormatToolParams\n- String values quoted: `key=\"val\"`\n- Non-string JSON-dumped: `key=42`\n- Empty dict ‚Üí `\"\"`\n\n### TestGetFilePath\n- Returns `file_path` key if present (absolute unchanged, relative made absolute)\n- Falls back to `path` key\n- `None` dict or missing keys ‚Üí `None`\n\n### TestParseRequestBody\n- Valid JSON file ‚Üí dict returned\n- Invalid JSON ‚Üí `None`\n- FileNotFoundError is NOT caught (raises)\n\n### TestWriteRequest / TestWriteResponse\n- Creates `request_headers.txt` with METHOD URL line\n- `x-api-key` redacted in headers\n- Valid JSON body pretty-printed in `request.json`\n- Invalid JSON body written raw\n- Empty body ‚Üí no `request.json` created\n- `None` response ‚Üí no `response_raw.txt` created\n\n### TestExtractReadFileWhitespace\n- `read_file` tool_result with string content ‚Üí stats counted\n- List content ‚Üí concatenated then counted\n- Non-read tools ignored\n- Multiple reads accumulated\n\n### TestCategorizeInputSources\n- Last user message tool_result ‚Üí `cache_write_chars > 0`\n- Earlier user message tool_result ‚Üí `cache_read_chars > 0`\n- Second-to-last message (assistant) tool_use ‚Üí `cache_write_chars > 0`\n- Earlier assistant tool_use ‚Üí `cache_read_chars > 0`\n- `total_chars == len(json.dumps(body))`\n\n### TestCategorizeOutputSources\n- SSE `content_block_start/delta/stop` sequence for text ‚Üí `llm_text` chars counted\n- SSE tool_use block ‚Üí `tool_calls[name]` chars counted\n- Non-streaming fallback (no SSE data lines)\n- `read_file` tool name resolved via `_resolve_read_file_name`\n\n### TestParseResponseContent\n- SSE text block assembled from deltas\n- SSE tool_use block with JSON input assembled\n- Invalid JSON in input_json_delta ‚Üí empty dict fallback\n- Non-streaming `{\"type\":\"message\",\"content\":[...]}` fallback\n\n### TestExportParsedResponse\n- Returns `True` on success, `False` when no blocks\n- Text blocks written as-is\n- Tool use formatted as `[name(params)]`\n\n### TestAttributeTokens\n- Zero `total_chars` ‚Üí empty input attribution\n- Zero `output_tokens` ‚Üí empty output attribution\n- Proportional input: tool with 50% of chars gets ~50% of tokens\n- Output has `__total` entry in tool_calls\n- `None` pricing ‚Üí empty input attribution\n\n### TestAggregateBySource / TestRoundBySource\n- Accumulates tokens, dollars, chars across calls\n- Non-dict entries skipped\n- Rounds dollars to 6 decimal places\n\n### TestAgentColor\n- Returns `#xxxxxx` format (7 chars)\n- Deterministic for same name\n- Different names ‚Üí different colors\n\n### TestRedactFlowFiles\n- No `.flow` files ‚Üí no-op\n- Flow with `x-api-key` ‚Üí header replaced with `[REDACTED]`, file rewritten\n- Flow without sensitive headers ‚Üí `modified=False`, file NOT rewritten\n- `FlowReadException` ‚Üí skipped\n- Non-HTTPFlow objects processed without error\n\n### TestExportFlows\n- No `.flow` files ‚Üí prints message, returns\n- `/count_token` URL ‚Üí flow skipped\n- Quota message (content==\"quota\", no system) ‚Üí flow skipped\n- Quota with system present ‚Üí NOT skipped\n- cc agent: step increments when system prompt hash changes (prev_hash must be non-None)\n- cc agent: first flow never increments step (prev_hash is None)\n- vix agent: step increments after `end_turn` response\n- vix agent: request_index increments for `tool_use` response\n- `FlowReadException` ‚Üí file skipped\n- `None` response ‚Üí timing.json still written (without response_end)\n- Creates `{step}/{request}/` directory structure\n\n### TestExtractUsage\n- SSE `message_delta` usage extracted and written to `usage.json`\n- Only TOKEN_FIELDS kept\n- Timing merged from `timing.json`, which is then deleted\n- Non-streaming fallback (`\"type\":\"message\"`)\n- No usage found ‚Üí warning printed, file not written\n\n### TestExtractPrompts\n- `system_prompt.md` written from text blocks\n- `first_user_message.md` written from first user message\n- Non-text system blocks skipped\n- Invalid request.json ‚Üí warning printed\n- String content in user message ‚Üí no file (only list content processed)\n\n### TestCalculateCosts\n- All cost fields computed: input, cache_write, cache_read, output, total\n- Top-level token keys removed\n- Canonical model name added\n- Unknown model ‚Üí warning, usage.json unchanged\n- No model field ‚Üí skipped\n\n### TestExtractFileOps\n- Read file tracked with file_path key\n- Write file (Write/write_file) uses `content` for chars\n- Edit file (Edit/edit_file) uses `new_string` for chars\n- Deduplication: same file_path + same tool_id ‚Üí counted once\n- Same file_path + different tool_ids ‚Üí calls=2\n- Missing file ‚Üí `file_size=None`\n\n### TestSummarizeUsage\n- Writes `usage.json` to agent directory\n- `by_model` aggregated per model\n- `by_step` aggregated per step directory\n- Known agent (vix/cc) gets preset color from `AGENT_COLORS`\n- Unknown agent gets MD5 color\n- `timing.wall_clock_ms` = (max_response_end - min_request_start) * 1000\n- `timing.avg_duration_ms` = total_duration_ms / request_count\n- `file_ops.tool_ids` maps finalized to `calls`/`chars` (dedup)\n- Dirs without numbered subdirectories skipped\n\n---\n\n## Coverage Exclusion\n`main()` (~25 lines) is not tested ‚Äî it's argparse scaffolding over functions already\ntested individually. This keeps overall covered % well above 80%.\n\n---\n\n## Verification\nRun: `cd /workspace && python -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py -v --tb=short`\n\nWith coverage: `python -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py --cov=export_flows --cov-report=term-missing`\n\n<system-reminder>\n## Exited Plan Mode\n\nYou have exited plan mode. You can now make edits, run tools, and take actions. The plan file is located at /root/.claude/plans/tingly-forging-canyon.md if you need to reference it.\n</system-reminder>","tool_use_id":"toolu_01T1ac1zikZPCqJLzR1WzDYD"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QuvCFxiM5GLn49i3qgauqZ","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Create evaluation/usage/ directory with conftest.py","description":"Create /workspace/evaluation/usage/ directory and write conftest.py with mitmproxy stubs, sys.path setup, and shared fixtures"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QuvCFxiM5GLn49i3qgauqZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Task #1 created successfully: Create evaluation/usage/ directory with conftest.py"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ric52i9gYFZvRfsqTVojWT","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Write test_export_flows.py with full test suite","description":"Write comprehensive pytest test suite covering all major functions in export_flows.py to achieve ‚â•80% coverage"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ric52i9gYFZvRfsqTVojWT","type":"tool_result","content":"Task #2 created successfully: Write test_export_flows.py with full test suite"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QtnDxDp8A8BPyYzuzRW4z3","name":"TaskUpdate","input":{"taskId":"1","status":"in_progress"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QtnDxDp8A8BPyYzuzRW4z3","type":"tool_result","content":"Updated task #1 status"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012vzFke2LD1VgfbyXzHcLSg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /workspace/evaluation/usage","description":"Create evaluation/usage directories"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012vzFke2LD1VgfbyXzHcLSg","type":"tool_result","content":"(Bash completed with no output)","is_error":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GoLpn9xJw6ijfE39aFsS9c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/evaluation/usage/conftest.py","content":"\"\"\"conftest.py: inject mitmproxy stubs before any module import, then expose shared fixtures.\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport types\nimport json\nimport pytest\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Inject mitmproxy stubs into sys.modules BEFORE export_flows is imported.\n# This must run at import time of conftest.py (i.e., before any test collection).\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass _FakeFlowReadException(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\nclass _FakeHTTPFlow:\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for mitmproxy.http.HTTPFlow.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass _FakeFlowReader:\n    def __init__(self, f):\n        pass\n\n    def stream(self):\n        return iter([])\n\n\nclass _FakeFlowWriter:\n    def __init__(self, f):\n        pass\n\n    def add(self, flow):\n        pass\n\n\n_mitmproxy_pkg = types.ModuleType(\"mitmproxy\")\n_mitmproxy_io = types.ModuleType(\"mitmproxy.io\")\n_mitmproxy_io.FlowReader = _FakeFlowReader\n_mitmproxy_io.FlowWriter = _FakeFlowWriter\n_mitmproxy_exceptions = types.ModuleType(\"mitmproxy.exceptions\")\n_mitmproxy_exceptions.FlowReadException = _FakeFlowReadException\n_mitmproxy_http = types.ModuleType(\"mitmproxy.http\")\n_mitmproxy_http.HTTPFlow = _FakeHTTPFlow\n\nsys.modules.setdefault(\"mitmproxy\", _mitmproxy_pkg)\nsys.modules.setdefault(\"mitmproxy.io\", _mitmproxy_io)\nsys.modules.setdefault(\"mitmproxy.exceptions\", _mitmproxy_exceptions)\nsys.modules.setdefault(\"mitmproxy.http\", _mitmproxy_http)\n\n# Add workspace root to path so `import export_flows` works\n_WORKSPACE = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\nif _WORKSPACE not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, _WORKSPACE)\n\n# Expose stub classes so tests can reference them\nFAKE_HTTPFlow = _FakeHTTPFlow\nFAKE_FlowReadException = _FakeFlowReadException\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shared helper classes\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass FakeHeaders:\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for mitmproxy Headers with .fields and .get().\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, fields=None):\n        # fields: list of (bytes, bytes) tuples\n        self.fields = fields or []\n        self._map = {k.lower(): v for k, v in self.fields}\n\n    def get(self, key, default=None):\n        if isinstance(key, str):\n            key = key.encode()\n        return self._map.get(key.lower(), default)\n\n    def __setitem__(self, key, value):\n        if isinstance(key, str):\n            key = key.encode()\n        self._map[key.lower()] = value\n        # Update fields list\n        self.fields = [(k, v) if k.lower() != key.lower() else (key, value)\n                       for k, v in self.fields]\n        if key.lower() not in [k.lower() for k, _ in self.fields]:\n            self.fields.append((key, value))\n\n\nclass FakeRequest:\n    def __init__(self, url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\",\n                 body_dict=None, body_text=None, method=\"POST\",\n                 headers=None):\n        self.method = method\n        self.pretty_url = url\n        self.timestamp_start = 1700000000.0\n        if headers is not None:\n            self.headers = headers\n        else:\n            self.headers = FakeHeaders([\n                (b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"),\n            ])\n        if body_text is not None:\n            self._body = body_text\n        elif body_dict is not None:\n            self._body = json.dumps(body_dict)\n        else:\n            self._body = \"\"\n\n    def get_text(self, strict=False):\n        return self._body\n\n\nclass FakeResponse:\n    def __init__(self, text=\"\", status_code=200, reason=\"OK\", headers=None):\n        self.status_code = status_code\n        self.reason = reason\n        self.timestamp_end = 1700000001.5\n        if headers is not None:\n            self.headers = headers\n        else:\n            self.headers = FakeHeaders([(b\"content-type\", b\"text/event-stream\")])\n        self._text = text\n\n    def get_text(self, strict=False):\n        return self._text\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# pytest fixtures\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef ef():\n    \"\"\"Return the export_flows module (imported once for the whole session).\"\"\"\n    import export_flows\n    return export_flows\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef fake_http_flow_class():\n    return _FakeHTTPFlow\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef fake_flow_read_exception():\n    return _FakeFlowReadException\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef make_flow():\n    \"\"\"Factory fixture: returns a function that creates mock HTTPFlow instances.\"\"\"\n    def _make(url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\",\n              body_dict=None, body_text=None,\n              response_text=\"\", has_response=True,\n              method=\"POST\", req_headers=None, resp_headers=None):\n        flow = _FakeHTTPFlow.__new__(_FakeHTTPFlow)\n        flow.request = FakeRequest(url, body_dict=body_dict, body_text=body_text,\n                                   method=method, headers=req_headers)\n        if has_response:\n            flow.response = FakeResponse(response_text, headers=resp_headers)\n        else:\n            flow.response = None\n        return flow\n\n    return _make\n"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GoLpn9xJw6ijfE39aFsS9c","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /workspace/evaluation/usage/conftest.py"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xb1ug6jQFLfgpyW9vbrN89","name":"TaskUpdate","input":{"taskId":"1","status":"completed"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xb1ug6jQFLfgpyW9vbrN89","type":"tool_result","content":"Updated task #1 status"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WxRK1H5D7KVjdUZjFPsF1R","name":"TaskUpdate","input":{"taskId":"2","status":"in_progress"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WxRK1H5D7KVjdUZjFPsF1R","type":"tool_result","content":"Updated task #2 status"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me write the comprehensive test file:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011yHN4diQ9tKhnog8vZWPGb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py","content":"\"\"\"Comprehensive pytest test suite for export_flows.py.\n\nTargets ‚â•80% code coverage. mitmproxy stubs are injected by conftest.py before\nthis module is imported, so `import export_flows` succeeds even without mitmproxy.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock, patch\n\nimport pytest\n\n# conftest.py already set up sys.path and stub modules; import the module under test\n# at module-level so @pytest.mark.parametrize can reference its attributes.\nimport export_flows as _ef\n\n# Pull in conftest helpers for use in test helpers\nfrom conftest import FakeHeaders, FakeRequest, FakeResponse, FAKE_HTTPFlow, FAKE_FlowReadException\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Helpers / builders used across multiple test classes\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"end_turn\", usage=None, extra_lines=\"\"):\n    \"\"\"Build a minimal SSE response string with a message_delta event.\"\"\"\n    if usage is None:\n        usage = {\"input_tokens\": 100, \"output_tokens\": 50,\n                 \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0}\n    delta_payload = json.dumps({\n        \"type\": \"message_delta\",\n        \"delta\": {\"stop_reason\": stop_reason, \"stop_sequence\": None},\n        \"usage\": usage,\n    })\n    return f\"data: {delta_payload}\\n{extra_lines}\"\n\n\ndef make_non_streaming_response(stop_reason=\"end_turn\", usage=None, content=None):\n    \"\"\"Build a minimal non-streaming JSON response.\"\"\"\n    if usage is None:\n        usage = {\"input_tokens\": 100, \"output_tokens\": 50,\n                 \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0}\n    if content is None:\n        content = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hello world\"}]\n    msg = {\n        \"type\": \"message\",\n        \"stop_reason\": stop_reason,\n        \"usage\": usage,\n        \"content\": content,\n        \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5\",\n    }\n    return json.dumps(msg)\n\n\ndef write_files(dirpath, request_body=None, usage=None, response_raw=None):\n    \"\"\"Write request.json, usage.json, response_raw.txt to dirpath.\"\"\"\n    if request_body is not None:\n        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n            json.dump(request_body, f)\n            f.write(\"\\n\")\n    if usage is not None:\n        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n            json.dump(usage, f)\n            f.write(\"\\n\")\n    if response_raw is not None:\n        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n            f.write(response_raw)\n\n\ndef make_sse_stream(text_chunks=None, tool_uses=None):\n    \"\"\"Build SSE stream lines for content blocks.\n\n    text_chunks: list of str ‚Äî will be emitted as text_delta events for block index 0\n    tool_uses: list of (name, input_dict) ‚Äî emitted at subsequent indices\n    \"\"\"\n    lines = []\n    idx = 0\n\n    if text_chunks:\n        lines.append(f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_start\", \"index\": idx, \"content_block\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"\"}})}')\n        for chunk in text_chunks:\n            lines.append(f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_delta\", \"index\": idx, \"delta\": {\"type\": \"text_delta\", \"text\": chunk}})}')\n        lines.append(f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_stop\", \"index\": idx})}')\n        idx += 1\n\n    for (name, input_dict) in (tool_uses or []):\n        partial = json.dumps(input_dict)\n        lines.append(f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_start\", \"index\": idx, \"content_block\": {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": f\"tu_{idx}\", \"name\": name}})}')\n        lines.append(f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_delta\", \"index\": idx, \"delta\": {\"type\": \"input_json_delta\", \"partial_json\": partial}})}')\n        lines.append(f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_stop\", \"index\": idx})}')\n        idx += 1\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestCountWhitespaceStats\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestCountWhitespaceStats:\n    def test_empty_string(self, ef):\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"\")\n        assert r == {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n\n    def test_single_newline(self, ef):\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"\\n\")\n        assert r[\"line_returns_count\"] == 1\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 0\n        assert r[\"total_chars\"] == 1\n\n    def test_double_spaces(self, ef):\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"a  b\")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 1\n\n    def test_triple_spaces(self, ef):\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"a   b\")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 2\n\n    def test_single_space_not_counted(self, ef):\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"a b\")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 0\n\n    def test_multiple_runs_accumulated(self, ef):\n        # Two runs: \"  \" (1 excess) + \"    \" (3 excess) = 4\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"a  b    c\")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 4\n\n    def test_total_chars_accurate(self, ef):\n        text = \"hello\\nworld  test\"\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(text)\n        assert r[\"total_chars\"] == len(text)\n\n    def test_only_spaces(self, ef):\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"     \")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 4\n        assert r[\"line_returns_count\"] == 0\n\n    def test_combined(self, ef):\n        r = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"a\\nb  c\\n  d\")\n        assert r[\"line_returns_count\"] == 3\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 2\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestGetCanonicalModel\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestGetCanonicalModel:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"model_id\", list(_ef.MODEL_PRICING.keys()))\n    def test_exact_match(self, ef, model_id):\n        assert ef.get_canonical_model(model_id) == model_id\n\n    def test_date_suffix_longer_prefix(self, ef):\n        # claude-opus-4-5-20250101 must match claude-opus-4-5, not claude-opus-4\n        result = ef.get_canonical_model(\"claude-opus-4-5-20250101\")\n        assert result == \"claude-opus-4-5\"\n\n    def test_date_suffix_shorter_prefix(self, ef):\n        result = ef.get_canonical_model(\"claude-opus-4-20250101\")\n        assert result == \"claude-opus-4\"\n\n    def test_haiku_with_date(self, ef):\n        result = ef.get_canonical_model(\"claude-haiku-3-5-20241022\")\n        assert result == \"claude-haiku-3-5\"\n\n    def test_unknown_model_returns_none(self, ef):\n        assert ef.get_canonical_model(\"gpt-4\") is None\n\n    def test_empty_string_returns_none(self, ef):\n        assert ef.get_canonical_model(\"\") is None\n\n    def test_partial_match_not_returned(self, ef):\n        # \"claude-opus\" alone doesn't match any key\n        assert ef.get_canonical_model(\"claude-opus\") is None\n\n    def test_sonnet_date_suffix(self, ef):\n        assert ef.get_canonical_model(\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250110\") == \"claude-sonnet-4-5\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestGetPricing\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestGetPricing:\n    def test_known_model_returns_dict(self, ef):\n        p = ef.get_pricing(\"claude-sonnet-4-5\")\n        assert isinstance(p, dict)\n        assert set(p.keys()) == {\"input\", \"cache_write\", \"cache_read\", \"output\"}\n\n    def test_model_with_date_suffix(self, ef):\n        p = ef.get_pricing(\"claude-opus-4-5-20250101\")\n        assert p is not None\n        assert p[\"output\"] == 25e-6\n\n    def test_unknown_model_returns_none(self, ef):\n        assert ef.get_pricing(\"unknown-model\") is None\n\n    def test_all_values_positive(self, ef):\n        for model in ef.MODEL_PRICING:\n            p = ef.get_pricing(model)\n            for v in p.values():\n                assert v > 0\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestSanitizePath\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestSanitizePath:\n    def test_replaces_slashes(self, ef):\n        assert ef.sanitize_path(\"/v1/messages\") == \"v1_messages\"\n\n    def test_strips_query_string(self, ef):\n        assert ef.sanitize_path(\"/path?foo=bar\") == \"path\"\n\n    def test_removes_special_chars(self, ef):\n        result = ef.sanitize_path(\"/v1/messages!\")\n        assert \"!\" not in result\n\n    def test_preserves_alphanumeric_hyphen_underscore(self, ef):\n        result = ef.sanitize_path(\"/api_v2/end-point\")\n        assert result == \"api_v2_end-point\"\n\n    def test_truncates_to_80_chars(self, ef):\n        long_path = \"/a\" * 50  # 100 chars after processing\n        result = ef.sanitize_path(long_path)\n        assert len(result) <= 80\n\n    def test_empty_string(self, ef):\n        result = ef.sanitize_path(\"\")\n        assert result == \"\"\n\n    def test_leading_trailing_underscores_stripped(self, ef):\n        # /v1/ -> _v1_ -> v1\n        result = ef.sanitize_path(\"/v1/\")\n        assert not result.startswith(\"_\")\n        assert not result.endswith(\"_\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestFormatHeaders\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestFormatHeaders:\n    def test_redacts_x_api_key(self, ef):\n        headers = FakeHeaders([\n            (b\"x-api-key\", b\"secret-key\"),\n            (b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"),\n        ])\n        result = ef.format_headers(headers)\n        assert \"[REDACTED]\" in result\n        assert \"secret-key\" not in result\n\n    def test_redacts_authorization(self, ef):\n        headers = FakeHeaders([\n            (b\"authorization\", b\"Bearer token123\"),\n        ])\n        result = ef.format_headers(headers)\n        assert \"[REDACTED]\" in result\n        assert \"token123\" not in result\n\n    def test_preserves_content_type(self, ef):\n        headers = FakeHeaders([\n            (b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"),\n        ])\n        result = ef.format_headers(headers)\n        assert \"application/json\" in result\n\n    def test_multiple_headers_joined_by_newline(self, ef):\n        headers = FakeHeaders([\n            (b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"),\n            (b\"accept\", b\"*/*\"),\n        ])\n        result = ef.format_headers(headers)\n        assert \"\\n\" in result\n\n    def test_empty_headers(self, ef):\n        headers = FakeHeaders([])\n        result = ef.format_headers(headers)\n        assert result == \"\"\n\n    def test_case_insensitive_redaction(self, ef):\n        headers = FakeHeaders([\n            (b\"X-Api-Key\", b\"should-be-redacted\"),\n        ])\n        # The check uses k.lower() so must match\n        result = ef.format_headers(headers)\n        assert \"[REDACTED]\" in result\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestExtractStopReason\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestExtractStopReason:\n    def test_sse_no_space_variant(self, ef):\n        raw = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"}}'\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"end_turn\"\n\n    def test_sse_space_variant(self, ef):\n        raw = 'data: {\"type\": \"message_delta\", \"delta\": {\"stop_reason\": \"tool_use\"}}'\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"tool_use\"\n\n    def test_sse_no_stop_reason_returns_unknown(self, ef):\n        raw = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{}}'\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"unknown\"\n\n    def test_non_streaming_fallback(self, ef):\n        raw = make_non_streaming_response(stop_reason=\"end_turn\")\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"end_turn\"\n\n    def test_non_streaming_multiline(self, ef):\n        raw = \"200 OK\\n\\n\" + make_non_streaming_response(stop_reason=\"end_turn\")\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"end_turn\"\n\n    def test_no_matching_data_returns_unknown(self, ef):\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(\"just some text\") == \"unknown\"\n\n    def test_empty_string_returns_unknown(self, ef):\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(\"\") == \"unknown\"\n\n    def test_malformed_sse_json_skipped(self, ef):\n        raw = \"data: {invalid json}\\ndata: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"message_delta\\\",\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\"}}\"\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"end_turn\"\n\n    def test_sse_priority_over_non_streaming(self, ef):\n        sse = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\"}}\\n'\n        non_streaming = make_non_streaming_response(stop_reason=\"end_turn\")\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(sse + non_streaming) == \"tool_use\"\n\n    def test_non_streaming_wrong_type_skipped(self, ef):\n        # JSON objects with wrong type should be skipped\n        raw = '{\"type\": \"error\", \"stop_reason\": \"end_turn\"}'\n        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"unknown\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestSystemPromptHash\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestSystemPromptHash:\n    def _body(self, system_blocks):\n        return {\"system\": system_blocks}\n\n    def test_cc_uses_index_2(self, ef):\n        blocks = [\n            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"block0\"},\n            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"block1\"},\n            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"target_block\"},\n        ]\n        result = ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(blocks), \"cc\")\n        expected = hashlib.sha256(\"target_block\".encode()).hexdigest()[:12]\n        assert result == expected\n\n    def test_vix_uses_index_0(self, ef):\n        blocks = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"vix_prompt\"}]\n        result = ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(blocks), \"vix\")\n        expected = hashlib.sha256(\"vix_prompt\".encode()).hexdigest()[:12]\n        assert result == expected\n\n    def test_unknown_agent_defaults_to_index_0(self, ef):\n        blocks = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"default_prompt\"}]\n        result = ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(blocks), \"other_agent\")\n        expected = hashlib.sha256(\"default_prompt\".encode()).hexdigest()[:12]\n        assert result == expected\n\n    def test_index_out_of_bounds_returns_none(self, ef):\n        # cc uses index 2; if system has only 1 block -> None\n        blocks = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"only_one\"}]\n        assert ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(blocks), \"cc\") is None\n\n    def test_no_system_key_returns_none(self, ef):\n        assert ef._system_prompt_hash({\"messages\": []}, \"cc\") is None\n\n    def test_empty_system_list_returns_none(self, ef):\n        assert ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body([]), \"vix\") is None\n\n    def test_empty_text_returns_none(self, ef):\n        blocks = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"\"}]\n        assert ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(blocks), \"vix\") is None\n\n    def test_returns_12_char_hex(self, ef):\n        blocks = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"some prompt text\"}]\n        result = ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(blocks), \"vix\")\n        assert result is not None\n        assert len(result) == 12\n        assert all(c in \"0123456789abcdef\" for c in result)\n\n    def test_deterministic(self, ef):\n        blocks = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"deterministic\"}]\n        r1 = ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(blocks), \"vix\")\n        r2 = ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(blocks), \"vix\")\n        assert r1 == r2\n\n    def test_different_texts_different_hashes(self, ef):\n        b1 = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"prompt_a\"}]\n        b2 = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"prompt_b\"}]\n        assert ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(b1), \"vix\") != ef._system_prompt_hash(self._body(b2), \"vix\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestResolveReadFileName\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestResolveReadFileName:\n    def test_read_file_compress_mode(self, ef):\n        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {\"mode\": \"compress\"}) == \"read_file_compressed\"\n\n    def test_read_file_original_mode(self, ef):\n        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {\"mode\": \"original\"}) == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n\n    def test_read_file_no_mode_key(self, ef):\n        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {}) == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n\n    def test_read_file_non_dict_input(self, ef):\n        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", None) == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n\n    def test_other_names_passthrough(self, ef):\n        for name in (\"Write\", \"Read\", \"edit_file\", \"Bash\"):\n            assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(name, {}) == name\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestFormatToolParams\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestFormatToolParams:\n    def test_string_value_quoted(self, ef):\n        result = ef._format_tool_params({\"key\": \"value\"})\n        assert result == 'key=\"value\"'\n\n    def test_non_string_json_dumped(self, ef):\n        result = ef._format_tool_params({\"count\": 42})\n        assert result == \"count=42\"\n\n    def test_empty_dict(self, ef):\n        assert ef._format_tool_params({}) == \"\"\n\n    def test_multiple_params(self, ef):\n        result = ef._format_tool_params({\"a\": \"x\", \"b\": 1})\n        assert 'a=\"x\"' in result\n        assert \"b=1\" in result\n        assert \", \" in result\n\n    def test_bool_value(self, ef):\n        result = ef._format_tool_params({\"flag\": True})\n        assert \"true\" in result.lower()\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestGetFilePath\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestGetFilePath:\n    def test_file_path_key_absolute(self, ef):\n        result = ef._get_file_path({\"file_path\": \"/absolute/path/file.py\"})\n        assert result == \"/absolute/path/file.py\"\n\n    def test_path_key_fallback(self, ef):\n        result = ef._get_file_path({\"path\": \"/some/path/file.py\"})\n        assert result == \"/some/path/file.py\"\n\n    def test_relative_path_made_absolute(self, ef):\n        result = ef._get_file_path({\"file_path\": \"relative/file.py\"})\n        assert os.path.isabs(result)\n        assert result.endswith(\"relative/file.py\")\n\n    def test_empty_dict_returns_none(self, ef):\n        assert ef._get_file_path({}) is None\n\n    def test_non_dict_returns_none(self, ef):\n        assert ef._get_file_path(None) is None\n        assert ef._get_file_path(\"string\") is None\n\n    def test_none_file_path_returns_none(self, ef):\n        assert ef._get_file_path({\"file_path\": None, \"path\": None}) is None\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestParseRequestBody\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestParseRequestBody:\n    def test_valid_json_returns_dict(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        p = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n        p.write_text(json.dumps({\"model\": \"test\", \"messages\": []}))\n        result = ef.parse_request_body(str(p))\n        assert result == {\"model\": \"test\", \"messages\": []}\n\n    def test_invalid_json_returns_none(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        p = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n        p.write_text(\"{not valid json}\")\n        assert ef.parse_request_body(str(p)) is None\n\n    def test_empty_braces_valid(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        p = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n        p.write_text(\"{}\")\n        assert ef.parse_request_body(str(p)) == {}\n\n    def test_file_not_found_raises(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        with pytest.raises(FileNotFoundError):\n            ef.parse_request_body(str(tmp_path / \"nonexistent.json\"))\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestWriteRequest\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestWriteRequest:\n    def test_creates_request_headers_txt(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(url=\"https://api.example.com/v1/test\", body_dict={\"k\": \"v\"})\n        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        assert (tmp_path / \"request_headers.txt\").exists()\n\n    def test_header_file_starts_with_method_url(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(url=\"https://api.example.com/v1/test\", method=\"POST\")\n        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"request_headers.txt\").read_text()\n        assert content.startswith(\"POST https://api.example.com/v1/test\")\n\n    def test_x_api_key_redacted_in_headers(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        headers = FakeHeaders([\n            (b\"x-api-key\", b\"super-secret\"),\n            (b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"),\n        ])\n        flow = make_flow(req_headers=headers, body_dict={})\n        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"request_headers.txt\").read_text()\n        assert \"[REDACTED]\" in content\n        assert \"super-secret\" not in content\n\n    def test_valid_json_body_pretty_printed(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(body_dict={\"key\": \"value\", \"num\": 42})\n        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"request.json\").read_text()\n        parsed = json.loads(content)\n        assert parsed == {\"key\": \"value\", \"num\": 42}\n        # Pretty-printed: should have indentation\n        assert \"  \" in content\n\n    def test_invalid_json_body_written_raw(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(body_text=\"not_json_body\")\n        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"request.json\").read_text()\n        assert \"not_json_body\" in content\n\n    def test_empty_body_no_request_json(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(body_text=\"\")\n        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (tmp_path / \"request.json\").exists()\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestWriteResponse\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestWriteResponse:\n    def test_creates_response_raw_txt(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(response_text=\"response body\")\n        ef.write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        assert (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").exists()\n\n    def test_none_response_no_file(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(has_response=False)\n        ef.write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").exists()\n\n    def test_status_code_on_first_line(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(response_text=\"body text\")\n        ef.write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").read_text()\n        assert content.startswith(\"200 OK\")\n\n    def test_response_body_included(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(response_text=\"actual body content\")\n        ef.write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").read_text()\n        assert \"actual body content\" in content\n\n    def test_empty_response_body(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow = make_flow(response_text=\"\")\n        ef.write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").read_text()\n        assert content.startswith(\"200 OK\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestExtractReadFileWhitespace\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestExtractReadFileWhitespace:\n    def _body_with_read(self, tool_use_id, tool_name, result_content, mode=None):\n        inp = {\"file_path\": \"/test.py\"}\n        if mode:\n            inp[\"mode\"] = mode\n        return {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": tool_use_id,\n                         \"name\": tool_name, \"input\": inp}\n                    ],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": tool_use_id,\n                         \"content\": result_content}\n                    ],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n\n    def test_read_file_string_content(self, ef):\n        text = \"hello\\nworld  test\"\n        body = self._body_with_read(\"id1\", \"read_file\", text)\n        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        expected = ef.count_whitespace_stats(text)\n        assert ws == expected\n\n    def test_read_file_list_content(self, ef):\n        text = \"line1\\nline2\"\n        body = self._body_with_read(\"id1\", \"read_file\",\n                                    [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text}])\n        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        expected = ef.count_whitespace_stats(text)\n        assert ws == expected\n\n    def test_ignores_non_read_tools(self, ef):\n        body = self._body_with_read(\"id1\", \"Write\", \"some content\")\n        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == 0\n\n    def test_read_file_compressed_tool(self, ef):\n        text = \"compressed content\\n\"\n        body = self._body_with_read(\"id1\", \"read_file\", text, mode=\"compress\")\n        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == len(text)\n\n    def test_Read_tool_name(self, ef):\n        text = \"Read tool result\"\n        body = self._body_with_read(\"id1\", \"Read\", text)\n        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == len(text)\n\n    def test_accumulates_multiple_reads(self, ef):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"id1\", \"name\": \"read_file\",\n                         \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/a.py\"}},\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"id2\", \"name\": \"read_file\",\n                         \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/b.py\"}},\n                    ],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"id1\",\n                         \"content\": \"aaa\"},\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"id2\",\n                         \"content\": \"bb\"},\n                    ],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == 5  # \"aaa\" + \"bb\"\n\n    def test_empty_messages(self, ef):\n        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace({\"messages\": []})\n        assert ws == {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestCategorizeInputSources\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestCategorizeInputSources:\n    def _multi_turn_body(self):\n        \"\"\"3 messages: user0 (tool_result), assistant1 (tool_use), user2 (tool_result - LAST).\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"early_id\",\n                         \"content\": \"early result text\"}\n                    ],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"new_id\", \"name\": \"Read\",\n                         \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/x.py\"}}\n                    ],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"new_id\",\n                         \"content\": \"last user result text\"}\n                    ],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n\n    def test_last_user_message_is_cache_write(self, ef):\n        body = self._multi_turn_body()\n        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n        # \"new_id\" -> Read tool; last user msg -> cache_write\n        read_tr = result[\"tool_results\"].get(\"Read\", {})\n        assert read_tr.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0) > 0\n        assert read_tr.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0) == 0\n\n    def test_earlier_user_messages_are_cache_read(self, ef):\n        body = self._multi_turn_body()\n        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n        unknown_tr = result[\"tool_results\"].get(\"unknown\", {})\n        assert unknown_tr.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0) > 0\n        assert unknown_tr.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0) == 0\n\n    def test_second_to_last_assistant_tool_use_is_cache_write(self, ef):\n        # 5-message: user, assistant(early), user, assistant(second-to-last), user(last)\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"},\n                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"early\", \"name\": \"Write\",\n                     \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/f.py\"}}\n                ]},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"early\", \"content\": \"ok\"}\n                ]},\n                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"recent\", \"name\": \"Read\",\n                     \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/g.py\"}}\n                ]},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"recent\", \"content\": \"ok2\"}\n                ]},\n            ]\n        }\n        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n        # second-to-last assistant (index 3) -> cache_write for tool_use\n        read_tc = result[\"tool_calls\"].get(\"Read\", {})\n        assert read_tc.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0) > 0\n\n    def test_earlier_assistant_tool_use_is_cache_read(self, ef):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"},\n                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"early\", \"name\": \"Write\",\n                     \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/f.py\"}}\n                ]},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"early\", \"content\": \"ok\"}\n                ]},\n                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"recent\", \"name\": \"Read\",\n                     \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/g.py\"}}\n                ]},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"recent\", \"content\": \"ok2\"}\n                ]},\n            ]\n        }\n        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n        # early assistant (index 1) -> cache_read for tool_use\n        write_tc = result[\"tool_calls\"].get(\"Write\", {})\n        assert write_tc.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0) > 0\n\n    def test_total_chars_equals_json_dumps(self, ef):\n        body = self._multi_turn_body()\n        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n        assert result[\"total_chars\"] == len(json.dumps(body))\n\n    def test_empty_messages(self, ef):\n        body = {\"messages\": []}\n        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n        assert result[\"tool_results\"] == {}\n        assert result[\"tool_calls\"] == {}\n\n    def test_non_list_content_skipped(self, ef):\n        # String content in user message should not crash\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"plain string\"},\n            ]\n        }\n        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n        assert result[\"tool_results\"] == {}\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestCategorizeOutputSources\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestCategorizeOutputSources:\n    def test_sse_text_block(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(text_chunks=[\"Hello \", \"world\"])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(sse)\n        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == len(\"Hello world\")\n\n    def test_sse_tool_use_block(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(tool_uses=[(\"Write\", {\"file_path\": \"/out.py\", \"content\": \"x\"})])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(sse)\n        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n        assert \"Write\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n        assert result[\"tool_calls\"][\"Write\"] > 0\n\n    def test_sse_mixed_blocks(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(\n            text_chunks=[\"some text\"],\n            tool_uses=[(\"Read\", {\"file_path\": \"/f.py\"})]\n        )\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(sse)\n        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == len(\"some text\")\n        assert \"read_file_uncompressed\" in result[\"tool_calls\"] or \"Read\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n\n    def test_non_streaming_fallback_text(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        raw = make_non_streaming_response(content=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"hello world\"}])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(raw)\n        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == len(\"hello world\")\n\n    def test_non_streaming_fallback_tool_use(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        raw = make_non_streaming_response(content=[\n            {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": \"Write\",\n             \"id\": \"tu1\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/f.py\", \"content\": \"abc\"}}\n        ])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(raw)\n        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n        assert \"Write\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n\n    def test_empty_file(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(\"\")\n        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == 0\n        assert result[\"tool_calls\"] == {}\n\n    def test_read_file_tool_name_resolved(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        # read_file with compress mode -> resolved to read_file_compressed\n        sse = make_sse_stream(\n            tool_uses=[(\"read_file\", {\"file_path\": \"/f.py\", \"mode\": \"compress\"})]\n        )\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(sse)\n        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n        assert \"read_file_compressed\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestParseResponseContent\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestParseResponseContent:\n    def test_sse_text_block_assembled(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(text_chunks=[\"Hello \", \"world!\"])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(sse)\n        blocks = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n        text_blocks = [b for b in blocks if b[\"type\"] == \"text\"]\n        assert len(text_blocks) == 1\n        assert text_blocks[0][\"text\"] == \"Hello world!\"\n\n    def test_sse_tool_use_input_assembled(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        inp = {\"file_path\": \"/test.py\", \"content\": \"code\"}\n        sse = make_sse_stream(tool_uses=[(\"Write\", inp)])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(sse)\n        blocks = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n        tool_blocks = [b for b in blocks if b[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\"]\n        assert len(tool_blocks) == 1\n        assert tool_blocks[0][\"name\"] == \"Write\"\n        assert tool_blocks[0][\"input\"] == inp\n\n    def test_sse_invalid_json_input_returns_empty_dict(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        idx = 0\n        lines = [\n            f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_start\", \"index\": idx, \"content_block\": {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"t1\", \"name\": \"Write\"}})}',\n            f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_delta\", \"index\": idx, \"delta\": {\"type\": \"input_json_delta\", \"partial_json\": \"{invalid\"}})}',\n            f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"content_block_stop\", \"index\": idx})}',\n        ]\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n        blocks = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n        tool_blocks = [b for b in blocks if b[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\"]\n        assert tool_blocks[0][\"input\"] == {}\n\n    def test_non_streaming_text_block(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        raw = make_non_streaming_response(content=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"plain text\"}])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(raw)\n        blocks = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n        assert any(b[\"type\"] == \"text\" and b[\"text\"] == \"plain text\" for b in blocks)\n\n    def test_non_streaming_tool_use(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        raw = make_non_streaming_response(content=[\n            {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": \"Edit\", \"id\": \"tu1\",\n             \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/f.py\", \"new_string\": \"x\"}}\n        ])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(raw)\n        blocks = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n        assert any(b[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\" and b[\"name\"] == \"Edit\" for b in blocks)\n\n    def test_empty_sse_returns_empty(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(\"\")\n        blocks = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n        assert blocks == []\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestExportParsedResponse\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestExportParsedResponse:\n    def test_returns_true_on_success(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(text_chunks=[\"Hello\"])\n        inp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        inp.write_text(sse)\n        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n        assert ef.export_parsed_response(str(inp), str(out)) is True\n\n    def test_returns_false_on_no_blocks(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        inp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        inp.write_text(\"\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n        assert ef.export_parsed_response(str(inp), str(out)) is False\n\n    def test_text_block_written_asis(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(text_chunks=[\"Some output text\"])\n        inp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        inp.write_text(sse)\n        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n        ef.export_parsed_response(str(inp), str(out))\n        assert \"Some output text\" in out.read_text()\n\n    def test_tool_use_formatted_with_brackets(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(tool_uses=[(\"Write\", {\"file_path\": \"/f.py\"})])\n        inp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        inp.write_text(sse)\n        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n        ef.export_parsed_response(str(inp), str(out))\n        content = out.read_text()\n        assert \"[Write(\" in content\n        assert \")]\" in content\n\n    def test_tool_use_params_included(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(tool_uses=[(\"Write\", {\"file_path\": \"/my/file.py\"})])\n        inp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        inp.write_text(sse)\n        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n        ef.export_parsed_response(str(inp), str(out))\n        content = out.read_text()\n        assert \"/my/file.py\" in content\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestAttributeTokens\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestAttributeTokens:\n    def _pricing(self):\n        return {\"input\": 3e-6, \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6, \"output\": 15e-6}\n\n    def _usage(self, input_tokens=1000, cache_write=200, cache_read=500, output_tokens=100):\n        return {\n            \"cost\": {\n                \"input\": {\"tokens\": input_tokens, \"dollars\": input_tokens * 3e-6},\n                \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": cache_write, \"dollars\": cache_write * 3.75e-6},\n                \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": cache_read, \"dollars\": cache_read * 0.30e-6},\n                \"output\": {\"tokens\": output_tokens, \"dollars\": output_tokens * 15e-6},\n                \"total\": {\"tokens\": input_tokens + cache_write + cache_read + output_tokens,\n                          \"dollars\": 0.0},\n            }\n        }\n\n    def test_zero_total_chars_empty_input(self, ef):\n        result = ef.attribute_tokens(\n            {\"total_chars\": 0, \"tool_results\": {}, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n            {\"llm_text\": 100, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n            self._usage(),\n            self._pricing(),\n        )\n        assert result[\"input\"] == {}\n\n    def test_zero_output_tokens_empty_output(self, ef):\n        result = ef.attribute_tokens(\n            {\"total_chars\": 1000, \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 100, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}}, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n            {\"llm_text\": 0, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n            self._usage(output_tokens=0),\n            self._pricing(),\n        )\n        assert result[\"output\"] == {}\n\n    def test_none_pricing_empty_input(self, ef):\n        result = ef.attribute_tokens(\n            {\"total_chars\": 1000, \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 500, \"cache_read_chars\": 500}}, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n            {\"llm_text\": 100, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n            self._usage(),\n            None,\n        )\n        assert result[\"input\"] == {}\n\n    def test_proportional_output_attribution(self, ef):\n        output_sources = {\"llm_text\": 500, \"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": 500}}\n        usage = self._usage(output_tokens=100)\n        result = ef.attribute_tokens(\n            {\"total_chars\": 1000, \"tool_results\": {}, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n            output_sources,\n            usage,\n            self._pricing(),\n        )\n        # 50/50 split\n        llm = result[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"]\n        assert llm[\"tokens\"] == 50\n        assert llm[\"chars\"] == 500\n\n    def test_output_total_in_tool_calls(self, ef):\n        output_sources = {\"llm_text\": 100, \"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": 900}}\n        usage = self._usage(output_tokens=100)\n        result = ef.attribute_tokens(\n            {\"total_chars\": 1000, \"tool_results\": {}, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n            output_sources,\n            usage,\n            self._pricing(),\n        )\n        assert \"__total\" in result[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"]\n\n    def test_input_tool_results_attributed(self, ef):\n        input_sources = {\n            \"total_chars\": 1000,\n            \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 500, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}},\n            \"tool_calls\": {},\n        }\n        result = ef.attribute_tokens(input_sources, {\"llm_text\": 0, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n                                     self._usage(), self._pricing())\n        assert \"tool_results\" in result[\"input\"]\n        assert \"Read\" in result[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"]\n        assert result[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"chars\"] == 500\n\n    def test_input_tool_calls_attributed(self, ef):\n        input_sources = {\n            \"total_chars\": 1000,\n            \"tool_results\": {},\n            \"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 200, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}},\n        }\n        result = ef.attribute_tokens(input_sources, {\"llm_text\": 0, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n                                     self._usage(), self._pricing())\n        assert \"tool_calls\" in result[\"input\"]\n        assert \"Write\" in result[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"]\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestAggregateBySource\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestAggregateBySource:\n    def _empty_agg(self):\n        return {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n\n    def test_first_call_initializes_keys(self, ef):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        flow = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"tokens\": 10, \"dollars\": 0.001, \"chars\": 100}}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"tokens\"] == 10\n\n    def test_accumulates_on_second_call(self, ef):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        flow = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"tokens\": 10, \"dollars\": 0.001, \"chars\": 100}}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"tokens\"] == 20\n\n    def test_skips_non_dict_entries(self, ef):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        flow = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"bad\": \"not_a_dict\"}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n        assert \"bad\" not in agg[\"input\"].get(\"tool_results\", {})\n\n    def test_output_llm_text(self, ef):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        flow = {\n            \"input\": {},\n            \"output\": {\"llm_text\": {\"tokens\": 50, \"dollars\": 0.0005, \"chars\": 200}},\n        }\n        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n        assert agg[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"][\"tokens\"] == 50\n\n    def test_output_tool_calls(self, ef):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        flow = {\n            \"input\": {},\n            \"output\": {\"tool_calls\": {\n                \"__total\": {\"tokens\": 20, \"dollars\": 0.0002, \"chars\": 100},\n                \"Write\": {\"tokens\": 20, \"dollars\": 0.0002, \"chars\": 100},\n            }},\n        }\n        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n        assert \"tool_calls\" in agg[\"output\"]\n        assert \"Write\" in agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"]\n\n    def test_empty_flow_by_source(self, ef):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}})\n        assert agg == {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestRoundBySource\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestRoundBySource:\n    def test_rounds_input_tool_results_dollars(self, ef):\n        agg = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"tokens\": 10, \"dollars\": 0.00000012345, \"chars\": 5}}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        ef._round_by_source(agg)\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.00000012345, 6)\n\n    def test_rounds_output_llm_text_dollars(self, ef):\n        agg = {\n            \"input\": {},\n            \"output\": {\"llm_text\": {\"tokens\": 50, \"dollars\": 0.00000056789, \"chars\": 100}},\n        }\n        ef._round_by_source(agg)\n        assert agg[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.00000056789, 6)\n\n    def test_rounds_output_tool_calls_dollars(self, ef):\n        agg = {\n            \"input\": {},\n            \"output\": {\"tool_calls\": {\n                \"Write\": {\"tokens\": 5, \"dollars\": 0.00000099999, \"chars\": 50}\n            }},\n        }\n        ef._round_by_source(agg)\n        assert agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][\"Write\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.00000099999, 6)\n\n    def test_empty_agg_no_error(self, ef):\n        ef._round_by_source({\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}})  # Should not raise\n\n    def test_six_decimal_places(self, ef):\n        agg = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": {\"tokens\": 1, \"dollars\": 1.123456789, \"chars\": 1}}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        ef._round_by_source(agg)\n        v = agg[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"][\"Write\"][\"dollars\"]\n        assert len(str(v).split(\".\")[-1]) <= 6\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestAgentColor\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestAgentColor:\n    def test_returns_hash_prefix(self, ef):\n        result = ef._agent_color(\"my_agent\")\n        assert result.startswith(\"#\")\n        assert len(result) == 7\n\n    def test_deterministic(self, ef):\n        assert ef._agent_color(\"test\") == ef._agent_color(\"test\")\n\n    def test_different_names_different_colors(self, ef):\n        assert ef._agent_color(\"agent_a\") != ef._agent_color(\"agent_b\")\n\n    def test_format_valid_hex(self, ef):\n        result = ef._agent_color(\"anything\")\n        hex_part = result[1:]\n        int(hex_part, 16)  # should not raise\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestRedactFlowFiles\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestRedactFlowFiles:\n    def test_no_flow_files_no_op(self, ef, tmp_path, capsys):\n        ef.redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))\n        # Should return without error and print 0\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        assert \"0\" in out\n\n    def test_redacts_x_api_key(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        # Create a fake .flow file\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"test.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n\n        # Build a mock flow with x-api-key header\n        mock_flow = FAKE_HTTPFlow.__new__(FAKE_HTTPFlow)\n        headers = FakeHeaders([\n            (b\"x-api-key\", b\"my-secret-key\"),\n        ])\n        mock_flow.request = FakeRequest(headers=headers)\n\n        written_flows = []\n\n        class CapturingWriter:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def add(self, flow):\n                written_flows.append(flow)\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self):\n                return iter([mock_flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader), \\\n             patch.object(ef, \"FlowWriter\", CapturingWriter):\n            ef.redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))\n\n        assert len(written_flows) == 1\n        assert mock_flow.request.headers.get(b\"x-api-key\") == \"[REDACTED]\"\n\n    def test_unmodified_flow_not_rewritten(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"clean.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n\n        mock_flow = FAKE_HTTPFlow.__new__(FAKE_HTTPFlow)\n        mock_flow.request = FakeRequest(headers=FakeHeaders([(b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\")]))\n\n        written_flows = []\n\n        class CapturingWriter:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def add(self, flow):\n                written_flows.append(flow)\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self):\n                return iter([mock_flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader), \\\n             patch.object(ef, \"FlowWriter\", CapturingWriter):\n            ef.redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))\n\n        # File not rewritten since nothing was modified\n        assert len(written_flows) == 0\n\n    def test_flow_read_exception_skipped(self, ef, tmp_path, capsys):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"bad.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"bad data\")\n\n        class FailingReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self):\n                raise FAKE_FlowReadException(\"corrupt\")\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", FailingReader):\n            ef.redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))  # Should not raise\n\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        assert \"Skipping\" in out\n\n    def test_non_http_flow_not_modified(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"test.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n\n        # A non-HTTPFlow object\n        non_http = object()\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self):\n                return iter([non_http])\n\n        class CapturingWriter:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def add(self, flow):\n                pass\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader), \\\n             patch.object(ef, \"FlowWriter\", CapturingWriter):\n            ef.redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))  # Should not raise\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestExportFlows\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestExportFlows:\n    def _make_mock_reader(self, flows):\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter(flows)\n        return MockReader\n\n    def test_no_flow_files_prints_message(self, ef, tmp_path, capsys):\n        ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(tmp_path))\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        assert \"No\" in out or \"0\" in out\n\n    def test_count_token_url_skipped(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        skipped_flow = make_flow(url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/count_token\",\n                                  body_dict={\"messages\": []})\n        normal_flow = make_flow(url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\",\n                                 body_dict={\"messages\": []},\n                                 response_text=make_sse_response())\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter([skipped_flow, normal_flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        vix_dir = out_dir / \"vix\"\n        # only normal_flow should be written -> step 1, req 1\n        assert (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"1\" / \"request_headers.txt\").exists()\n        # No step-1/req-2 or higher from skipped flow\n        assert not (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"2\").exists()\n\n    def test_quota_message_skipped(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        quota_flow = make_flow(\n            body_dict={\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"quota\"}]},\n            # no \"system\" key -> quota check triggers\n        )\n        normal_flow = make_flow(\n            body_dict={\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"real\"}]},\n            response_text=make_sse_response(),\n        )\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter([quota_flow, normal_flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        vix_dir = out_dir / \"vix\"\n        assert (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"1\").exists()\n        assert not (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"2\").exists()\n\n    def test_quota_with_system_not_skipped(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        # Has both \"quota\" content AND a system key -> should NOT be skipped\n        quota_with_system = make_flow(\n            body_dict={\n                \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"quota\"}],\n                \"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"sys prompt\"}],\n            },\n            response_text=make_sse_response(),\n        )\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter([quota_with_system])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        vix_dir = out_dir / \"vix\"\n        assert (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"1\").exists()\n\n    def test_creates_flow_directory_structure(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        flow = make_flow(\n            body_dict={\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hello\"}]},\n            response_text=make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"tool_use\"),\n        )\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter([flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        vix_dir = out_dir / \"vix\"\n        assert (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"1\" / \"request_headers.txt\").exists()\n        assert (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"1\" / \"timing.json\").exists()\n\n    def test_writes_timing_json(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        flow = make_flow(\n            body_dict={\"messages\": []},\n            response_text=make_sse_response(),\n        )\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter([flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        timing_file = out_dir / \"vix\" / \"1\" / \"1\" / \"timing.json\"\n        timing = json.loads(timing_file.read_text())\n        assert \"request_start\" in timing\n\n    def test_none_response_handled(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        flow = make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": []}, has_response=False)\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter([flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        timing_file = out_dir / \"vix\" / \"1\" / \"1\" / \"timing.json\"\n        timing = json.loads(timing_file.read_text())\n        assert \"response_end\" not in timing\n\n    def test_vix_step_increments_on_end_turn(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        # Flow 1: tool_use -> step 1, req 1, then req++\n        # Flow 2: end_turn -> step 1, req 2, then step++, req=1\n        # Flow 3: tool_use -> step 2, req 1\n        flows = [\n            make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": []},\n                      response_text=make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"tool_use\")),\n            make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": []},\n                      response_text=make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"end_turn\")),\n            make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": []},\n                      response_text=make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"tool_use\")),\n        ]\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter(flows)\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        vix_dir = out_dir / \"vix\"\n        assert (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"1\").exists()\n        assert (vix_dir / \"1\" / \"2\").exists()\n        assert (vix_dir / \"2\" / \"1\").exists()\n\n    def test_cc_step_increments_on_hash_change(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"cc.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        def sys_blocks(text):\n            # cc uses index 2, so we need 3 blocks\n            return [\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"b0\"},\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"b1\"},\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text},\n            ]\n\n        flows = [\n            make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": [], \"system\": sys_blocks(\"promptA\")},\n                      response_text=make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"tool_use\")),\n            make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": [], \"system\": sys_blocks(\"promptA\")},\n                      response_text=make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"tool_use\")),\n            make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": [], \"system\": sys_blocks(\"promptB\")},\n                      response_text=make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"tool_use\")),\n        ]\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter(flows)\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        cc_dir = out_dir / \"cc\"\n        assert (cc_dir / \"1\" / \"1\").exists()\n        assert (cc_dir / \"1\" / \"2\").exists()\n        # promptB is different -> step 2\n        assert (cc_dir / \"2\" / \"1\").exists()\n\n    def test_cc_first_flow_no_step_increment(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"cc.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        sys_blocks = [\n            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"b0\"},\n            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"b1\"},\n            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"promptA\"},\n        ]\n        flow = make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": [], \"system\": sys_blocks},\n                          response_text=make_sse_response(stop_reason=\"tool_use\"))\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter([flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        cc_dir = out_dir / \"cc\"\n        # First flow always goes to step 1\n        assert (cc_dir / \"1\" / \"1\").exists()\n        assert not (cc_dir / \"2\").exists()\n\n    def test_flow_read_exception_skipped(self, ef, tmp_path, capsys):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"bad.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"bad data\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        class FailingReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                raise FAKE_FlowReadException(\"read error\")\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", FailingReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))  # Should not raise\n\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        assert \"Skipping\" in out\n\n    def test_non_http_flow_skipped(self, ef, tmp_path, make_flow):\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"placeholder\")\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        out_dir.mkdir()\n\n        non_http = object()\n        normal_flow = make_flow(body_dict={\"messages\": []},\n                                 response_text=make_sse_response())\n\n        class MockReader:\n            def __init__(self, f):\n                pass\n            def stream(self_inner):\n                return iter([non_http, normal_flow])\n\n        with patch.object(ef, \"FlowReader\", MockReader):\n            ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        # Only normal_flow exported\n        assert (out_dir / \"vix\" / \"1\" / \"1\").exists()\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestExtractUsage\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestExtractUsage:\n    def _setup_flow_dir(self, base, step=\"1\", req=\"1\"):\n        d = base / step / req\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        return d\n\n    def test_sse_usage_extracted(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup_flow_dir(tmp_path)\n        usage_data = {\"input_tokens\": 100, \"output_tokens\": 50,\n                      \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 20, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 30}\n        (d / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(make_sse_response(usage=usage_data))\n        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert usage[\"input_tokens\"] == 100\n        assert usage[\"output_tokens\"] == 50\n\n    def test_token_fields_filtered(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup_flow_dir(tmp_path)\n        usage_data = {\"input_tokens\": 100, \"output_tokens\": 50,\n                      \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0,\n                      \"unknown_field\": 999}\n        (d / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(make_sse_response(usage=usage_data))\n        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"unknown_field\" not in usage\n\n    def test_timing_merged_and_file_deleted(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup_flow_dir(tmp_path)\n        usage_data = {\"input_tokens\": 10, \"output_tokens\": 5,\n                      \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0}\n        (d / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(make_sse_response(usage=usage_data))\n        timing = {\"request_start\": 1700000000.0, \"response_end\": 1700000001.5}\n        (d / \"timing.json\").write_text(json.dumps(timing))\n\n        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n\n        assert not (d / \"timing.json\").exists()\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"timing\" in usage\n        assert usage[\"timing\"][\"duration_ms\"] == round((1700000001.5 - 1700000000.0) * 1000)\n\n    def test_non_streaming_fallback(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup_flow_dir(tmp_path)\n        raw = make_non_streaming_response(\n            usage={\"input_tokens\": 200, \"output_tokens\": 100,\n                   \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0}\n        )\n        (d / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(raw)\n        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert usage[\"input_tokens\"] == 200\n\n    def test_no_usage_found_warning(self, ef, tmp_path, capsys):\n        d = self._setup_flow_dir(tmp_path)\n        (d / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(\"no useful data here\")\n        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (d / \"usage.json\").exists()\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        assert \"Warning\" in out\n\n    def test_sse_space_variant(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup_flow_dir(tmp_path)\n        usage_data = {\"input_tokens\": 77, \"output_tokens\": 33,\n                      \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0}\n        payload = json.dumps({\n            \"type\": \"message_delta\",\n            \"delta\": {\"stop_reason\": \"end_turn\"},\n            \"usage\": usage_data,\n        })\n        # Use space variant: \"type\": \"message_delta\"\n        payload_spaced = payload.replace('\"type\":\"message_delta\"', '\"type\": \"message_delta\"')\n        (d / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(f\"data: {payload_spaced}\\n\")\n        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert usage[\"input_tokens\"] == 77\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestExtractPrompts\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestExtractPrompts:\n    def _setup(self, base, body):\n        d = base / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        (d / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n        return d\n\n    def test_extracts_system_prompt(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"You are helpful.\"}],\n            \"messages\": [],\n        }\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, body)\n        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        assert (d / \"system_prompt.md\").read_text() == \"You are helpful.\"\n\n    def test_extracts_first_user_message(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hello AI\"}]},\n            ]\n        }\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, body)\n        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        assert (d / \"first_user_message.md\").read_text() == \"Hello AI\"\n\n    def test_system_prompt_concatenates_text_blocks(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"system\": [\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Part one.\"},\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Part two.\"},\n            ],\n            \"messages\": [],\n        }\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, body)\n        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        content = (d / \"system_prompt.md\").read_text()\n        assert \"Part one.\" in content\n        assert \"Part two.\" in content\n\n    def test_skips_non_text_system_blocks(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"system\": [\n                {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"text\": \"should be ignored\"},\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"valid text\"},\n            ],\n            \"messages\": [],\n        }\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, body)\n        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        content = (d / \"system_prompt.md\").read_text()\n        assert \"valid text\" in content\n        assert \"should be ignored\" not in content\n\n    def test_invalid_request_json_warning(self, ef, tmp_path, capsys):\n        d = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        (d / \"request.json\").write_text(\"{invalid json}\")\n        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        assert \"Warning\" in out\n\n    def test_string_user_content_no_file(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"plain string\"},\n            ]\n        }\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, body)\n        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (d / \"first_user_message.md\").exists()\n\n    def test_only_first_user_message_extracted(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"First msg\"}]},\n                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Reply\"}]},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Second msg\"}]},\n            ]\n        }\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, body)\n        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        content = (d / \"first_user_message.md\").read_text()\n        assert content == \"First msg\"\n        assert \"Second msg\" not in content\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestCalculateCosts\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestCalculateCosts:\n    def _setup(self, base, model, tokens):\n        d = base / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        body = {\"model\": model, \"messages\": []}\n        (d / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n        usage = {\n            \"input_tokens\": tokens.get(\"input\", 0),\n            \"output_tokens\": tokens.get(\"output\", 0),\n            \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": tokens.get(\"cache_write\", 0),\n            \"cache_read_input_tokens\": tokens.get(\"cache_read\", 0),\n        }\n        (d / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps(usage))\n        return d\n\n    def test_computes_all_cost_fields(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, \"claude-sonnet-4-5\",\n                        {\"input\": 1000, \"output\": 500, \"cache_write\": 200, \"cache_read\": 300})\n        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        cost = usage[\"cost\"]\n        assert set(cost.keys()) == {\"input\", \"cache_write\", \"cache_read\", \"output\", \"total\"}\n        assert cost[\"input\"][\"tokens\"] == 1000\n        assert cost[\"output\"][\"tokens\"] == 500\n\n    def test_removes_top_level_token_keys(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, \"claude-sonnet-4-5\",\n                        {\"input\": 100, \"output\": 50})\n        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"input_tokens\" not in usage\n        assert \"output_tokens\" not in usage\n\n    def test_adds_canonical_model(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250110\",\n                        {\"input\": 100, \"output\": 50})\n        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert usage.get(\"model\") == \"claude-sonnet-4-5\"\n\n    def test_unknown_model_warning(self, ef, tmp_path, capsys):\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, \"unknown-model-xyz\",\n                        {\"input\": 100, \"output\": 50})\n        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        assert \"Warning\" in out\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"cost\" not in usage\n\n    def test_no_model_field_skipped(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        (d / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"messages\": []}))\n        (d / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"input_tokens\": 10, \"output_tokens\": 5,\n                                                   \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0,\n                                                   \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0}))\n        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"cost\" not in usage\n\n    def test_zero_tokens_zero_cost(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        d = self._setup(tmp_path, \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n                        {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0})\n        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert usage[\"cost\"][\"total\"][\"dollars\"] == 0.0\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestExtractFileOps\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestExtractFileOps:\n    def _body_with_read_write(self, read_fp=\"/test/read.py\", write_fp=\"/test/write.py\"):\n        return {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"r1\", \"name\": \"read_file\",\n                         \"input\": {\"file_path\": read_fp}},\n                    ],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"r1\",\n                         \"content\": \"file contents here\"},\n                    ],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n\n    def _write_response(self, tmp_path, write_fp=\"/test/write.py\", content=\"new code\"):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(tool_uses=[(\"Write\", {\"file_path\": write_fp, \"content\": content})])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(sse)\n        return str(p)\n\n    def test_read_file_tracked(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = self._body_with_read_write()\n        response_path = self._write_response(tmp_path)\n        result = ef.extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n        assert result[\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] == 1\n        assert \"/test/read.py\" in result[\"input\"][\"per_file\"]\n\n    def test_write_file_tracked(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = {\"messages\": []}\n        response_path = self._write_response(tmp_path, content=\"code here\")\n        result = ef.extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n        assert result[\"output\"][\"files_written\"] == 1\n        assert result[\"output\"][\"total_write_chars\"] == len(\"code here\")\n\n    def test_edit_file_uses_new_string(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        sse = make_sse_stream(tool_uses=[(\"Edit\", {\"file_path\": \"/f.py\", \"new_string\": \"replacement\"})])\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(sse)\n        result = ef.extract_file_ops({\"messages\": []}, str(p))\n        assert result[\"output\"][\"total_write_chars\"] == len(\"replacement\")\n\n    def test_deduplication_by_tool_id(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"Same file read twice with different tool_ids -> calls=2.\"\"\"\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"r1\", \"name\": \"read_file\",\n                         \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/same/file.py\"}},\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"r2\", \"name\": \"read_file\",\n                         \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/same/file.py\"}},\n                    ],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"r1\", \"content\": \"content1\"},\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"r2\", \"content\": \"content22\"},\n                    ],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(\"\")\n        result = ef.extract_file_ops(body, str(p))\n        pf = result[\"input\"][\"per_file\"][\"/same/file.py\"]\n        assert pf[\"calls\"] == 2\n        assert pf[\"chars\"] == len(\"content1\") + len(\"content22\")\n\n    def test_same_tool_id_not_duplicated(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"Same tool_id appearing in tool_ids map twice -> calls stays 1.\"\"\"\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"r1\", \"name\": \"read_file\",\n                         \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/file.py\"}},\n                    ],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"r1\", \"content\": \"content\"},\n                    ],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(\"\")\n        result = ef.extract_file_ops(body, str(p))\n        assert result[\"input\"][\"per_file\"][\"/file.py\"][\"calls\"] == 1\n\n    def test_missing_file_size_none(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = self._body_with_read_write(read_fp=\"/nonexistent/file.py\")\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(\"\")\n        result = ef.extract_file_ops(body, str(p))\n        assert result[\"input\"][\"per_file\"][\"/nonexistent/file.py\"][\"file_size\"] is None\n\n    def test_total_read_chars(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        body = self._body_with_read_write()\n        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        p.write_text(\"\")\n        result = ef.extract_file_ops(body, str(p))\n        assert result[\"input\"][\"total_read_chars\"] == len(\"file contents here\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TestSummarizeUsage\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestSummarizeUsage:\n    def _make_usage_json(self, model=\"claude-sonnet-4-5\", input_tokens=100, output_tokens=50,\n                          duration_ms=500, request_start=1700000000.0, response_end=1700000001.0,\n                          by_source=None, read_file_whitespace=None, file_ops=None):\n        usage = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"cost\": {\n                \"input\": {\"tokens\": input_tokens, \"dollars\": input_tokens * 3e-6},\n                \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0},\n                \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0},\n                \"output\": {\"tokens\": output_tokens, \"dollars\": output_tokens * 15e-6},\n                \"total\": {\"tokens\": input_tokens + output_tokens,\n                          \"dollars\": (input_tokens * 3e-6 + output_tokens * 15e-6)},\n            },\n            \"timing\": {\n                \"duration_ms\": duration_ms,\n                \"request_start\": request_start,\n                \"response_end\": response_end,\n            },\n        }\n        if by_source:\n            usage[\"by_source\"] = by_source\n        if read_file_whitespace:\n            usage[\"read_file_whitespace\"] = read_file_whitespace\n        if file_ops:\n            usage[\"file_ops\"] = file_ops\n        return usage\n\n    def _setup_agent(self, base, agent_name, steps):\n        \"\"\"steps: list of list of usage dicts (one list per step).\"\"\"\n        agent_dir = base / agent_name\n        for step_i, reqs in enumerate(steps, start=1):\n            for req_i, usage in enumerate(reqs, start=1):\n                req_dir = agent_dir / str(step_i) / str(req_i)\n                req_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n                (req_dir / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps(usage))\n        return agent_dir\n\n    def test_writes_usage_json(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u = self._make_usage_json()\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        assert (tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").exists()\n\n    def test_request_count(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage_json(input_tokens=100)\n        u2 = self._make_usage_json(input_tokens=200)\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1, u2]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"total\"][\"request_count\"] == 2\n\n    def test_by_model_aggregation(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage_json(model=\"claude-sonnet-4-5\", input_tokens=100)\n        u2 = self._make_usage_json(model=\"claude-haiku-4-5\", input_tokens=50)\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1, u2]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"claude-sonnet-4-5\" in summary[\"by_model\"]\n        assert \"claude-haiku-4-5\" in summary[\"by_model\"]\n\n    def test_by_step_aggregation(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage_json(input_tokens=100)\n        u2 = self._make_usage_json(input_tokens=200)\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1], [u2]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"1\" in summary[\"by_step\"]\n        assert \"2\" in summary[\"by_step\"]\n\n    def test_known_agent_color_vix(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u = self._make_usage_json()\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"color\"] == \"#7B2FBE\"\n\n    def test_known_agent_color_cc(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u = self._make_usage_json()\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"cc\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"cc\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"color\"] == \"#D77656\"\n\n    def test_unknown_agent_gets_md5_color(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u = self._make_usage_json()\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"my_agent\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"my_agent\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"color\"].startswith(\"#\")\n        assert len(summary[\"color\"]) == 7\n\n    def test_skips_dirs_without_numbered_subdirs(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        non_agent = tmp_path / \"not_an_agent\"\n        non_agent.mkdir()\n        (non_agent / \"some_file.json\").write_text(\"{}\")\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (non_agent / \"usage.json\").exists()\n\n    def test_timing_wall_clock_computed(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u = self._make_usage_json(request_start=1700000000.0, response_end=1700000010.0,\n                                   duration_ms=10000)\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"total\"][\"timing\"][\"wall_clock_ms\"] == 10000\n\n    def test_timing_avg_duration_computed(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage_json(duration_ms=1000, request_start=1.0, response_end=2.0)\n        u2 = self._make_usage_json(duration_ms=3000, request_start=2.0, response_end=5.0)\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1, u2]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"total\"][\"timing\"][\"avg_duration_ms\"] == 2000  # (1000+3000)/2\n\n    def test_read_file_whitespace_aggregated(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        ws = {\"line_returns_count\": 5, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 3, \"total_chars\": 200}\n        u = self._make_usage_json(read_file_whitespace=ws)\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"read_file_whitespace\"][\"line_returns_count\"] == 5\n\n    def test_file_ops_finalized(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        file_ops = {\n            \"input\": {\n                \"unique_files_read\": 1,\n                \"total_read_chars\": 100,\n                \"per_file\": {\n                    \"/some/file.py\": {\n                        \"calls\": 1, \"chars\": 100,\n                        \"tool_ids\": {\"tid1\": 100},\n                        \"file_size\": None,\n                    }\n                },\n            },\n            \"output\": {\n                \"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0,\n                \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {},\n            },\n        }\n        u = self._make_usage_json(file_ops=file_ops)\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"total\"][\"file_ops\"][\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] == 1\n\n    def test_by_source_aggregated(self, ef, tmp_path):\n        by_source = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"tokens\": 50, \"dollars\": 0.0001, \"chars\": 500}}},\n            \"output\": {\"llm_text\": {\"tokens\": 30, \"dollars\": 0.0003, \"chars\": 200}},\n        }\n        u = self._make_usage_json(by_source=by_source)\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"by_source\"][\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"tokens\"] == 50\n\n    def test_multiple_agents(self, ef, tmp_path, capsys):\n        u = self._make_usage_json()\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u]])\n        self._setup_agent(tmp_path, \"cc\", [[u]])\n        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        assert \"2\" in out  # Summarized 2 agent types\n"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011yHN4diQ9tKhnog8vZWPGb","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let's run the tests to see if they pass and check coverage:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FmuNuWLEkjDDdiy4hZ1jVV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py -v --tb=short 2>&1 | head -120","description":"Run test suite with verbose output","timeout":120000}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FmuNuWLEkjDDdiy4hZ1jVV","type":"tool_result","content":"/bin/bash: line 1: python: command not found","is_error":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LkHNmYxtS1EMc5LrvcASNq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py -v --tb=short 2>&1 | head -200","description":"Run tests from workspace directory","timeout":120000}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LkHNmYxtS1EMc5LrvcASNq","type":"tool_result","content":"============================= test session starts ==============================\nplatform linux -- Python 3.11.2, pytest-9.0.2, pluggy-1.6.0 -- /usr/bin/python3\ncachedir: .pytest_cache\nrootdir: /workspace\nplugins: cov-7.1.0\ncollecting ... collected 204 items\n\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_empty_string PASSED [  0%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_single_newline PASSED [  0%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_double_spaces PASSED [  1%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_triple_spaces PASSED [  1%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_single_space_not_counted PASSED [  2%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_multiple_runs_accumulated PASSED [  2%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_total_chars_accurate PASSED [  3%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_only_spaces PASSED [  3%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestCountWhitespaceStats::test_combined FAILED [  4%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestGetCanonicalModel::test_exact_match[claude-opus-4-6] PASSED [  4%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestGetCanonicalModel::test_exact_match[claude-opus-4-5] PASSED [  5%]\nevaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py::TestGetCanonicalModel::test_exact_match[claude-opus-4-1] PASSED [  5%]\nevaluation/usage/test_